aicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyAffFace.lean:73:affine tests: `DivFamZarAff.mapAlg` at the algebra structure `RingHom.toAlgebra` of the map.\\nAlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyAffFace.lean:75:The instance-parameterized `DivFamZarAff.mapAlg` remains the preferred form whenever a scalar\\nAlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyAffFace.lean:78:def mapAlgHom (φ : A →ₐ[k] A') : DivFamZarAff C A n → DivFamZarAff C A' n :=\\nAlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyAffFace.lean:81:  DivFamZarAff.mapAlg A' n\\nAlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyAffFace.lean:83:/-- `mapAlgHom` along the identity is the identity (`DivFamZarAff.mapAlg_id`). -/\\nAlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyAffFace.lean:84:theorem mapAlgHom_id (F : DivFamZarAff C A n) : mapAlgHom (AlgHom.id k A) F = F :=\\nAlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyAffFace.lean:85:  DivFamZarAff.mapAlg_id n F\\nAlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyAffFace.lean:88:(`DivFamZarAff.mapAlg_comp`). -/\\nAlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyAffFace.lean:89:theorem mapAlgHom_comp (φ : A →ₐ[k] A') (ψ : A' →ₐ[k] A'') (F : DivFamZarAff C A n) :\\nAlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyAffFace.lean:98:  (DivFamZarAff.mapAlg_comp A' n A'' F).symm\\nAlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyAffFace.lean:102:/-- `DivFamZarAff.mapAlg` depends on the `A`-algebra structure of the target only through the\\nAlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyAffFace.lean:115:    (F : DivFamZarAff C A n) :\\nAlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyAffFace.lean:116:    @DivFamZarAff.mapAlg k _ C A _ _ A' _ _ a₁ t₁ n _ F\\nAlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyAffFace.lean:117:      = @DivFamZarAff.mapAlg k _ C A _ _ A' _ _ a₂ t₂ n _ F := by\\nAlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyAffFace.lean:122:map of a scalar tower in scope is the instance-based `DivFamZarAff.mapAlg` of the tower.\\nAlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyAffFace.lean:128:    (hφ : ∀ a, φ a = algebraMap A A' a) (F : DivFamZarAff C A n) :\\nAlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyAffFace.lean:129:    mapAlgHom φ F = DivFamZarAff.mapAlg A' n F := by\\nAlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyAffFace.lean:137:lemma picClass_mapAlgHom (φ : A →ₐ[k] A') (F : DivFamZarAff C A n) :\\nAlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyAffFace.lean:144:  DivFamZarAff.picClass_mapAlg A' n F\\nAlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyAffFace.lean:149:def congr (e : A ≃ₐ[k] A') : DivFamZarAff C A n ≃ DivFamZarAff C A' n where\\n\", \"exit_code\": 0}, \"usage\": null}\n{\"kind\": \"tool_call\", \"at\": \"2026-08-06T03:59:21.340688+00:00\", \"text\": \"\", \"tool\": \"Bash\", \"data\": {\"command\": \"/bin/bash -lc \\\"nl -ba AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyZarVehicle.lean | sed -n '1,250p'\\\"\"}, \"usage\": null}\n{\"kind\": \"tool_result\", \"at\": \"2026-08-06T03:59:21.340700+00:00\", \"text\": \"\", \"tool\": \"Bash\", \"data\": {\"content\": \"     1\\t/-\\n     2\\tCopyright (c) 2026 The AlgebraicJacobian authors. All rights reserved.\\n     3\\tReleased under Apache 2.0 license as described in the file LICENSE.\\n     4\\tAuthors: The AlgebraicJacobian Contributors\\n     5\\t-/\\n     6\\timport AlgebraicJacobian.Picard.DivisorFamilyZarMapAlg\\n     7\\timport AlgebraicJacobian.Picard.DivisorFamilyVehicle\\n     8\\t\\n     9\\t/-!\\n    10\\t# The locally certified divisor functor on all test objects: the vehicle (DD-2 stage S6a)\\n    11\\t\\n    12\\tThe Addendum-2 divisor-functor value on an affine test is `DivFamZar C R π n`\\n    13\\t(`AlgebraicJacobian.Picard.DivisorFamilyZar`), with base change `DivFamZar.mapAlg`\\n    14\\talong arbitrary test changes (`AlgebraicJacobian.Picard.DivisorFamilyZarMapAlg`).\\n    15\\tThis file extends it to **all** of `Over (Spec k)` by the bespoke affine-opens limit,\\n    16\\tmirroring the globally certified vehicle `AlgebraicJacobian.Picard.DivisorFamilyVehicle`\\n    17\\tclause for clause:\\n    18\\t\\n    19\\t* `AlgebraicGeometry.DivFamZar.mapAlgHom`: base change of locally certified divisor\\n    20\\t  classes along an **explicit** `k`-algebra map — `DivFamZar.mapAlg` at the induced\\n    21\\t  algebra tower, with the functor laws `DivFamZar.mapAlgHom_id`/`DivFamZar.mapAlgHom_comp`\\n    22\\t  from the S5b laws `DivFamZar.mapAlg_id`/`DivFamZar.mapAlg_comp`.\\n    23\\t* `AlgebraicGeometry.DivFamZar.mapAlgHom_eq_mapAlg`: **the face-change bridge** — along\\n    24\\t  an algebra map agreeing with a scalar-tower structure map, the explicit face is the\\n    25\\t  instance face (`DivFamZar.mapAlg_congr`, algebra structures with equal structure maps\\n    26\\t  are equal).  This is how the S6 general-test statements consume the S5b keystones\\n    27\\t  `DivFamZar.eq_of_away_eq`/`DivFamZar.exists_glue_of_away_compat`, which are spelled in\\n    28\\t  the instance face.\\n    29\\t* `AlgebraicGeometry.DivFamZar.congr`: transport along an isomorphism of test algebras.\\n    30\\t* `AlgebraicGeometry.divFamZar C π n T`: **the vehicle** — compatible families of\\n    31\\t  locally certified divisor classes over the affine opens of `T.left`, with\\n    32\\t  `divFamZar.eval` the evaluation at an affine open.\\n    33\\t* `AlgebraicGeometry.divFamZarAffineEquiv C π n R`: **the affine comparison** — on an\\n    34\\t  affine test `overSpec k R` the vehicle collapses by evaluation at the top affine open\\n    35\\t  to `DivFamZar C R π n` (the `divFamAffineEquiv` template, clause for clause).\\n    36\\t* `AlgebraicGeometry.divFam.toZarVehicle`: **the comparison from the globally certified\\n    37\\t  vehicle** — componentwise `DivFam.toZar`, compatible by `DivFam.toZar_mapAlg`\\n    38\\t  (packaged on the explicit face as `DivFam.toZar_mapAlgHom`); it intertwines the two\\n    39\\t  affine comparisons (`divFamZarAffineEquiv_toZarVehicle`).\\n    40\\t\\n    41\\tFunctoriality in `T` along an *arbitrary* morphism of test objects (glued values over\\n    42\\tbasic-open refinements, the `picEtMap` pattern) is\\n    43\\t`AlgebraicJacobian.Picard.DivisorFamilyZarMap`; the sheaf statements at arbitrary tests\\n    44\\tare `AlgebraicJacobian.Picard.DivisorFamilyZarSheaf`.\\n    45\\t\\n    46\\tThe `k`-algebra structure on section rings is `Over.sectionsAlgebra` and the algebra\\n    47\\tstructures on the relative curve's section rings are `Scheme.overModule`/\\n    48\\t`Scheme.overSectionsAlgebra` (LOCAL instances, house rule) — consumers must activate\\n    49\\tthe same instances.\\n    50\\t-/\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\tset_option autoImplicit false\\n    53\\t/- Statements mix the section rings `Γ(T.left, ·)` with the locally certified\\n    54\\tdivisor-functor values over them, which are stated on the product spelling\\n    55\\t`(C ⊗ overSpec k R).left`; see `AlgebraicJacobian.Cohomology.RelativeSectionsLinear`. -/\\n    56\\tset_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false\\n    57\\t/- `lake env lean` drops the lakefile's `[leanOptions]` (I-0161), so the pinned synthesis\\n    58\\tdepth must be set in-file for the faithful per-file check. -/\\n    59\\tset_option maxSynthPendingDepth 3\\n    60\\t\\n    61\\tuniverse u\\n    62\\t\\n    63\\topen CategoryTheory\\n    64\\t\\n    65\\tnamespace AlgebraicGeometry\\n    66\\t\\n    67\\tattribute [local instance] Over.sectionsAlgebra Scheme.overModule Scheme.overSectionsAlgebra\\n    68\\t\\n    69\\tvariable {k : Type u} [Field k] {C : Over (Spec (.of k))}\\n    70\\tvariable {π : C.left ⟶ P1 k} [IsAffineHom π] {n : ℕ}\\n    71\\t\\n    72\\tnoncomputable section\\n    73\\t\\n    74\\t/-! ## Base change of locally certified classes along an explicit algebra map\\n    75\\t\\n    76\\t`DivFamZar.mapAlg` (`AlgebraicJacobian.Picard.DivisorFamilyZarMapAlg`) is parameterized\\n    77\\tby an algebra-tower instance pack `[Algebra R R'] [IsScalarTower k R R']`.  The vehicle\\n    78\\tindexes its compatibilities by the section-restriction maps `Over.resAlgHom`, so it\\n    79\\tconsumes the explicit-map face — the `DivFam.mapAlgHom` packaging of\\n    80\\t`AlgebraicJacobian.Picard.DivisorFamilyVehicle`, verbatim. -/\\n    81\\t\\n    82\\tnamespace DivFamZar\\n    83\\t\\n    84\\tvariable {A A' A'' : Type u} [CommRing A] [Algebra k A] [CommRing A'] [Algebra k A']\\n    85\\t  [CommRing A''] [Algebra k A'']\\n    86\\t\\n    87\\t/-- Base change of locally certified divisor classes along an explicit `k`-algebra map\\n    88\\tof affine tests: `DivFamZar.mapAlg` at the algebra structure `RingHom.toAlgebra` of the\\n    89\\tmap.  The instance-parameterized `DivFamZar.mapAlg` remains the preferred form whenever\\n    90\\ta scalar tower is already in scope. -/\\n    91\\tdef mapAlgHom (φ : A →ₐ[k] A') : DivFamZar C A π n → DivFamZar C A' π n :=\\n    92\\t  letI : Algebra A A' := φ.toRingHom.toAlgebra\\n    93\\t  haveI : IsScalarTower k A A' := .of_algebraMap_eq fun a => (φ.commutes a).symm\\n    94\\t  DivFamZar.mapAlg A' n\\n    95\\t\\n    96\\t/-- `mapAlgHom` along the identity is the identity (`DivFamZar.mapAlg_id`). -/\\n    97\\ttheorem mapAlgHom_id (F : DivFamZar C A π n) : mapAlgHom (AlgHom.id k A) F = F :=\\n    98\\t  DivFamZar.mapAlg_id n F\\n    99\\t\\n   100\\t/-- `mapAlgHom` along a composite is the composite of the base changes\\n   101\\t(`DivFamZar.mapAlg_comp`). -/\\n   102\\ttheorem mapAlgHom_comp (φ : A →ₐ[k] A') (ψ : A' →ₐ[k] A'') (F : DivFamZar C A π n) :\\n   103\\t    mapAlgHom (ψ.comp φ) F = mapAlgHom ψ (mapAlgHom φ F) :=\\n   104\\t  letI : Algebra A A' := φ.toRingHom.toAlgebra\\n   105\\t  haveI : IsScalarTower k A A' := .of_algebraMap_eq fun x => (φ.commutes x).symm\\n   106\\t  letI : Algebra A' A'' := ψ.toRingHom.toAlgebra\\n   107\\t  haveI : IsScalarTower k A' A'' := .of_algebraMap_eq fun x => (ψ.commutes x).symm\\n   108\\t  letI : Algebra A A'' := (ψ.comp φ).toRingHom.toAlgebra\\n   109\\t  haveI : IsScalarTower k A A'' := .of_algebraMap_eq fun x => ((ψ.comp φ).commutes x).symm\\n   110\\t  haveI : IsScalarTower A A' A'' := .of_algebraMap_eq fun _ => rfl\\n   111\\t  (DivFamZar.mapAlg_comp A' n A'' F).symm\\n   112\\t\\n   113\\t/-! ### The face-change bridge -/\\n   114\\t\\n   115\\t/-- `DivFamZar.mapAlg` depends on the `A`-algebra structure of the target only through\\n   116\\tthe structure itself: equal algebra structures give equal base changes (the scalar-tower\\n   117\\twitnesses are proof-irrelevant).  The congruence backing the face-change bridge\\n   118\\t`mapAlgHom_eq_mapAlg`. -/\\n   119\\ttheorem mapAlg_congr {a₁ a₂ : Algebra A A'} (h : a₁ = a₂)\\n   120\\t    (t₁ : @IsScalarTower k A A' Algebra.toSMul a₁.toSMul Algebra.toSMul)\\n   121\\t    (t₂ : @IsScalarTower k A A' Algebra.toSMul a₂.toSMul Algebra.toSMul)\\n   122\\t    (F : DivFamZar C A π n) :\\n   123\\t    @DivFamZar.mapAlg k _ C A _ _ π _ A' _ _ a₁ t₁ n F\\n   124\\t      = @DivFamZar.mapAlg k _ C A _ _ π _ A' _ _ a₂ t₂ n F := by\\n   125\\t  subst h\\n   126\\t  rfl\\n   127\\t\\n   128\\t/-- **The face-change bridge**: `mapAlgHom` along an algebra map that agrees with the\\n   129\\tstructure map of a scalar tower in scope is the instance-based `DivFamZar.mapAlg` of the\\n   130\\ttower.  This is how the vehicle statements (spelled at `Over.resAlgHom`) consume the S5b\\n   131\\tZariski keystones (spelled at localization instance packs). -/\\n   132\\ttheorem mapAlgHom_eq_mapAlg [Algebra A A'] [IsScalarTower k A A'] (φ : A →ₐ[k] A')\\n   133\\t    (hφ : ∀ a, φ a = algebraMap A A' a) (F : DivFamZar C A π n) :\\n   134\\t    mapAlgHom φ F = DivFamZar.mapAlg A' n F := by\\n   135\\t  unfold mapAlgHom\\n   136\\t  exact mapAlg_congr (Algebra.algebra_ext _ _ hφ) _ _ F\\n   137\\t\\n   138\\t/-! ### Transport along an isomorphism of test algebras -/\\n   139\\t\\n   140\\t/-- Transport of locally certified divisor classes along an isomorphism of test\\n   141\\talgebras. -/\\n   142\\tdef congr (e : A ≃ₐ[k] A') : DivFamZar C A π n ≃ DivFamZar C A' π n where\\n   143\\t  toFun := mapAlgHom e.toAlgHom\\n   144\\t  invFun := mapAlgHom e.symm.toAlgHom\\n   145\\t  left_inv F := by\\n   146\\t    rw [← mapAlgHom_comp, show e.symm.toAlgHom.comp e.toAlgHom = AlgHom.id k A from\\n   147\\t      AlgHom.ext fun a => e.symm_apply_apply a, mapAlgHom_id]\\n   148\\t  right_inv F := by\\n   149\\t    rw [← mapAlgHom_comp, show e.toAlgHom.comp e.symm.toAlgHom = AlgHom.id k A' from\\n   150\\t      AlgHom.ext fun a => e.apply_symm_apply a, mapAlgHom_id]\\n   151\\t\\n   152\\t/-- The transport along an isomorphism is `mapAlgHom` of its underlying map. -/\\n   153\\t@[simp]\\n   154\\tlemma congr_apply (e : A ≃ₐ[k] A') (F : DivFamZar C A π n) :\\n   155\\t    congr e F = mapAlgHom e.toAlgHom F :=\\n   156\\t  rfl\\n   157\\t\\n   158\\t/-- The inverse transport along an isomorphism is `mapAlgHom` of the inverse map. -/\\n   159\\t@[simp]\\n   160\\tlemma congr_symm_apply (e : A ≃ₐ[k] A') (F : DivFamZar C A' π n) :\\n   161\\t    (congr e).symm F = mapAlgHom e.symm.toAlgHom F :=\\n   162\\t  rfl\\n   163\\t\\n   164\\tend DivFamZar\\n   165\\t\\n   166\\t/-- **`toZar` intertwines the explicit-face base changes**: the comparison from\\n   167\\tglobally certified to locally certified classes is natural in the test algebra along an\\n   168\\texplicit `k`-algebra map — `DivFam.toZar_mapAlg` at the induced tower. -/\\n   169\\tlemma DivFam.toZar_mapAlgHom {A A' : Type u} [CommRing A] [Algebra k A] [CommRing A']\\n   170\\t    [Algebra k A'] (φ : A →ₐ[k] A') (F : DivFam C A π n) :\\n   171\\t    (DivFam.mapAlgHom φ F).toZar = DivFamZar.mapAlgHom φ F.toZar :=\\n   172\\t  letI : Algebra A A' := φ.toRingHom.toAlgebra\\n   173\\t  haveI : IsScalarTower k A A' := .of_algebraMap_eq fun a => (φ.commutes a).symm\\n   174\\t  DivFam.toZar_mapAlg A' n F\\n   175\\t\\n   176\\t/-! ## The affine-opens limit -/\\n   177\\t\\n   178\\tvariable (C π n)\\n   179\\t\\n   180\\t/-- **The locally certified divisor functor at an arbitrary test object**\\n   181\\t(`informal/spec-dd-2.md` §6 on the Addendum-2 carrier; the `divFam` vehicle):\\n   182\\tcompatible families of locally certified divisor classes over the affine opens of\\n   183\\t`T.left` — the value at a smaller affine open is the base change of the value at a\\n   184\\tlarger one along the section-restriction algebra map.  On affine tests this is\\n   185\\t`DivFamZar` itself (`divFamZarAffineEquiv`); on general tests it is its canonical\\n   186\\tZariski-continuous extension. -/\\n   187\\tdef divFamZar (T : Over (Spec (.of k))) : Type u :=\\n   188\\t  {s : Π U : T.left.affineOpens, DivFamZar C Γ(T.left, U.1) π n //\\n   189\\t    ∀ (U V : T.left.affineOpens) (h : U.1 ≤ V.1),\\n   190\\t      DivFamZar.mapAlgHom (Over.resAlgHom T h) (s V) = s U}\\n   191\\t\\n   192\\tnamespace divFamZar\\n   193\\t\\n   194\\tvariable {C π n} {T : Over (Spec (.of k))}\\n   195\\t\\n   196\\t/-- The compatibility of a section of `divFamZar` along an inclusion of affine opens. -/\\n   197\\tlemma compat (s : divFamZar C π n T) (U V : T.left.affineOpens) (h : U.1 ≤ V.1) :\\n   198\\t    DivFamZar.mapAlgHom (Over.resAlgHom T h) (s.1 V) = s.1 U :=\\n   199\\t  s.2 U V h\\n   200\\t\\n   201\\t/-- Two sections of `divFamZar` agreeing at every affine open are equal. -/\\n   202\\t@[ext]\\n   203\\tlemma ext {s t : divFamZar C π n T} (h : ∀ U : T.left.affineOpens, s.1 U = t.1 U) :\\n   204\\t    s = t :=\\n   205\\t  Subtype.ext (funext h)\\n   206\\t\\n   207\\tvariable (C π n T) in\\n   208\\t/-- Evaluation of a section of `divFamZar` at an affine open. -/\\n   209\\tdef eval (U : T.left.affineOpens) : divFamZar C π n T → DivFamZar C Γ(T.left, U.1) π n :=\\n   210\\t  fun s => s.1 U\\n   211\\t\\n   212\\t/-- Evaluation is projection to the component at the affine open. -/\\n   213\\t@[simp]\\n   214\\tlemma eval_apply (U : T.left.affineOpens) (s : divFamZar C π n T) :\\n   215\\t    eval C π n T U s = s.1 U :=\\n   216\\t  rfl\\n   217\\t\\n   218\\tend divFamZar\\n   219\\t\\n   220\\t/-! ## The affine comparison -/\\n   221\\t\\n   222\\tsection Affine\\n   223\\t\\n   224\\tvariable (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [Algebra k R]\\n   225\\t\\n   226\\t/-- Evaluation at the top affine open of an affine test, composed with the\\n   227\\t`ΓSpecIso`-transport into the test algebra: the forward direction of the affine\\n   228\\tcomparison. -/\\n   229\\tdef divFamZarToAff : divFamZar C π n (overSpec k R) → DivFamZar C R π n :=\\n   230\\t  fun s => DivFamZar.congr (Over.overSpecΓTopAlgEquiv k R) (s.1 (overSpecTopAffine R))\\n   231\\t\\n   232\\t/-- The section of `divFamZar` over an affine test determined by a locally certified\\n   233\\tdivisor class of the test algebra: restrict from the top affine open — the inverse\\n   234\\tdirection of the affine comparison. -/\\n   235\\tdef divFamZarOfAff : DivFamZar C R π n → divFamZar C π n (overSpec k R) :=\\n   236\\t  fun x =>\\n   237\\t    ⟨fun U => DivFamZar.mapAlgHom\\n   238\\t      ((Over.resAlgHom (overSpec k R) le_top).comp\\n   239\\t        (Over.overSpecΓTopAlgEquiv k R).symm.toAlgHom) x,\\n   240\\t      fun U V h => by rw [← DivFamZar.mapAlgHom_comp, ← AlgHom.comp_assoc,\\n   241\\t        Over.resAlgHom_comp]⟩\\n   242\\t\\n   243\\t/-- The value of `divFamZarOfAff` at every affine open is the restricted transported\\n   244\\tclass. -/\\n   245\\tlemma divFamZarOfAff_val (x : DivFamZar C R π n) (U : (overSpec k R).left.affineOpens) :\\n   246\\t    (divFamZarOfAff C π n R x).1 U\\n   247\\t      = DivFamZar.mapAlgHom\\n   248\\t          ((Over.resAlgHom (overSpec k R) le_top).comp\\n   249\\t            (Over.overSpecΓTopAlgEquiv k R).symm.toAlgHom) x :=\\n   250\\t  rfl\\n\", \"exit_code\": 0}, \"usage\": null}\n{\"kind\": \"tool_call\", \"at\": \"2026-08-06T03:59:22.265698+00:00\", \"text\": \"\", \"tool\": \"Bash\", \"data\": {\"command\": \"/bin/bash -lc \\\"nl -ba AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivisorFamilyAffMapAlg.lean | sed -n '1,230p'\\\"\"}, \"usage\": null}\n{\"kind\": \"tool_result\", \"at\": \"2026-08-06T03:59:22.265711+00:00\", \"text\": \"\", \"tool\": \"Bash\", \"data\": {\"content\": \"     1\\t/-\\n     2\\tCopyright (c) 2026 The AlgebraicJacobian authors. All rights reserved.\\n     3\\tReleased under Apache 2.0 license as described in the file LICENSE.\\n     4\\tAuthors: The AlgebraicJacobian Contributors\\n     5\\t-/\\n     6\\timport AlgebraicJacobian.Picard.DivisorFamilyAffCert\\n     7\\timport AlgebraicJacobian.Picard.DivisorFamilyAffZar\\n     8\\timport AlgebraicJacobian.Picard.DivisorFamilyAffCompare\\n     9\\timport AlgebraicJacobian.Picard.DivisorFamilyZarMapAlg\\n    10\\t\\n    11\\t/-!\\n    12\\t# The widened divisor-functor map (R2, human decision I-0492)\\n    13\\t\\n    14\\t`DivFamZarAff.mapAlg` along an arbitrary test change `R → R'`, with the functor laws, the Abel\\n    15\\thook, and the Zariski separation keystone.  This is what makes the widened value a functor\\n    16\\tVALUE rather than a bare type: before this file nothing could base-change a widened class.\\n    17\\t\\n    18\\t## Where the widening does and does not show\\n    19\\t\\n    20\\tAlmost nowhere.  `IsLocallyCertifiedAff` widens where the pieces live on the CURVE and changes\\n    21\\tnothing about the Zariski cover of the BASE, so the base-side machinery of\\n    22\\t`DivisorFamilyZarMapAlg.lean` — the `Localization.Away` towers, `IsLocalization.map`,\\n    23\\t`span_range_algebraMap_eq_top` — applies verbatim; the cover datum only appears inside the\\n    24\\topaque `mapAlg` of the local certified family.  Likewise\\n    25\\t`Scheme.LocalEquations.divEq_pullback`, `divEq_pullback_id` and `divEq_pullback_pullback` are\\n    26\\tstated for ARBITRARY scheme morphisms and know nothing about covers, so the functor laws are\\n    27\\tthe same three lines as in the chart-typed case.\\n    28\\t\\n    29\\t## The one honest cost of the widening: overlap affineness\\n    30\\t\\n    31\\t`AffCoverData` demands affineness of the pieces only (that is the R2 shape), so the certificate\\n    32\\ttransport takes an explicit `hinf` — the overlaps are affine.  A `CertifiedDivisorFamilyAff`\\n    33\\ttherefore cannot be base-changed without it, and rather than weaken the structure this file\\n    34\\tcarries `hinf` as a hypothesis on `mapAlg` at the family level.  It is not a hidden\\n    35\\tassumption: it is visible in every signature below, as I-0492 clause 4 requires.  For a\\n    36\\trelative curve over a proper `C` it is discharged by separatedness (`IsAffineOpen.inf`).\\n    37\\t\\n    38\\t## Main declarations\\n    39\\t\\n    40\\t* `CertifiedDivisorFamilyAff.mapAlg` — base change of a widened certified family.\\n    41\\t* `IsLocallyCertifiedAff.pullback` — certificate transport along an arbitrary test change.\\n    42\\t* `DivFamZarAff.mapAlg`, with `mapAlg_mk`, `picClass_mapAlg`, `mapAlg_id`, `mapAlg_comp`.\\n    43\\t* `DivFamZarAff.eq_of_away_eq` — Zariski separation at the widened Zar level.\\n    44\\t-/\\n    45\\t\\n    46\\tset_option autoImplicit false\\n    47\\tset_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false\\n    48\\tset_option maxSynthPendingDepth 3\\n    49\\t\\n    50\\tuniverse u\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\topen CategoryTheory Limits MonoidalCategory CartesianMonoidalCategory TopologicalSpace\\n    53\\topen Opposite TensorProduct\\n    54\\t\\n    55\\tnamespace AlgebraicGeometry\\n    56\\t\\n    57\\tattribute [local instance] Scheme.overModule Scheme.overSectionsAlgebra\\n    58\\t\\n    59\\tvariable {k : Type u} [Field k] {C : Over (Spec (.of k))}\\n    60\\tvariable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [Algebra k R]\\n    61\\t\\n    62\\t/-- **Overlap affineness of a widened cover** — the one datum the certificate transport needs\\n    63\\tbeyond `AffCoverData`'s own fields.  Named so that it can be threaded explicitly and read off\\n    64\\tany signature; for a relative curve over a proper `C` it follows from separatedness. -/\\n    65\\tdef AffCoverData.HasAffineOverlaps (D : AffCoverData C R) : Prop :=\\n    66\\t  ∀ i j : D.index, IsAffineOpen (D.pieces i ⊓ D.pieces j)\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\tvariable (R' : Type u) [CommRing R'] [Algebra k R'] [Algebra R R'] [IsScalarTower k R R']\\n    69\\tvariable (n : ℕ)\\n    70\\t\\n    71\\t/-- **Base change of a widened certified family**: pulled equations, base-changed cover and\\n    72\\tadaptation, transported certificate. -/\\n    73\\tnoncomputable def CertifiedDivisorFamilyAff.mapAlg (F : CertifiedDivisorFamilyAff C R n)\\n    74\\t    (hinf : F.cover.HasAffineOverlaps) : CertifiedDivisorFamilyAff C R' n where\\n    75\\t  eqns := F.adaptation.pulledEquations R' F.certified.projective_colength\\n    76\\t  cover := F.cover.baseChange R'\\n    77\\t  adaptation := F.adaptation.pullback R' F.certified.projective_colength\\n    78\\t  certified := F.adaptation.isCertified_pullback R' hinf F.certified\\n    79\\t\\n    80\\t@[simp]\\n    81\\tlemma CertifiedDivisorFamilyAff.mapAlg_cover (F : CertifiedDivisorFamilyAff C R n)\\n    82\\t    (hinf : F.cover.HasAffineOverlaps) :\\n    83\\t    (F.mapAlg R' n hinf).cover = F.cover.baseChange R' := rfl\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t/-- **The base-changed cover again has affine overlaps**: overlaps of base-changed pieces are\\n    86\\tpreimages of overlaps, and preimages of affine opens under `relCurveMap` are affine.  So the\\n    87\\t`hinf` obligation propagates along a tower rather than accumulating. -/\\n    88\\ttheorem AffCoverData.hasAffineOverlaps_baseChange {D : AffCoverData C R}\\n    89\\t    (hinf : D.HasAffineOverlaps) : (D.baseChange R').HasAffineOverlaps := fun i j => by\\n    90\\t  rw [show (D.baseChange R').pieces i ⊓ (D.baseChange R').pieces j\\n    91\\t      = relCurveMap C R R' ⁻¹ᵁ (D.pieces i ⊓ D.pieces j) from rfl]\\n    92\\t  exact isAffineOpen_relCurveMap_preimage C R' (hinf i j)\\n    93\\t\\n    94\\t/-- **`HasAffineOverlaps` is FREE for a proper `C`** — which is the only case the DD-R lane\\n    95\\tever uses.  The relative curve over a proper `C` is a separated scheme, so its affine opens are\\n    96\\tclosed under intersection (`Over.isAffineOpen_inf`, via the affine diagonal).\\n    97\\t\\n    98\\tSo the `hinf` threading below is bookkeeping, not a standing assumption: it is dischargeable\\n    99\\twherever `C` is proper, and it is stated rather than assumed so that a reader can see the cost\\n   100\\tof `AffCoverData` demanding affineness of the pieces only. -/\\n   101\\ttheorem AffCoverData.hasAffineOverlaps_of_isProper [IsProper C.hom] (D : AffCoverData C R) :\\n   102\\t    D.HasAffineOverlaps := fun i j =>\\n   103\\t  Over.isAffineOpen_inf (A := R) C (D.isAffineOpen i) (D.isAffineOpen j)\\n   104\\t\\n   105\\t/-! ## Witness transport along a tower -/\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\t/-- **Witness transport along a tower `R → A → B`**, widened: a certified family over `A`\\n   108\\tdivisor-equal to the pulled system stays divisor-equal after `mapAlg` to `B`.  Verbatim the\\n   109\\tchart-typed `CertifiedDivisorFamily.divEq_mapAlg_pullback` — `divEq_pullback` along\\n   110\\t`relCurveMap C A B`, then the composite collapse `divEq_pullback_pullback` at\\n   111\\t`relCurveMap_comp`; both are statements about arbitrary scheme morphisms. -/\\n   112\\ttheorem CertifiedDivisorFamilyAff.divEq_mapAlg_pullback\\n   113\\t    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [Algebra k A] [Algebra R A] [IsScalarTower k R A]\\n   114\\t    (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [Algebra k B] [Algebra R B] [Algebra A B]\\n   115\\t    [IsScalarTower k R B] [IsScalarTower k A B] [IsScalarTower R A B]\\n   116\\t    (E : CertifiedDivisorFamilyAff C A n) (hinf : E.cover.HasAffineOverlaps)\\n   117\\t    {d : (relCurve C R).LocalEquations} {hregA} (hregB)\\n   118\\t    (hdiv : Scheme.LocalEquations.DivEq E.eqns (d.pullback (relCurveMap C R A) hregA)) :\\n   119\\t    Scheme.LocalEquations.DivEq (E.mapAlg B n hinf).eqns\\n   120\\t      (d.pullback (relCurveMap C R B) hregB) := by\\n   121\\t  have hcomp : relCurveMap C A B ≫ relCurveMap C R A = relCurveMap C R B :=\\n   122\\t    relCurveMap_comp (R' := A) (R'' := B)\\n   123\\t  have hregMid := Scheme.LocalEquations.germ_pullbackEqn_mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_divEq\\n   124\\t    (relCurveMap C A B) hdiv\\n   125\\t    (E.adaptation.germ_pullbackEqn_mem_nonZeroDivisors B E.certified.projective_colength)\\n   126\\t  exact Scheme.LocalEquations.DivEq.trans\\n   127\\t    (Scheme.LocalEquations.divEq_pullback (relCurveMap C A B) hdiv\\n   128\\t      (E.adaptation.germ_pullbackEqn_mem_nonZeroDivisors B\\n   129\\t        E.certified.projective_colength) hregMid)\\n   130\\t    (Scheme.LocalEquations.divEq_pullback_pullback hcomp d hregA hregMid hregB)\\n   131\\t\\n   132\\t/-! ## The mapAlg-hreg engine, widened\\n   133\\t\\n   134\\tThe widened analogue of `IsLocallyCertified.germ_pullbackEqn_mem_nonZeroDivisors`: a widened\\n   135\\tlocally certified system has regular pulled equations along an arbitrary test tower.\\n   136\\tRegularity is germ-local on the curve, and the covering argument is on the BASE, so the proof\\n   137\\tis the chart-typed one with `CertifiedDivisorFamily` replaced by\\n   138\\t`CertifiedDivisorFamilyAff`. -/\\n   139\\t\\n   140\\ttheorem IsLocallyCertifiedAff.germ_pullbackEqn_mem_nonZeroDivisors\\n   141\\t    {d : (relCurve C R).LocalEquations}\\n   142\\t    (hloc : IsLocallyCertifiedAff (C := C) (R := R) n d)\\n   143\\t    (y z : relCurve C R') (hz : z ∈ (d.cover.pullback (relCurveMap C R R')).opens y) :\\n   144\\t    ((relCurve C R').presheaf.germ ((d.cover.pullback (relCurveMap C R R')).opens y)\\n   145\\t        z hz).hom (Scheme.LocalEquations.pullbackEqn (relCurveMap C R R') d y)\\n   146\\t      ∈ nonZeroDivisors ((relCurve C R').presheaf.stalk z) := by\\n   147\\t  classical\\n   148\\t  obtain ⟨m, g, hg, hG⟩ := hloc\\n   149\\t  haveI himm : ∀ i : ULift.{u} (Fin m),\\n   150\\t      IsOpenImmersion (relCurveMap C R'\\n   151\\t        (Localization.Away (algebraMap R R' (g i.down)))) := fun i =>\\n   152\\t    isOpenImmersion_relCurveMap_away C R'\\n   153\\t      (Localization.Away (algebraMap R R' (g i.down))) (algebraMap R