erSpec k R).left.Opens))\\n   187\\t            = AlgHom.id k Γ((overSpec k R).left, ⊤) from Over.resAlgHom_rfl _ le_top,\\n   188\\t          AlgHom.id_comp,\\n   189\\t          show (Over.overSpecΓTopAlgEquiv k R).toAlgHom.comp\\n   190\\t              (Over.overSpecΓTopAlgEquiv k R).symm.toAlgHom\\n   191\\t            = AlgHom.id k R from\\n   192\\t            AlgHom.ext fun a => (Over.overSpecΓTopAlgEquiv k R).apply_symm_apply a]\\n   193\\t    _ = x := DivFamZarAff.mapAlgHom_id x\\n   194\\t\\n   195\\t/-- **The widened affine comparison equivalence**: on an affine test `overSpec k R`, the\\n   196\\twidened affine-opens limit collapses by evaluation at the terminal element `⊤` of the\\n   197\\taffine-opens poset to the widened value `DivFamZarAff C R n` of the test algebra.\\n   198\\t\\n   199\\tThis is what makes the vehicle a genuine extension rather than a new object: the widened\\n   200\\tcertificate lane's endpoint lands in the right-hand side, so this equivalence is the step that\\n   201\\tcarries it into the vehicle.\\n   202\\t\\n   203\\t**Exactly how far that reaches, stated so nobody over-reads it.**  It carries the endpoint into\\n   204\\ta vehicle *section over an affine test*, and no further.  Getting from there to a general test\\n   205\\tis `divFamZarAff.map` along an arbitrary morphism of test objects, which does **not** exist yet\\n   206\\t(`informal/spec-dd-r.md` ADDENDUM 8 §8.3 item 2); its input is the widened form of the base-side\\n   207\\tZariski gluing keystone `DivFamZar.exists_glue_of_away_compat`.  So the honest reading of this\\n   208\\tfile is: the widened value now has a vehicle and collapses correctly on affine tests; the\\n   209\\tZariski-continuous *extension* to all tests is still owed. -/\\n   210\\tdef divFamZarAffAffineEquiv :\\n   211\\t    divFamZarAff C n (overSpec k R) ≃ DivFamZarAff C R n where\\n   212\\t  toFun := divFamZarAffToAff C n R\\n   213\\t  invFun := divFamZarAffOfAff C n R\\n   214\\t  left_inv := divFamZarAffOfAff_divFamZarAffToAff C n R\\n   215\\t  right_inv := divFamZarAffToAff_divFamZarAffOfAff C n R\\n   216\\t\\n   217\\t/-- The widened affine comparison evaluates at the top affine open and transports along\\n   218\\t`Over.overSpecΓTopAlgEquiv`. -/\\n   219\\t@[simp]\\n   220\\tlemma divFamZarAffAffineEquiv_apply (s : divFamZarAff C n (overSpec k R)) :\\n   221\\t    divFamZarAffAffineEquiv C n R s\\n   222\\t      = DivFamZarAff.mapAlgHom (Over.overSpecΓTopAlgEquiv k R).toAlgHom\\n   223\\t          (s.1 (overSpecTopAffine R)) :=\\n   224\\t  rfl\\n   225\\t\\n   226\\t/-- The inverse widened affine comparison restricts the transported class from the top affine\\n   227\\topen. -/\\n   228\\t@[simp]\\n   229\\tlemma divFamZarAffAffineEquiv_symm_apply_val (x : DivFamZarAff C R n)\\n   230\\t    (U : (overSpec k R).left.affineOpens) :\\n   231\\t    ((divFamZarAffAffineEquiv C n R).symm x).1 U\\n   232\\t      = DivFamZarAff.mapAlgHom\\n   233\\t          ((Over.resAlgHom (overSpec k R) le_top).comp\\n   234\\t            (Over.overSpecΓTopAlgEquiv k R).symm.toAlgHom) x :=\\n   235\\t  rfl\\n   236\\t\\n   237\\tend Affine\\n   238\\t\\n   239\\t/-! ## The comparison from the chart-typed vehicle\\n   240\\t\\n   241\\t`DivFamZar.toAff` (`…AffCompare.lean`) sends a chart-typed class to a widened one at a single\\n   242\\taffine test, and `DivFamZar.toAff_mapAlgHom` (`…AffFace.lean`) makes that compatible with\\n   243\\trestriction on the explicit face.  Together they lift the comparison to the *vehicles*, which is\\n   244\\twhat a consumer holding a section over a general test needs.\\n   245\\t\\n   246\\tThe direction is old → new and only old → new.  That is not a limitation of the construction: it\\n   247\\tis the content of R2.  A widened certificate cover is an arbitrary family of affine opens, and by\\n   248\\t`informal/spec-dd-r.md` ADDENDUM 3 §2 / ADDENDUM 4 §4.3 there is a straddling divisor at every\\n   249\\tgenus `≥ 2` that no fixed pair of `P¹` charts can confine, so no map back can exist. -/\\n   250\\t\\n\", \"exit_code\": 0}, \"usage\": null}\n{\"kind\": \"tool_call\", \"at\": \"2026-08-06T04:00:20.063609+00:00\", \"text\": \"\", \"tool\": \"Bash\", \"data\": {\"command\": \"/bin/bash -lc '\\\"$HORIZON_BIN\\\" inbox --help'\"}, \"usage\": null}\n{\"kind\": \"tool_result\", \"at\": \"2026-08-06T04:00:20.063621+00:00\", \"text\": \"\", \"tool\": \"Bash\", \"data\": {\"content\": \"\\n   ___           __               __ __         _             \\n  / _ | ________/ /  ___  ___    / // /__  ____(_)__ ___  ___ \\n / __ |/ __/ __/ _ \\\\/ _ \\\\/ _ \\\\  / _  / _ \\\\/ __/ /_ // _ \\\\/ _ \\\\\\n/_/ |_/_/  \\\\__/_//_/\\\\___/_//_/ /_//_/\\\\___/_/ /_//__/\\\\___/_//_/\\n\\n v0.1.2    https://github.com/frenzymath/Archon-Horizon  ───────────────────────\\n\\n[HORIZON] ◈ REQUIRED · 8 active protections: I-1925 \\\" Parallel AJCR \\ntranslated-cover o...\\\"; I-1222 \\\"SESSION-END RE-MEASUREMENT (review-ajcr r6 \\ncl...\\\"; I-0838 \\\"  REPRESENTABILITY PU...\\\"; +5 more — consult before editing: \\n`horizon inbox list --mine --status open --kind protection --json`\\n[HORIZON] ◈ Advisory · 18 unread inbox items: I-1920 \\\" Retired task-private \\nconversatio...\\\"; I-0220 \\\"HOUSE-RULE VIOLATION: Cohomology/RelCurveColl...\\\"; \\nI-1503 \\\"TWO PROSE DEFECTS, DivisorFamilyDegreeZero.lean.\\\"; +15 more — review \\nwhen relevant: `horizon inbox list --mine --unread --json`\\n[HORIZON] ◈ Running sessions: run 0123 · task ajcr-review-sepclosed-cover — \\nmessage a team with `horizon inbox dm task:ajcr-review-sepclosed-cover --body \\n\\\"Title\\\\n\\\\nMessage\\\"`; details: `horizon ps`\\n                                                                                \\n Usage: horizon inbox [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...                               \\n                                                                                \\n Manage the local inbox.                               