entirely: picEt is CommGrpCat-valued (picEtCommGrp), so ANY representing scheme is a group object over Spec k by Yoneda transport, and a group scheme over a field is separated.\\n\\nTHE BRICK: 'group scheme over a field is separated' is absent from mathlib (measured) and from AJC (three names checked). AJCR has it at AbelianVariety/GroupSeparated.lean.\\n\\nWHAT THIS DOES NOT DO: it does not close the seam and does not witness field 1. k'-side representability remains the campaign's undischarged output.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.projectivity\",\n    \"title\": \"Smooth proper curves over a field are projective\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"pic-b\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\",\n    \"summary\": \"Closed without new hypotheses. Arbitrary relative projective coordinate charts are identified with affine space; the two normalized chart factors are closed immersions; their target opens have exact preimages equal to the pulled-back Laurent charts and cover the global map's range; target-locality gives an immersion, and properness gives projectivity. The rooted theorem isProjective_of_smoothProperGeometricallyIrreducible uses exactly the AJC smooth/proper/geometrically irreducible binders.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.quot\",\n    \"title\": \"Nitsure Quot representability\",\n    \"status\": \"rejected\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"low\",\n    \"summary\": \"OFF-PATH, retained not revived. Under projectivity, relative very ampleness and coherence, representability of the Quot functor from boundedness, the Grassmannian embedding, flattening stratification and closedness (Nitsure section 5). One open leaf: QuotRepresentability.lean:79.\\n\\nThis is the engine of the abandoned quotient endgame, not of the committed Milne-Kollar route (AJC.picrep). It is kept because the surrounding Grassmannian, graded-algebra and flattening substrate is sorry-free, genuinely reusable, and imported by the committed route; only this node's own leaf and AJC.picrep.serre are exclusive to the endgame. Do not build new consumers against HasSmoothProperQuotient.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.quotbasechange\",\n    \"title\": \"Quot base change and support\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"normal\",\n    \"summary\": \"Sorry-free. Flat base change for the Quot construction and base change of the support of a quotient; these are the inputs the Nitsure representability endgame consumes. Modules: Picard/QuotFlatBaseChange, Picard/QuotSupportBaseChange, and the quasi-coherent descent machinery of Picard/QuotScheme.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.rational-point\",\n    \"title\": \"DECIDED: etale-sheafify — no rational-point binder on the headline\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\",\n    \"summary\": \"DECIDED BY THE HUMAN 2026-07-28: BRANCH (2), ETALE-SHEAFIFY. This node is no longer a decision; it is execution work. Binding form: protection I-0491. Full reasoning: I-0372 (human comment, same date).\\n\\nTHE CLAIM THE PROJECT NOW MAKES: the Jacobian headline is stated over an ARBITRARY base field with NO rational-point binder, exactly as Challenge.lean declares it. The relative Picard functor is ETALE-sheafified and that is what gets represented — Kleimans own formulation, full challenge strength.\\n\\nWHY, and it is a specification argument. Challenge.lean binds Jacobian C with no rational point, and binds a point explicitly only where Abel-Jacobi needs one (ofCurve (P : 1 -> C)). A headline carrying [HasRationalPoint C] therefore answers a different question than the one posed. Moreover hasRationalPoint_of_curve is FALSE rather than unproved, so everything under the general-field witness rested on an inconsistent hypothesis. The build-cost asymmetry between branches, reported honestly by ajc-truth over four sessions, was explicitly NOT the deciding factor.\\n\\nTHE FOUR EXECUTION CLAUSES (protection I-0491