_proved and baseChange comes by affine-target descent from rigidPushforwardGammaBaseChange_proved.  MEASURED AT THE SYNTHESIS SITE, which is the only check that separates this from the gate-quantified-theorem trap: the three extraction theorems of RigidPushforward.lean are restated in §4 of that file WITHOUT the [HasRigidPushforward C] binder, so Lean must synthesize the gate to elaborate them, and rigidPushforward_locallyFree / _baseChange / _isLocallyTrivial all measure [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]. The same measurement applied to HasPicScheme is what exposes instHasPicScheme as poisoned (scripts/axiom-frontier.lean §8); this one comes out the other way. First campaign gate in the project to reach a clean global instance.  ROUTE FROM FOUR LEAVES TO ZERO: IsIntegral (P^1_k) from the chart-ring identification Gamma(P^1_k, D+(Xi)) = k[T] plus two-chart irreducibility; the rank identity for every k-algebra; affine-target descent reducing the baseChange field to one Gamma-level statement; then that statement, via universal exactness of ker d for a surjective two-term Cech complex. hasRigidPushforward_of_leaves is now historical, a four-leaf factorization rather than a frontier.  Blueprint: FGA chapter sec:fga_pic_milne_kollar, thm:rigid_pushforward_gate over lem:gamma_base_change over thm:rigid_pushforward_locally_free over lem:p1_integral, complete proofs, pins resolving lean_ok. CAVEAT ON THE VANISHING HYPOTHESIS: it is FiberH1Vanishing (some two-chart cover of the fibre has surjective difference map), which equals sheaf H^1 vanishing for a separated fibre with affine chart intersection; cover-independence remains the P2-interface TODO.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.rigidpushforward.basechange\",\n    \"title\": \"The baseChange gate field -- non-affine cohomology and base change\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"normal\",\n    \"summary\": \"CLOSED (run 0053 s0006, commit f4a56a754). Adelic.rigidPushforwardGammaBaseChange_proved supplies the Gamma-level statement; rigidPushforwardBaseChange_of_gamma lifts it to the field. The non-affine case -- the whole content, since every IsIso theorem for the adjoint mate in this tree wants IsAffineHom on the family while q : C_A -> Spec A is proper -- is handled by replacing affineness with the two-term Cech complex of the preimage cover: exists_gammaBaseChange_of_kerPure sandwiches exists_kerChartTensorEquiv between globalSectionsEquivKerModuleSectionDiffBase on both sides and pushforwardTopEquivBaseSections at the two tops. Cech purity comes from surjectivity (the P1 engine's first conjunct, which transports to C_A by 'exact' -- moduleSectionDiff_pushforward is rfl and Surjective sees only the underlying function, so no congruence helper was needed) plus flatness of the overlap sections (free from CoherentSheafFlat q L). Axiom-clean.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.rigidpushforward.p1integral\",\n    \"title\": \"IsIntegral P^1_k -- the last H0-finiteness leaf\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"normal\",\n    \"summary\": \"IsIntegral (P^1_k) -- CLOSED (run 0053 s0004) as the instance Adelic.instIsIntegralP1OverLeft (Picard/RigidPushforwardInstance.lean). Chain: p1AwayAlgEquiv (the chart ring of the INTEGRAL model Proj Z[X0,X1] is a polynomial ring, over any base ring; the field case was ported from the Rebuild project) -> p1ChartSectionsAlgEquivX/Y (Gamma(P^1_k, D+(Xi)) =alg[k]= k[T], the injectivity half coming from a retraction built on the CommRingCat section-ring pushout, whose compatibility square is free because Gamma(top_Scheme) is initial) -> IsDomain of both chart rings -> IsReduced.of_openCover plus the overlap being a dense irreducible subset -> IsIntegral. Axiom-clean; the instance fires by synthesis.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.rigidpushforward.rank\",\n    \"title\": \"The rank identity: rankAtStalk (p_*M) = fiberH0 M\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"normal\",\n    \"summary\": \"The rank identity rankAtStalk (p_*M) = fiberH0 M -- CLOSED (run 0053 s0004). Adelic.p1RankIdentity_proved (Picard/RigidPushforwardRank.lean) for EVERY k-algebra A, no FiniteType needed; a specialisation of the P^1-free rank_pushforward_eq_fiberH0. Three new bricks: finrank transport across a compatible pair of ring isomorphisms (no mathlib counterpart), the residue-field appLE computation extracted from FiberChart section 9, and FiberChart section 7's Cech square concluded on KERNELS instead of surjectivity. Adversarially re-verified: no broken brick, no vacuity, the finiteness/projectivity/base-change hypotheses load-bearing. Axiom-clean.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.semicontinuity\",\n    \"title\": \"B5: h0 upper semicontinuity — unconditional curve instance\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\",\n    \"summary\": \"CLOSED by a998c7c43f. instHasH0SemicontinuityOfCurve now synthesizes for every smooth proper geometrically integral curve, with no additional hypothesis. The proof pushes the line bundle to P1_A along the canonical finite map, obtains flat Cech terms and finite H0/H1, forms the finite Mumford replacement, applies kernel-rank upper semicontinuity, and transports residue fields across Gamma(Spec A, O) ≃ A. The exact target and rooted AlgebraicJacobian builds pass; both new declarations are source-clean and use only propext, Classical.choice, and Quot.sound.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.sepclosed-finite\",\n    \"title\": \"The section at a FINITE Galois level -- what G1 consumes, and the half that stays open\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\",\n    \"summary\": \"OPENED by ajc-p3 (run 0085 r2) after closing the k^s half (AJC.picrep.sepclosed-section). Unowned.\\n\\nTHE OBLIGATION. Campaign G1 spreads J5's datum to a FINITE Galois k'/k. My landed producer needs [IsSepClosed], false at every finite level -- probe fails with 'failed to synthesize IsSepClosed k''. So the route consumes a section at finite levels and the tree supplies one only at k^s.\\n\\nMATHEMATICAL CONTENT, priced not guessed: a k^s-point of a finite-type k-scheme is defined over a finite subextension, i.e. a filtered-colimit-of-schemes argument. NOT a transcription. The ring-level engine is in mathlib (RingHom.EssFiniteType.exists_eq_comp_ι_app_of_isColimit, needs FinitePresentation plus a filtered colimit cocone). The finite-subextension poset with directedness, cofiltered-op and iSup = top IS built -- in the SIBLING, at Picard/PicRepColimitResidual.lean (FinSubext, six declarations) -- but that file imports project-local modules, so per I-1183 it is a design lead and not a port.\\n\\nFREE INPUTS already measured: separableClosure.isSeparable and separableClosure.isAlgebraic both close by exact?, so the algebraicity side of the colimit presentation is not the cost.\\n\\nDO NOT re-derive Curve/SeparablyClosedRationalPoint.lean (12 declarations, sorry-free, axiom-clean) nor review-ajc's refuted closed-point route (I-1135 author's correction).\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.sepclosed-galois\",\n    \"title\": \"The section at a finite GALOIS level -- the last step of G1's spread, unpriced\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"normal\",\n    \"summary\": \"\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.sepclosed-point\",\n    \"title\": \"Rational point over a separably closed field: the Milne-Kollar route's unformalised foundation\",\n    \"status\": \"rejected\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\",\n    \"summary\": \"SUPERSEDED, not work: this row duplicated AJC.picrep.sepclosed-section (ajc-p3). Both were created within 47s of each other by two lanes reading review-ajc's one finding through two channels (issue I-1135 to horizon + hint I-1137 to p4); see I-1145 (reviewer's own account) and I-1142/I-1143 (the two lanes settling it). ajc-p3 holds the whole obligation, BOTH halves (the port and the base-change bridge). Nothing was proved against this row. TWO MEASUREMENTS from ajc-p4 that survive on the OTHER row, do not re-derive them: (1) the hint's prescribed proof route is FALSE -- over an imperfect separably closed K, A^1_K has closed points with residue field K(a^(1/p)), so pointEquivClosedPoint has no separable analogue and no closed-point argument transposes; (2) the provable signature needs [SmoothOfRelativeDimension 1 f], not bare [Smooth], because the chart lemma needs the numeral to get etale-over-A^1.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.sepclosed-section\",\n    \"title\": \"The Milne-Kollar route root: rational point over a separably closed field, and the HasRationalPoint bridge\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\",\n    \"summary\": \"CLOSED by ajc-p3 (run 0085 r2), pinned 9e9ef819cd / e0d70544f3. Curve/SeparablyClosedRationalPoint.lean, rooted, 10 declarations, sorry-free, all axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] vs a control firing sorryAx. lake build AlgebraicJacobian EXIT=0, 8868 jobs, no new sorry. Non-vacuity: P1 over Q via Adelic.p1Over, both binders inferInstance, bridge typechecks, SeparableClosure Q != Q.\\n\\nWHAT IS CLOSED. The section at k^s, unconditionally on C(k): hasRationalPoint_of_isSepClosed closes the exact goal PicEtSubcanonical.lean:82-89 asserted without a producer. Two shapes of the bridge, at GeometricallyIntegral and at GeometricallyIrreducible -- the latter is what Challenge.lean and picardJacobianWitness carry, so a headline consumer needs no bridging instance. Sections 1-3 transcribed from the sibling (brick DAT-P, import Mathlib only, no carrier gap); section 4 is new here.\\n\\nWHAT IS NOT, all four measured not assumed (I-1182). (1) G1 spreads J5's datum to a FINITE Galois level, where IsSepClosed is false -- probe fails; that step is a THIRD obligation no site prices. (2) J1 wants a TUPLE; density transports but two DISTINCT sections do not follow. (3) ZERO formal consumers: cluster J is campaign prose, not Lean binders. (4) fgaPicardRepresentability untouched.\\n\\nNEXT LANE: the finite-level section is the open half and it looks cheaper than it is. Do not re-derive sections 1-3. review-ajc's I-1135 proof route is FALSE (imperfect separably closed K has non-rational closed points, so pointEquivClosedPoint has no separable analogue); the numeral binder is load-bearing.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.serre\",\n    \"title\": \"Serre finiteness and Hilbert polynomial\",\n    \"status\": \"rejected\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"low\",\n    \"summary\": \"OFF-PATH, retained not revived. Finite generation of the section graded module plus the fibrewise graded Hilbert function; the two open leaves in SerreFiniteness.lean.\\n\\nNeeded by the Quot endgame (AJC.picrep.quot), not by the committed Milne-Kollar route, whose uniform-H1 input comes from cluster P instead (AJC.rr, task ajc-rr). Serre finiteness remains of independent interest and may yet be the cheapest route to the H0-finite-generation leaf flagged in RigidPushforwardP1Engine.lean.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.tensor\",\n    \"title\": \"Pullback-tensor and fibre base change\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\",\n    \"summary\": \"AUDITED 2026-07-30 (review-ajc r4). This row bundles TWO deliverables; the first is LANDED and sorry-free, the second is genuinely OPEN. The row read as wholly unstarted since its creation on 2026-07-23 and was never re-measured, so a lane pricing it would have re-proved the landed half.\\n\\nCLAUSE 1 -- DONE, DO NOT RE-PROVE. 'The canonical pullback tensor comparison is an isomorphism' IS proved: Scheme.Modules.pullbackTensorIsoOfLocallyTrivial (Picard/TensorObjSubstrate/PullbackTensorIso.lean:153), for line bundles via the chart-chase plus isIso_of_isIso_restrict. Zero body sorries in that file (comments stripped). It has a one-sided companion pullbackTensorIsoOfRightLocallyTrivial and the IsIso form pullbackTensorMap_isIso_of_right_locallyTrivial (PullbackTensorOneSided.lean:275, :264). Already CONSUMED at 8+ sites in Picard/RelPicFunctor.lean (:366, :389, :433, :468, :609, :792, :819) and cited by QuotFunctorDef.lean:448 -- so this is settled substrate, not a frontier.\\n\\nCLAUSE 2 -- OPEN, and the file that would host it says so in the subjunctive. 'The quasi-coherent tensor-section input used by Hilbert-function base change' is NOT landed. Picard/TensorSectionFormula.lean:145-155 states that the affine tensor-section formula 'WOULD give, for A B quasi-coherent and V affine, the fact that the section restriction Gamma(A tensor B, V) -> Gamma(A tensor B, D(f)) is IsLocalizedModule (powers f)' -- and then supplies only the CONVERSE packaging (isQuasicoherent_of_isLocalizedModule_basicOpen, :185), explicitly described as 'exactly the criterion the 01CB (tensorObj/sheafTensorObj) instance feeds ONCE THE AFFINE SECTION-LOCALIZATION IS IN HAND'. That antecedent is absent.\\n\\nMEASURED ABSENT, with the project filter (a bare horizon search returns SubProjects hits under identical names -- I-1124): tensorSectionHom_isIso, isIso_tensorSectionHom, tensorSection_localization, affine_tensorSection all return no exact-name match under --lib Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge. No instance of IsQuasicoherent for tensorObj exists anywhere in AlgebraicJacobian/. What DOES exist in that file is the substrate: tensorSectionHom (:101), its naturality (:115), the top-level identification (:123), and the categorical crux isIso_sheafification_tensorSectionUnit (:137).\\n\\nSO THE OPEN OBLIGATION, named: the affine tensor-section formula -- for A B quasi-coherent and V affine, Gamma(A,V) tensor_{Gamma(X,V)} Gamma(B,V) -> Gamma(A tensor B, V) is an isomorphism (equivalently the basic-open localization form). Its heart is RingTheory.Localization.BaseChange ((M tensor_R N)_f = M_f tensor_{R_f} N_f), per the file's own note. Discharging it feeds isQuasicoherent_of_isLocalizedModule_basicOpen and yields the 01CB instance.\\n\\nNOT ON THE CRITICAL PATH to the seam. The Hilbert-function base-change consumers are all sorry-free already (GradedHilbertSerre, HilbertPolynomial, QuotFlatBaseChange, QuotSupportBaseChange, RigidPushforward{Chart,Gamma}BaseChange, SectionBaseChange -- 0 body sorries each), and no .lean file flags the tensor comparison as open. Nothing consumes this row as blocking. Left pending deliberately: it is real but off the representability critical path, so it is not a round target.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.rr\",\n    \"title\": \"Riemann--Roch, divisors, and the adelic genus\",\n    \"status\": \"active\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"normal\",\n    \"summary\": \"Riemann--Roch, divisors, and the adelic genus. Cluster-P items 1 and 3 (bounded H1 vanishing, global generation) and exact Riemann--Roch are CLOSED at AJC's own curve under three curve binders (RiemannRoch/Ledger/FiberBound.lean). Item 2, extension-uniformity, is still OPEN but is now ONE input rather than two. r5 decomposed the open half into (a) base-field invariance of the genus and (b) a kappa-independent degree bound on a vanishing base divisor; r6 PROVED (a). Ledger/SectionsFieldBaseChange.lean supplies the comparison map r5 identified as the actual deliverable -- Gamma(C,V) tensor_k kappa = Gamma(C_kappa, fst^-1 V), kappa-linearly, for every qcqs open and every field extension -- and Ledger/GenusFieldInvariance.lean turns it into genus C_kappa = genus C for EVERY field extension, with no finiteness, separability, perfectness or algebraic-closedness hypothesis. Both files sorry-free, kernel-built, 20 declarations axiom-clean measured at SYNTHESIS sites with two live controls (one reaching a sorry through an import). Engine: termwise Cech base change plus right-exactness on the cokernel -- not semicontinuity, not Mumford II.5, and not Serre duality, which this workspace still does not have (r5's retraction of the 2g-1 shortcut stands). Provenance: argument adapted from AJCR's H1BaseFieldInvariance.lean, statements rederived at AJC carriers; not portable as-is because AJCR states it over AffineTwoCover (absent from AJC entirely) and because AJC lacked the right-exactness brick quotRangeBaseChangeEquiv. r5's carrier measurement is corrected: the object-level rfl between AJC and AJCR base-change carriers was true but was NOT the obstacle -- the cover-level assembly and the missing brick were. WHAT REMAINS: input (b) only, uniformVanishing_of_uniformBaseDivisor's single hypothesis, genuinely open in AJC and AJCR both (AJCR's analogue is a Nat.find per field). UniformVanishing C is NOT proved. Global generation is untouched and is still not uniform over extensions. Caveat: the Ledger vanishing chain including these two files sits outside the root import cone (262 modules reachable from the roll-up); rooting is one import line, outside this task's write scope.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.rr.adelic\",\n    \"title\": \"Adelic Riemann--Roch and cohomological finiteness\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"normal\",\n    \"summary\": \"Sorry-free. The adelic model of H^0 and H^1 for a smooth proper curve: a nonconstant map to P^1, its finiteness, the P^1 base case and chart data, the adelic cokernel, the Euler-characteristic ledger, and unconditional finiteness of the genus. Modules: RiemannRoch/CohomologyKit and the RiemannRoch/Adelic package (Substrate, NonconstantToP1, FiniteMapToP1, FinitenessP1, P1BaseCase, P1ChartData, Cokernel, ChiLedger, CechAcyclicInstance, CechComparisonGate, GateInstances, GenusFiniteness, GenusUnconditional).\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.rr.degvanish\",\n    \"title\": \"Single-field bounded vanishing on a degree half-space\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"normal\",\n    \"summary\": \"DONE (run 0074 r3, ajc-rr). Ledger/DegreeVanishing.lean, 12 decls, 0 sorries, kernel-checked (lake build 8581 jobs exit 0), 16/16 axiom-clean including four synthesis-site probes at the challenge curve.\\n\\nThe order-cone peel of AJC.rr.sectiondrop reaches a DEGREE HALF-SPACE. subsingleton_hModule_one_of_deg_ge: from ONE base vanishing at ONE divisor D0, H1(O(D)) = 0 for every D with deg D >= deg D0 + 1 - chi(O_X). Also exact Riemann-Roch above that bound, the D0 = 0 form (unconditional given H1(O_C) = 0, hence unconditional at genus zero), and the contrapositive that non-vanishing H1 is a bounded-degree phenomenon.\\n\\nThe mathematical point, and it retracts this lane's own r2 claim: sectiondrop published exists_bound_of_cofinal_vanishing as an OPEN hypothesis, saying nothing in AJC or AJCR produces it. Both ingredients were in the same directory. H1 vanishing is a linear-equivalence invariant (Ledger/MulEquiv.mulEquivDivisorSheaf), so the whole class of D0 is available to the peel; and riemann_inequality (Ledger/ChiLedger) manufactures the translating unit once deg(D - D0) + chi >= 1. The peel never needed the GIVEN D0.\\n\\nRESIDUE: one base vanishing at a general curve, i.e. the AJCR FLVVanishing:302 port (measured: 59-module local closure; new layer FLVFiberToolkit/FLVLattice/FLVQcoh/FiberTwist/Degree plus AffineVanishingQcoh/QcohSections; Degree drags in Picard/ presentation modules the Ledger tree lacks).\\n\\nNOT this row, and still genuinely open: extension-uniformity (every statement is over the single field K; the bound depends on X, K, D0) and global generation (no evaluation map appears). Scratch-path: DegreeVanishing imports SectionDrop, which is out of the root cone (I-0600).\\n\\nRESIDUE CLOSED 2026-07-28 (run 0074 r4, same lane). The \\\"one base vanishing at a general curve\\\"\\nabove is no longer a residue. Ledger/FiberVanishing.lean ports AJCR's fibrewise large-twist\\nvanishing (bodies unchanged) and Ledger/FiberBound.lean composes it with the chi-ledger, giving\\n\\n  exists_bound_subsingleton_hModule_one_curve : three curve binders, NO vanishing hypothesis\\n  exists_bound_h0_eq_genus_curve             : h0(O(D)) = 1 - genus C + deg D above a threshold\\n\\nThe pi is CONSTRUCTED inside (MapToP1.exists_isFinite_isDominant_toP1) and both Module.Finite\\nbinders are SYNTHESISED by ChiCurve, so nothing is left for a caller to instantiate. The quantifier\\norder is what makes the bound uniform in D: the tower threshold is taken at the FIXED divisor 0,\\nfixing one D0 = n0*F before any D is seen, and the degree slack is then carried by the\\nlinear-equivalence translate this row already built.\\n\\n41/41 axiom-clean with a firing control. Eight new files, 2,556 lines, 0 sorries.\\n\\nSTILL OPEN, unchanged: extension-uniformity. Every constant here lives over the single field K.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.rr.divisor\",\n    \"title\": \"Weil divisors and the degree map\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"normal\",\n    \"summary\": \"Sorry-free. The group of Weil divisors on a curve, the degree of a divisor, and the divisor functor with its base-change well-definedness. Modules: Picard/DivDegree, Picard/DivFunctorDef. The one open obligation on this substrate, deg(div f) = 0, is tracked separately under AJC.rr.principal.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.rr.extuniform\",\n    \"title\": \"Extension-uniform H1 vanishing: one threshold serving every field extension\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"normal\",\n    \"summary\": \"RE-PRICED 2026-07-29 (ajc-p2, run 0084): the residue is the DEGREE BOUND ALONE. Read the novelty caveat at the bottom -- it is part of the finding.\\n\\nUniformBaseDivisor C d has two clauses.\\n\\n(1) EXISTENCE of a vanishing divisor over every field extension -- a THEOREM AT EVERY GENUS: Ledger/BaseDivisorEveryField.exists_base_subsingleton_baseChangeField, three curve binders, no genus hypothesis, no hypothesis on kappa/k. Kernel EXIT=0, axiom-clean. CARRIER VERIFIED BY MACHINE: UniformBaseDivisor C d is derivable from it plus a hypothesis with NO vanishing content, only deg kappa D0 <= d -- so the carriers are the same object, not similar spellings.\\n\\n(2) DEGREE BOUND -- open, and it is the whole gap.\\n\\nWHY THE OLD PRICING WAS WRONG. The genus-0 ceiling of the previous producer (VanishingFieldDescent.uniformBaseDivisor_zero_of_subsingleton) belongs to its ROUTE: transporting the UNIT sheaf's vanishing by faithful flatness forces the zero divisor as witness, hence forces H1(O_C) to vanish. It is not a property of the obligation, which never mentions the unit sheaf. GenusFieldInvariance.lean's index said otherwise and is corrected (6618d6979). The UPSTREAM ExtensionUniformity docstring had it right all along -- when two docstrings about one gap disagree, the one nearer the definition tends to be right. Filed as I-0897; lesson as I-0906.\\n\\nNOVELTY CAVEAT, from a fresh-context audit (I-0914) whose points I re-verified and accepted (8decce128). The PRICING is right; the THEOREMS add no new mathematics. Both existence statements derive at the parent commit with no new lemma, instance or import; the proof body is FiberBound's exists_bound_subsingleton_hModule_one_curve with one 'exact' renamed; and uniformBaseDivisor_of_exists_deg_le is the IDENTITY (its hypothesis is definitionally its conclusion, Iff.rfl closes it). One audit clause was refuted: the pre-existing threshold form does NOT imply these without exists_deg_ge, whose hypothesis (a non-generic point of positive residue degree) is not free on C -- so they are incomparable inputs, not a chain.\\n\\nREMAINING OBLIGATION, exact: a uniform bound on n0(kappa) * deg_kappa F_kappa, where n0 is the Noetherian fibre-lattice stabilisation index (FiberVanishing.lean) re-run at each base field.\\n\\nWHERE TO START, measured this round: finrank_stabilisationAmbient_eq_h1 (fd811e5fd) shows the quotient in which n0 is chosen has dimension h1(O(D + n*F)), so at D = 0 it is the GENUS -- base-field-invariant. A bound n0 <= genus C would close the clause with d := genus C * deg_kappa F_kappa. The missing step is STRICTNESS: a monotone chain in a g-dimensional space may repeat a term without reaching the top, so bounded dimension alone bounds nothing. n0 <= genus MUST NOT be cited as available.\\n\\nDEAD END: absolute large-degree vanishing (Serre duality deg >= 2g-1) is absent from BOTH projects -- searched. And DegreeVanishing's threshold is deg D0 + 1 - chi(O), stated relative to a base divisor already in hand, so bounding deg D0 by it is circular.\\n\\nALSO RELEVANT (I-0908, reviewer): closing P5 does not close the seam. fgaPicardRepresentability clause (1) is about picEt, while every Milne-Kollar milestone targets picSharp; the gap is tracked at AJC.picrep.etale-rep and needs a human decision.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.rr.ledger\",\n    \"title\": \"The AJCR chi-ledger, ported into AJC and unconditional at a curve\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"normal\",\n    \"summary\": \"RiemannRoch/Ledger/, 41 files, 9877 lines, sorry-free (re-measured at HEAD by the janitor\\npass of run 0074; the earlier \\\"38 files, ~9.4k\\\" was a mid-session count). PORT of the AJCR\\nchi-ledger cone (proof bodies byte-identical bar named adaptations) plus four AJC-native\\nrederivations.\\n\\nLANDED: chi(O(D)) = 1 - genus C + deg D on AJC's OWN frozen genus, binders\\n[IsProper][SmoothOfRelativeDimension 1][GeometricallyIrreducible] only -- both Module.Finite\\ncohomology binders are SYNTHESISED, not assumed, measured at a synthesis site rather than at\\nthe declaration. Plus riemann_inequality, h0 unbounded along n*x, deg_divOf.\\n\\nAJC-NATIVE (not ports, no producer existed in either project): ledgerGenus_eq_genus (the\\nuniverse gap is an annotation, discharged via chgUnivLinearEquiv); residueDeg = 1 over kbar,\\nwhich collapses the residue weighting to the bare coefficient sum; divOf agrees with\\nWeilDivisor.principal coefficient-wise INCLUDING SIGNS.\\n\\nNOT DONE: the port is rootable (co-importability verified after fixing three name collisions,\\nI-0576) but is imported by NOTHING -- AlgebraicJacobian.lean carries no RiemannRoch.Ledger\\nimport and nothing outside Ledger/ references it, re-confirmed at HEAD. So the root target\\nelaborates none of the cone and the standing axiom probe never sees it. The root roll-up is\\noutside this lane's write scope; tracked as issue I-0600. Extension-uniformity and global\\ngeneration remain untouched; single-field bounded vanishing is not supplied by this ledger.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.rr.principal\",\n    \"title\": \"Principal divisors have degree zero\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"normal\",\n    \"summary\": \"Principal divisors have degree zero. CLOSED 2026-07-28 (run 0067, ajc-pic0av, commit 8b654f78d).\\nRiemannRoch/WeilDivisor.lean has ZERO sorries. principal_degree_zero is proved at its own binders\\n(smooth proper geometrically irreducible curve over kbar, regular in codim 1), axiom-clean\\n([propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], no sorryAx), 8607 jobs, zero warnings.\\n\\nTHE IMPORT INVERSION WAS NEVER REAL, and that is the whole story of why this took four sessions.\\nThree predecessor summaries -- including two of mine -- recorded the leaf as blocked because\\nLedger/PrincipalTransport.degree_principal_eq_zero_curve, the theorem with the leaf's conclusion,\\nhas a 51-file cone containing WeilDivisor.lean. That measurement is correct and irrelevant: it is\\nthe cone of the CONSUMER, and PrincipalTransport is downstream only because it also imports the\\nindex bridge for convenience. The INPUTS were always importable:\\n  Ledger/OrdCompare             7 files, WeilDivisor-free\\n  Ledger/ResidueOneAlgClosed   37 files, WeilDivisor-free\\n  Adelic/FiniteMapToP1          4 files, WeilDivisor-free\\nUnion 42, containing neither WeilDivisor nor CurveCoheight nor CurveDivisorIndexBridge; cycle\\ndetection over all modules with the three new edges returns zero.\\n\\nAdelic.coheight_le_one_of_curve is the one nobody had checked. It was called 'strictly downstream'\\nin three roadmap summaries, in CurveCoheight.lean's own docstring and in the leaf's comment block,\\nand its cone is FOUR files -- it is downstream of Genus, which WeilDivisor.lean already imported.\\nSo the coheight bound, which CurveCoheight.lean carries as an explicit hypothesis precisely\\nbecause it was thought unavailable upstream, is simply discharged at the leaf.\\n\\nTHE PROOF, and it needs NO case split. Hartshorne II.6.10's route (finite phi : C -> P^1 from a\\nnon-constant f, then degree multiplicativity under finite pullback) is NOT taken and its two\\ngeometric sub-lemmas are no longer owed by this project. Instead the ported chi-ledger\\nchi(O(D)) = chi(O_C) + deg D gives deg(div g) = 0 by transporting chi along O(0) = O(-div g)\\n(Ledger/ChiLedger.deg_divOf, a devissage induction over closed points with skyscraper quotients).\\nThree carrier comparisons connect it to this project's degree, each DISCHARGED not assumed:\\n * ORDERS: ordZ read additively = the Ring.ordFrac-based RationalMap.order, no sign correction\\n   (Ledger/OrdCompare.ordZ_toAdd_eq_log_ordFrac);\\n * INDEX SETS: PrimeDivisor = {x != eta}, reproved inline in two lines (le_antisymm of the\\n   coheight bound against one_le_coheight_of_ne_genericPoint) since CurveCoheight imports the leaf;\\n * WEIGHTS: over kbar the residue weighting collapses to the bare coefficient sum\\n   (Ledger/ResidueOneAlgClosed). This is where [IsAlgClosed] is load-bearing and it is NOT\\n   bookkeeping -- over a general field the weighted and unweighted degrees are different numbers.\\nSince the chain is uniform in f, the former constant/non-constant split is deleted: a constant f\\nhas every coefficient zero and the same chain returns 0.\\n\\nSCOPE, stated plainly: the theorem carries [IsAlgClosed kbar], as it always did. The\\ngeneral-field statement is NOT proved and is not what this node asked for. An earlier version of\\nthis summary said the leaf had no IsAlgClosed binder; that was wrong, and ajc-rr repeated it from\\nhere -- the theorem has bound it since it was written.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.rr.sectiondrop\",\n    \"title\": \"Section drop and the H1 peel on the ledger carrier\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"normal\",\n    \"summary\": \"Ledger/SectionDrop.lean, new, ~490 lines, 19 declarations, 0 sorries, LSP clean, KERNEL-CHECKED (olean built after last edit).\\n\\nTHE RESULT: on the ported chi-ledger carrier, H1-vanishing propagation is a theorem rather than a hypothesis. The devissage quotient 0 -> O(D-x) -> O(D) -> sky -> 0 has a SKYSCRAPER third term, so H1(sky) = 0, so ChiSlice.surjective_map_f applies at n = 1 and H1(O(D-x)) -> H1(O(D)) is onto.\\n\\nGENUINELY NEW HERE (checked against AJCR after a false first claim, see below):\\n * subsingleton_hModule_one_of_le -- the D0 <= D ORDER form of the peel;\\n * the two-sided section drop h0(O(D-x)) <= h0(O(D)) <= h0(O(D-x)) + [kappa(x):K];\\n * the drop IDENTITY: h0 gain plus h1 loss equals the residue degree exactly;\\n * exact Riemann-Roch on the order-cone above a vanishing D0, and the exact drop there;\\n * exists_bound_of_cofinal_vanishing -- degree-threshold vanishing reduced to one named COFINALITY hypothesis.\\n\\nTHE PEEL CHAIN NEEDS NO FINITENESS: 11 of 19 declarations omit both Module.Finite cohomology binders (the linter found this, not me). Hence vanishing is stated as Subsingleton (H1 ...), never h1 = 0 -- the latter is vacuously true for infinite-dimensional H1 since Module.finrank reads 0 there. Filed as memory I-0620.\\n\\nTWO RETRACTIONS OF THIS LANE'S OWN CLAIMS, found by fresh-context ground review (I-0623), verified in AJCR source and fixed at b7383a4d5:\\n\\n 1. The PEEL CHAIN IS A RE-DERIVATION, not new. AJCR RiemannRoch/FLVClass.lean already has peel_single (:260), peel_nsmul_single (:277), peel_effective (:292) -- the same three steps, the same Subsingleton spelling, the same variable block, the same surjective_map_f. Cause: this lane searched SectionBound.lean (where the finrank INEQUALITY lives), found it, and never opened FLVClass.lean (where the PROPAGATION lives). Also h0_divisorSheaf_of_subsingleton_of_le duplicates AJCR h0_eq_deg_add_chi_of_subsingleton_hModule_one at a fixed divisor.\\n\\n 2. THE BASE VANISHING IS NOT OPEN. This lane reported it open \\\"at every curve, P^1 included\\\"; that was measured inside AJC's Ledger tree only and is false about the workspace. AJCR RiemannRoch/FLVVanishing.lean:302, subsingleton_hModule_divisorSheaf_one_of_isFinite_toP1, proves it ON THIS CARRIER: for finite dominant pi : Y -> P^1 compatible with the structure maps and any D, there is n0 with H1(O(D + n*F)) = 0 for all n >= n0, F the fibre divisor.\\n\\nSO THE NEXT STEP IS A PORT, NOT A PROOF: AJC has no fibre-divisor / finite-map-to-P1 layer on the Ledger carrier. Porting it discharges the base, and exists_bound_of_cofinal_vanishing is already the right shape to consume it, since a tower D + n*F is exactly a cofinal family.\\n\\nSTILL OPEN: extension-uniformity (nothing here quantifies over a second field; AJCR lacks it too). Global generation is untouched on this carrier -- the adelic lane owns that bridge on its own degK carrier, gated on hledger.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.substrate\",\n    \"title\": \"Foundational substrate (rigidity, genus, and line bundles)\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"normal\",\n    \"summary\": \"Complete and sorry-free: RigidityLemma, Genus, AbelJacobi, line-bundle coherence and pullback, RelPicFunctor, and RelativeSpec. The earlier experimental cotangent modules were deliberately removed and are not part of the current AJC route.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.substrate.descent\",\n    \"title\": \"Gluing and descent\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"normal\",\n    \"summary\": \"Sorry-free. Gluing schemes and quasi-coherent data along an open cover, Zariski-local representability descent, and semilinear (Galois) descent for modules and algebras. Modules: Picard/GlueDescent, Picard/ZariskiDescentRepresentability, Picard/GaloisDescent/SemilinearModules, Picard/GaloisDescent/SemilinearAlgebras.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.substrate.genus\",\n    \"title\": \"Genus and the Abel--Jacobi interface\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"normal\",\n    \"summary\": \"Sorry-free. The genus of a smooth proper curve as dim_k H^1(C, O_C) together with the Abel--Jacobi interface consumed by the final witness. Modules: Genus, AbelJacobi.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.substrate.relspec\",\n    \"title\": \"Relative Spec, projective morphisms, and section rings\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"normal\",\n    \"summary\": \"Sorry-free. The relative spectrum of a quasi-coherent algebra, projective space and projective morphisms over a base, the universal property of the section ring, and localisation of invertible sections with its graded bridge. Modules: Picard/RelativeSpec, Picard/ProjectiveSpace, Picard/ProjectiveMorphism, Picard/SectionRingUniversal, Picard/InvertibleSectionLocalization, Picard/InvertibleGrBridge.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.substrate.rigidity\",\n    \"title\": \"Rigidity lemma\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"normal\",\n    \"summary\": \"Sorry-free. Mumford's rigidity lemma in Form I and the consequence that a pointed morphism of group schemes is a homomorphism, in hypotheses weaker than Milne I.1.2. Module: RigidityLemma.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.substrate.schemes\",\n    \"title\": \"Curve and scheme base objects\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"normal\",\n    \"summary\": \"Sorry-free. Geometric connectedness and integrality of curve sections, base change of the curve along a field extension, standard-smooth relative dimension, finite Galois quotients and their affine charts, and stable affine covers. Modules: RiemannRoch/CurveBaseChange, Picard/GeometricallyConnectedSection, Picard/FiniteGaloisQuotient, Picard/FiniteGaloisQuotientAffine, Picard/GaloisQuotientGlue, Picard/StableAffineCover, Albanese/StandardSmoothDimension, Albanese/SmoothPrimeRegularity.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.substrate.sheaves\",\n    \"title\": \"Quasi-coherent sheaves on schemes\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"normal\",\n    \"summary\": \"Sorry-free. The tilde construction and its sections, restriction to basic opens, the over-category equivalence for sheaves on an open, conservativity of a module cover, exactness of tilde, structure-sheaf module objects over the base field, and quasi-coherence of pullbacks. Modules: Cohomology/QcohTildeSections, Cohomology/QcohRestrictBasicOpen, Cohomology/TildeExactness, Cohomology/ModulesCoverConservativity, Cohomology/SheafCompose, Cohomology/StructureSheafAb, Cohomology/StructureSheafModuleK, Cohomology/PullbackQuasicoherent, Picard/SheafOverEquivalence.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"AJC.substrate.tangent\",\n    \"title\": \"Dual numbers and tangent spaces\",\n    \"status\": \"done\",\n    \"owner\": \"\",\n    \"priority\": \"normal\",\n    \"summary\": \"Sorry-free. Units of the dual numbers, scheme-valued points over k[eps], the identity-section tangent vector, the stalk-algebra description of the tangent space, and the dual-number cocycle presentation used for the Pic^0 tangent space. Modules: Picard/DualNumberUnits, Picard/TangentSpaceDualNumbers, Picard/TangentSpaceSchemePoints, Picard/TangentSpaceIdentitySection, Picard/TangentSpaceStalkAlgebra, Picard/Pic0DualNumberCocycle, Picard/Pic0TangentSpace.\"\n  }\n]\n", "exit_code": 0}, "usage": null}
/home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon/.archon-horizon/runs/0093/sessions/0014-horizon-pic-b/transcript.jsonl:62:{"kind": "tool_result", "at": "2026-07-31T00:24:30.721100+00:00", "text": "", "tool": "Bash", "data": {"content": "[HORIZON] ◈ REQUIRED · 5 active protections: I-1222 \"SESSION-END RE-MEASUREMENT \n(review-ajcr r6 cl...\"; I-0074 \"**FGA picSharp rewire LANDED (run 0008): \nrout...\"; I-0838 \"  REPRESENTABILITY PU...\"; +2 more — consult before editing: \n`horizon inbox list --mine --status open --kind protection --json`\n[HORIZON] ◈ Advisory · 26 unread inbox items: I-1624 \"RESULT/RELEASE pic-e (0095\nr5): the divisor q...\"; I-1623 \"AJCR ROOT BUILD IS BROKEN AT HEAD in \npic-d's...\"; I-1622 \"A 'STRICTLY WEAKER REDUCTION' CAN BE INTERDER...\"; +23 more\n— review when relevant: `horizon inbox list --mine --unread --json`\n[HORIZON] ◈ Running sessions: run 0092 · task pic-c; run 0095 · task pic-e; run \n0096 · task pic-g — message a team with `horizon inbox dm task:pic-c --body \n\"Title\\n\\nMessage\"`; details: `horizon ps`\n{\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.jacobian\",\n      \"title\": \"Jacobian via Picard scheme and Albanese\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"North star: construct the Jacobian of a smooth proper geometrically integral curve as Pic^0, prove it is an abelian variety of dimension equal to the genus, and establish the Albanese universal property. The children distinguish completed infrastructure from remaining representability, base-change, Pic0, and Albanese obligations. The supporting divisor blueprint now exposes principal degree zero through the exact finite-map and pullback-degree gates and keeps coefficient degree over an algebraically closed field separate from the general-field adelic degree.\",\n      \"status\": \"active\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.jacobian\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"9dac093df\",\n        \"a49bf3c38\",\n        \"f5e9c3b5e\",\n        \"21eefaf60\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 0,\n      \"subtree_done\": 72,\n      \"subtree_total\": 114\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.albanese\",\n      \"title\": \"Albanese and abelian-variety leg\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Albanese and abelian-variety leg. Three of five children done (.ab, .codim1, .rationalmaps);\\n.symmetric and .universal remain, and BOTH are blocked on the same single object.\\n\\nSTATE AT RUN 0069 r5, measured not estimated:\\n * Milne III.6.1 (the Albanese universal property) is PROVED over the symmetric power taken\\n   as an interface -- Albanese/AlbaneseFromData.lean, sorry-free, both directions.\\n * Milne Lemma 3.3 (pure codim-1 indeterminacy into a group variety) is PROVED, and with it\\n   Thm 3.2's rational-map extension is unconditional. CodimOneExtension.lean and\\n   RigidityLemma.lean are at ZERO sorries -- any brief or note citing sorries there is\\n   quoting docstring prose.\\n * ALL SIX remaining sorries in the leg are in Albanese/AlbaneseUP.lean, and every one is\\n   stated against SymmetricPower, a sorry-BODIED definition. They are undischargeable as\\n   stated, not merely unproved: an equation between morphisms out of a junk term carries no\\n   information. albanese_universal_property reports sorryAx and must not be called landed.\\n\\nTHE ONE MISSING OBJECT is Sym^g C for the proper curve, equivalently the instance\\nHasColimit (permDiagram C g) in Over (Spec kbar) -- proved EQUIVALENT to the datum the\\nAlbanese theorems consume (SymPowColimit.hasColimit_permDiagram_iff), so the reduction is\\nlossless. Over.forget creates colimits, so no over-category bookkeeping is needed: it is a\\nstatement about Scheme.\\n\\nTHE AFFINE HALF IS NOW DONE, with its carrier named and over the base: SymPowTensorAction\\n.lean (the S_n-action on the n-fold tensor power of a RING -- mathlib had permutation only as\\na linear equiv, so Milne's carrier was not even STATEABLE) and SymPowInvariantsUnder.lean\\n(the invariants ARE the limit in Under k, dually a colimit in (Under k)^op).\\n\\nWHAT REMAINS IS THE GLUING, and it is now three named inputs rather than an unsized\\nsubproject. One of the three closed this round: StableAffineCoverGroup.lean proves every\\npoint has a G-STABLE affine open neighbourhood for a bare finite group -- the same proof as\\nPicard/StableAffineCover.lean, whose Galois binder its body never touches. The other two:\\n(i) cocycle/overlap agreement of the affine chart quotients; (ii) OrbitsInAffineOpen for the\\ncurve, which is where quasi-projectivity enters and mathlib has no quasi-projectivity\\nvocabulary at this pin.\\n\\nAvailability measured at this pin so nobody re-searches: HasCoproducts Scheme YES,\\nHasCoequalizers/HasPushouts Scheme NO, Scheme.GlueData YES.\\n\\nDELTA, run 0069 r7 (nothing above is retracted; the sorry count is UNCHANGED at six).\\nThe affine half of the symmetric-power route closed out. Item 3 of the four-item glue-data\\nbill is DONE (Albanese/TensorPowerCofan.lean packages the tensor power as the n-ary coproduct\\nin Under k), so the bill is 3 SUPPLIED / 1 OPEN, and the affine carrier is now NAMED at both\\nends: SymPowAffineCarrier.tensorPowerOpIsoPiObj (the n-fold product permDiagram is built on IS\\nop of the tensor power, actions matched) and SymPowAffineQuotient.colimitPermDiagramIsoFixed\\n(the colimit IS op of Milne's (A^{\\u2297n})^{S_n}). SymPowColimit \\u00a75's bold caveat \\\"the carrier is\\nnot named in Lean\\\" is discharged and deleted. 12 new declarations, all kernel-checked EXIT=0\\nand axiom-clean with controls firing sorryAx.\\n\\nWHAT THIS DOES NOT DO, stated because \\\"3 of 4\\\" invites the wrong inference: item 4 -- the\\noverlap/cocycle agreement of the chart quotients and OrbitsInAffineOpen FOR THE CURVE -- is\\nthe whole of the geometry, and it is untouched. The affine chain is stated over mkUnder k A in\\n(Under k)-op; C is a proper curve in Over (Spec kbar). Nothing in AlbaneseUP /\\nAlbaneseFromData / AlbaneseFromColimit mentions any of the new names (checked, zero hits), so\\nthis is integration WITHIN the affine story, not with the capstone. Also unbuilt: the second\\nbridge of Milne's affine half, that (Under k)-op IS affine k-schemes -- so all of it is\\nk-algebra language rather than Spec-language.\\n\\nTWO SELF-CORRECTIONS worth more than the lemmas, both caught before or by the kernel:\\n (a) I first offered an EXISTENCE restatement as the carrier-naming payoff. Vacuous: it was\\n     literally symPowData_affineAlgebra instantiated, and which proof supplied the instance is\\n     invisible in it. Then I measured the instance -- infer_instance discharges the HasColimit\\n     from cocompleteness alone -- so that theorem adds nothing provable either. Naming an\\n     object requires a statement that MENTIONS the object.\\n (b) My first header said the \\\"carrier is not named\\\" caveat was \\\"now false\\\" on the strength of\\n     naming the INPUT (the object the action acts on) when the caveat is about the QUOTIENT.\\n     Input vs output. Repaired, then the quotient actually proved, then the caveat deleted.\",\n      \"status\": \"active\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.jacobian\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.albanese\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"21eefaf60\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 1,\n      \"subtree_done\": 3,\n      \"subtree_total\": 5\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.albanese.ab\",\n      \"title\": \"Auslander--Buchsbaum and the coheight bridge\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Sorry-free. The Auslander--Buchsbaum formula and the coheight bridge relating codimension to depth, together with pole purity; these feed the codimension-one extension of rational maps. Modules: Albanese/AuslanderBuchsbaum, Albanese/CoheightBridge, Albanese/PolePurity.\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.albanese\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.albanese\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.albanese.codim1\",\n      \"title\": \"Extend rational maps across codimension one\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Extend rational maps across codimension one. SORRY-FREE (run 0069, commit 8a5dc2a66).\\n\\nMilne Lemma 3.3 (indeterminacy_pure_codim_one_into_grpScheme, Albanese/Milne33.lean) is proved and axiom-clean, so Z(f) = empty for group-variety targets and extend_to_av (Milne Theorem 3.2) is unconditional. Albanese/CodimOneExtension.lean carries no sorry.\\n\\nIt lives DOWNSTREAM of CodimOneExtension.lean rather than in it: the difference-map / pole-purity / Hauptidealsatz-transport layers (Albanese/Milne33{Rows,Diagonal,RowSection,Pullback,CMEquidim,KernelGen,Transport,TransportLocal}.lean) import that file, so stating the keystone there is an import cycle. Ported sorry-free from the sibling Rebuild tree, which had developed the chain on the identical toolchain and mathlib pin; every algebra prerequisite already existed in AJC. Route and both implementation notes are on hgraph node ca0776c343e5.\\n\\nCaveat on the axiom claim: extend_to_av is unconditional GIVEN an abelian variety. A fresh-context review found no axiom-clean inhabitant of the AV instance package in this development today (a synthesis site at A := Jacobian C reports sorryAx, via the Picard seam upstream). That is not a defect in this leg, but the two claims are different.\\n\\nRE-MEASURED run 0069 r7, because the ajc-albanese task brief handed to that session listed five\\nsorry line numbers in CodimOneExtension.lean (:216, :218, :752, :1402, :1751) and three in\\nRigidityLemma.lean (:481, :673, :764), and flagged Milne 3.3 as the highest-leverage OPEN node.\\nAll of that is stale: those line numbers land in DOCSTRING PROSE, both files carry zero code\\nsorries, and #print axioms on the lock-free scratch root gives\\n[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] for every one of\\n\\n  Scheme.RationalMap.CodimOneFree, Scheme.gammaSpecField_ringEquiv,\\n  Scheme.localRing_dvr_of_codim_one, Scheme.RationalMap.indeterminacy_pure_codim_one_into_grpScheme,\\n  Scheme.RationalMap.extend_to_av, rigidity_core.\\n\\nSo this row's `done` is correct and the brief is what needs fixing (recorded as inbox I-0732).\\nThe caveat above about the AV instance package still stands unchanged -- it is about inhabiting\\nthe abelian-variety hypotheses at A := Jacobian C, which is the Picard seam, not this leg.\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.albanese\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.albanese\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"8a5dc2a66\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.albanese.rationalmaps\",\n      \"title\": \"Rational-map substrate\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Sorry-free. Rational maps to a scheme through the function field, precomposition and products, the difference map of a rational map to a group scheme, the Milne III.3.3 substeps, and the Theorem 3.2 rational-map extension. Modules: Albanese/RationalMapFunctionField, Albanese/RationalMapPrecomp, Albanese/RationalMapProd, Albanese/DifferenceMap, Albanese/Milne33Substeps, Albanese/Thm32RationalMapExtension.\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.albanese\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.albanese\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.albanese.symmetric\",\n      \"title\": \"Abel-Jacobi and symmetric-power factorisation\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Abel-Jacobi and symmetric-power factorisation. Milne's argument over the symmetric power\\nis PROVED (Albanese/AlbaneseFromData.lean, axiom-clean); the residue is the OBJECT\\nSym^g C, equivalently the single instance HasColimit (permDiagram C g)\\n(SymPowColimit.hasColimit_permDiagram_iff -- an equivalence, so the reduction is lossless).\\n\\nRoute: explicit Scheme.GlueData from affine charts. The bill is four items. As of run 0069 r7:\\n3 SUPPLIED, 1 OPEN. The authoritative count lives in StableAffineCoverGroup.lean's header --\\nthis row is a pointer to it, not a second source of truth (a review found the two disagreeing).\\nRead the change from r6's \\\"2 supplied, 1 partial, 1 open\\\" as item 3 completing, NOT as\\nvindicating an older row that said \\\"3 of 4\\\" for a different and wrong reason.\\n\\n 1. DONE. G-stable affine open neighbourhoods for a finite group acting by automorphisms\\n    (Albanese/StableAffineCoverGroup.lean) plus exists_stable_affineOpen_perm{,_over}.\\n 2. DONE. The Aut-valued S_n-action MonObj.permAutHom (Albanese/GrpObjFoldSum.lean).\\n 3. DONE (r7). Algebra level: TensorPowerCoproduct.lean (existsUnique_coprodLift,\\n    coprodLift_permAlgHom, permAlgHom_comp_singleAlgHom). The Cofan/IsColimit packaging that\\n    was the missing half: TensorPowerCofan.lean (tensorPowerCofanIsColimit, plus\\n    tensorPowerFanIsLimit for the (Under k)-op variance and tensorPowerCofan_inj_permAlgHom\\n    for equivariance on the coprojections). The one trap, measured: CommRingCat.toAlgHom is\\n    typed over the algebra instance REBUILT from the structure morphism, not the ambient one,\\n    so it does not unify -- algHomOfMkUnderHom is the version over the ambient instance\\n    (proof: Under.w plus a congrArg; both round trips rfl).\\n 4. OPEN, and genuinely geometric: the overlap/cocycle agreement of the chart quotients, and\\n    OrbitsInAffineOpen FOR THE CURVE -- where quasi-projectivity enters and mathlib has no\\n    such vocabulary at this pin. THIS IS THE WHOLE REMAINING RESIDUE of the affine-and-glue\\n    route.\\n\\nBEYOND THE BILL, r7 also named the affine carrier, which three files had recorded as expected\\nbut unproved:\\n * SymPowAffineCarrier.tensorPowerOpIsoPiObj -- the n-fold product in (Under k)-op that\\n   permDiagram is BUILT ON is op (mkUnder k (tensor power)), i.e. (Spec_k A)^n = Spec_k A^{\\u2297n},\\n   with permAut_eq_op_permAlgHom matching the actions (and it carries e-inverse; the kernel\\n   forced that -- the wrong variance leaves a goal true only at an involution).\\n * SymPowAffineQuotient.colimitPermDiagramIsoFixed -- the QUOTIENT:\\n   colimit (permDiagram (op (mkUnder k A)) n) is iso to op (fixedUnder ... (tensor power)),\\n   Milne III.3 Prop 3.1's affine half with the object identified. SymPowColimit \\u00a75's bold\\n   caveat \\\"the carrier is not named in Lean\\\" is discharged and deleted.\\n\\nTWO HONEST LIMITS ON THAT, both measured this round rather than assumed:\\n (a) The accompanying HasColimit (permDiagram (op (mkUnder k A)) n) is NOT a new fact --\\n     infer_instance discharges it from cocompleteness. Only the ISO is new. An earlier draft\\n     offered an existence restatement as the payoff; it was vacuous, because naming an object\\n     needs a statement that MENTIONS the object.\\n (b) The SECOND bridge of Milne's affine half -- that (Under k)-op IS the category of affine\\n     k-schemes, via Over.opEquivOpUnder and AffineScheme.equivCommRingCat -- is still unbuilt.\\n     So all of the above is k-ALGEBRA language, not Spec-language, and symPowData_affineAlgebra\\n     was not rewritten to consume the named carrier.\\n\\nCONSUMPTION, checked by grep not asserted: SymPowAffineCarrier.lean consumes the Cofan layer in\\nproof bodies (:138, :150, :184) and SymPowAffineQuotient consumes that -- the first consumer of\\nanything this lane has built in five rounds. But AlbaneseUP / AlbaneseFromData /\\nAlbaneseFromColimit mention NONE of these names (zero hits). This is a consumer inside the\\naffine story, not integration with the capstone; item 4 is what stands between.\\n\\nAlbaneseUP.lean's six sorries are UNCHANGED and albanese_universal_property still reports\\nsorryAx. All six are stated against the sorry-BODIED SymmetricPower, so they remain\\nundischargeable as stated rather than merely unproved.\\n\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.albanese\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.albanese\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"1fedb22e4\",\n        \"f7391b281\",\n        \"a1dd46a99\",\n        \"21eefaf60\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.albanese.universal\",\n      \"title\": \"Albanese universal property\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Albanese universal property. THE ARGUMENT IS PROVED (run 0069); what remains is one precisely-named typeclass instance, not \\\"one missing object\\\" in general.\\n\\nMILNE III.6.1 IS PROVED, both connector directions, over the symmetric power taken as an interface rather than a sorry -- Albanese/AlbaneseFromData.lean and Albanese/AlbaneseJacobian.lean, sorry-free. Forward (symAVMap_eq_of_albanese_eq) needs psi to be a HOMOMORPHISM: pushing psi through the g-fold sum is map_prod (IsMonHom.monoidHom), exactly where Milne's step 5 uses homomorphy. Backward (albanese_eq_of_symAVMap_eq) needs neither that nor the quotient universal property -- it is restriction along Q |-> (Q,P0,...,P0) plus the collapse basePointShift_comp_powSum.\\n\\nTHE RESIDUE IS NOW PRECISE (Albanese/AlbaneseFromColimit.lean, corrected 2026-07-28 commit af3d7b6a2 after an earlier draft got the binder wrong): exists_unique_albanese_of_scheme_colimits takes no SymPowData argument and no hproj argument -- the symmetric power is symPowOfColimit C g and its symmetry is colimit.w, free at every n. The single remaining typeclass hypothesis is HasColimit (permDiagram C g): ONE diagram, for THIS curve and THIS g, in Over (Spec kbar). It is NOT HasColimitsOfShape (SingleObj (Equiv.Perm (Fin g))) Scheme -- that shape-quantified form is strictly stronger, is not what hasColimit_permDiagram_iff covers, and is believed FALSE at this pin (schemes have no coequalizers in general); a theorem carrying it would be vacuous. See AJC.albanese.symmetric for the state of discharging that instance. UPDATED run 0069 r7: this row previously said \\\"TWO residues now, in order: the Cofan/IsColimit packaging in (Under k)-op ... and then the gluing\\\". The FIRST is closed (Albanese/TensorPowerCofan.lean), so there is ONE residue left and it is the geometric wall: the gluing/cocycle compatibility of the chart quotients plus OrbitsInAffineOpen for the curve, where quasi-projectivity enters and mathlib has no such vocabulary at this pin. r7 also named the affine carrier at both ends (SymPowAffineCarrier.tensorPowerOpIsoPiObj for the input, SymPowAffineQuotient.colimitPermDiagramIsoFixed for the quotient = Milne III.3 Prop 3.1's affine half with the object identified), which discharged SymPowColimit \\u00a75's \\\"carrier is not named in Lean\\\" caveat. NONE of that shortens the curve residue: the affine chain is stated over mkUnder k A in (Under k)-op, and C is a proper curve in Over (Spec kbar). Do not read \\\"3 of 4 items supplied\\\" as \\\"3/4 of the way to Sym^g C\\\" -- item 4 is the whole of the geometry.\\n\\nTHE MEASUREMENT, which attributes the residual sorry rather than asserting whose it is:\\n    #print axioms exists_unique_albanese_of_scheme_colimits -> [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]  AXIOM-CLEAN\\n    #print axioms Pic0.albanese_universal_property_of_symPowData    -> [propext, sorryAx, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\\nSame statement; the sole difference is whether the target group object is Pic0.jacobianScheme C or an arbitrary abelian variety. So the entire sorryAx residue of the Pic0 form is the PICARD REPRESENTABILITY SEAM upstream of this leg, and none of it is Milne's argument.\\n\\nDISCHARGED UNCONDITIONALLY (Albanese/AVSelfProduct.lean, on the project's four-instance abelian-variety package): commutativity of an abelian variety (Milne I.1.4) and pointed rigidity (Milne I.1.2). The obstruction had been instance KEYING through the monoidal notation, not missing mathematics.\\n\\nREMAINING INPUTS: (1) HasColimit (permDiagram C g) -- see AJC.albanese.symmetric; (2) Milne III.5.1(a) birationality as a SECTION of f^(g) over a dense open. The descent around them is closed: extend_to_av (Milne Thm 3.2) is unconditional and axiom-clean, and exists_unique_descent_of_section / hom_ext_of_dense_open package it in elementary terms with no rational map in the statement.\\n\\nNOT A CLOSED RESULT ABOUT THE JACOBIAN, and the module headers say so in those words. The pinned Pic0.albanese_universal_property still reports sorryAx and its six sorries in AlbaneseUP.lean are UNCHANGED -- they are stated against a sorry-BODIED SymmetricPower and are undischargeable as stated, which the AlbaneseUP.lean header now records along with a pointer to where the mathematics lives.\\n\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.albanese\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.albanese\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"af3d7b6a2\",\n        \"7b71f602f\",\n        \"a88231902\",\n        \"2e58d6cd1\",\n        \"21eefaf60\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.cohomology\",\n      \"title\": \"Cohomology and flat base change\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"The Cech comparison engine is complete and sorry-free (AJC.cech), and tilde-exactness is done (AJC.cohomology.tilde-exact, run 0068). AJC.fbc is the only open child.\\n\\nCORRECTED (run 0068 r2 janitor pass): the previous summary said \\\"flat base change remains open at flat-pullback exactness and two cosimplicial naturality checks\\\". Both halves now contradict the children.\\n\\n * FLAT-PULLBACK EXACTNESS IS NOT A FRONTIER. AJC.fbc.exactness records pullback_preservesMonomorphisms (arbitrary O_S-modules) as a deliberate MONUMENT: bypassed on quasi-coherent objects by pullback_preservesKernel_of_isQuasicoherent, de-instanced so it no longer leaks through synthesis, and now also off the hypothesis list. Its own summary says the arbitrary-module statement should NOT be attempted, and its status is pending for exactly that reason.\\n\\n * ONLY ONE OF THE TWO COSIMPLICIAL LEAVES IS A NATURALITY CHECK. AJC.fbc.cosimplicial.pushforward's naturality obligation was removed by the whiskered-mate construction, leaving one IsIso per index tuple; AJC.fbc.cosimplicial.twisted is a comparison of two nerves and is the harder leaf.\\n\\nENDPOINT FORM TO CONSUME: cech_flatBaseChange_qcoh -- the cech_flatBaseChange conclusion with no extra hypotheses and the flat-exactness leaf absent from the proof term.\\n\\nCohomology/CechHigherDirectImageUnconditional.lean carries exactly three sorry terms, in pullback_preservesMonomorphisms (the monument), cech_pushforward_baseChange_natIso, and twisted_cech_nerve_iso. Everything else under this node is sorry-free.\\n\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.jacobian\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.cohomology\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 1,\n      \"subtree_done\": 9,\n      \"subtree_total\": 13\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.cech\",\n      \"title\": \"\\u010cech higher-direct-image engine\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Complete and sorry-free: for a separated quasi-compact morphism with a finite affine cover, \\u010cech cohomology computes higher direct images. The construction is functorial through `pushPull`; the remaining base-change obligations are tracked under `AJC.fbc`.\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.cohomology\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.cohomology\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2,\n      \"subtree_done\": 6,\n      \"subtree_total\": 6\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.cech.acyclic\",\n      \"title\": \"Affine acyclicity and acyclic resolutions\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Sorry-free. Serre vanishing on affines, termwise acyclicity of the Cech complex, the generic exact-augmentation lemmas that compute cohomology from an acyclic resolution, and the augmented Cech resolution. Modules: Cohomology/AffineSerreVanishing, Cohomology/CechAcyclic, Cohomology/CechTermAcyclic, Cohomology/AcyclicResolution, Cohomology/CechAugmentedResolution.\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.cech\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.cohomology\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.cech.engine\",\n      \"title\": \"Combinatorial and section Cech complexes\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Sorry-free. The alternating coface complex of a presheaf, its free resolution, the section Cech complex of a finite affine cover, the contracting homotopy in degree zero, positive degree, and the isolated degree-one identity, and coboundary splitting. Modules: Cohomology/PresheafCech, Cohomology/FreePresheafComplex, Cohomology/CechSectionComplex, Cohomology/CechSectionContractibility, Cohomology/CechSectionContractibilityCore, Cohomology/CechSectionContractibilityOne, Cohomology/CechSectionContractibilitySucc, Cohomology/CechCoboundarySplitting.\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.cech\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.cohomology\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.cech.identification\",\n      \"title\": \"Section-complex identification\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Sorry-free. Identification of the section Cech complex with the evaluated complex, through the base, leg, and top comparison stages and the augmentation comparison. Modules: Cohomology/CechSectionIdentification, Cohomology/CechSectionIdentificationBase, Cohomology/CechSectionIdentificationLeg, Cohomology/CechSectionIdentificationLegAux, Cohomology/CechSectionIdentificationLegMid1, Cohomology/CechSectionIdentificationLegMid2, Cohomology/CechSectionIdentificationLegTop, Cohomology/CechSectionAugmentationComparison.\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.cech\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.cohomology\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.cech.main\",\n      \"title\": \"cech_computes_higherDirectImage\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Sorry-free and unconditional (no enough-injectives appeal). For a separated quasi-compact morphism, a quasi-coherent sheaf, and a finite affine open cover, the cohomology of the relative Cech complex computes R^i f_*. Modules: Cohomology/AbsoluteCohomology, Cohomology/CechToCohomology, Cohomology/CechBridge, Cohomology/CechToHigherDirectImage.\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.cech\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.cohomology\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.cech.mayervietoris\",\n      \"title\": \"Mayer--Vietoris for a two-element cover\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Sorry-free. The Mayer--Vietoris sequence in the (0,1) slice for a two-element affine cover, and its cover-level packaging. Modules: Cohomology/MayerVietorisCore, Cohomology/MayerVietorisCover.\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.cech\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.cohomology\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.cech.pushpull\",\n      \"title\": \"Higher direct images and pushPull functoriality\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Sorry-free. Higher direct images as derived pushforward, their presheaf model, the relative Cech complex of a cover and its pushPull functoriality (composition, leg coherence, pentagon), acyclicity of pushforward along an affine morphism, the essential image of affine pushPull, and pushforward along an open immersion. Modules: Cohomology/HigherDirectImage, Cohomology/HigherDirectImagePresheaf, Cohomology/CechHigherDirectImage, Cohomology/AffinePushPullEssImage, Cohomology/OpenImmersionPushforward.\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.cech\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.cohomology\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.cohomology.tilde-exact\",\n      \"title\": \"Exactness of the tilde functor (Stacks 01HV)\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Exactness of the tilde functor (Stacks 01HV), blueprint lem:tilde_preserves_kernels. DONE, sorry-free, kernel-verified (run 0068). Cohomology/TildeExactness.lean is now entirely sorry-free -- this was that file's long-open named target, with a header section literally titled \\\"Why tildePreservesFiniteLimits itself is NOT closed here\\\".\\n\\nLANDED: tilde_preservesMonomorphisms, tildePreservesFiniteLimits, tilde_preservesHomology, plus the supporting sectMap / sectMap_eq / tilde_injective_app_basicOpen.\\n\\nROUTE -- basic opens, not stalks. Basic opens are a basis of Spec R, and mathlib ALREADY exhibits Gamma(M~, D(r)) as a localisation of M at the powers of r (tilde.toOpen carries an IsLocalizedModule.Away instance). So the section map of ~f over D(r) IS IsLocalizedModule.map of f (by IsLocalizedModule.ext against the naturality square tilde.toOpen_map_app), injective by IsLocalizedModule.map_injective since localisation is flat. Basis injectivity gives stalkwise injectivity hence mono; right exactness is free (left adjoint); right exact + mono-preserving => left exact.\\n\\nWHY IT IS WORTH RECORDING AS A LESSON, not just a result. The file's own header prescribed a DIFFERENT route and estimated 100-150 LOC for it: R-linearity of the Ab STALK map, then a jointly-reflecting stalk family through JointlyReflectIsomorphisms.jointlyReflectsLimit, with a long warning that the ModuleCat-valued stalk path is dead because mathlib keeps toStalk_l / stalkIso_l / stalkToLocalization_l private. NONE of that is needed on the basic-open route: the injectivity check happens BEFORE any stalk is formed, so no stalk colimit and no jointly-reflecting step enters, and the R-linearity that matters is on SECTIONS where Scheme.Modules.Hom.app_smul supplies it in one line. A carefully-written plan in a docstring is evidence about ONE route, not about the difficulty of the statement. The header has been corrected in place; the section-1 stalk material is retained as the sharpest per-point statement.\\n\\nCONSUMES: nothing open. FEEDS: the affine-morphism ingredient of AJC.fbc.exactness (tildePullback_preservesFiniteLimits), and any consumer that wanted \\\"qcoh kernels are qcoh\\\".\\n\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.cohomology\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.cohomology\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"fcc4e9591\",\n        \"36f623f46\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.fbc\",\n      \"title\": \"Flat base change (1 walled naturality leaf + 1 bypassed monument)\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Flat base change for higher direct images along a flat g. ONE open obligation, and as of run 0068 r6\\nit is a PULLBACK-PSEUDOFUNCTOR COHERENCE identity, not a Beck-Chevalley mate statement.\\n\\nSTATE. The global scaffolding (Cohomology/FlatBaseChange, FlatBaseChangeGlobal), the affine termwise\\ncomparison, and the S-level cosimplicial half are sorry-free. AJC.fbc.cosimplicial.pushforward closed\\nat r3 (cech_pushforward_baseChange_natIso_flat). Cohomology/CechHigherDirectImageUnconditional.lean\\ncarries 3 sorries: :2743 and :2919 are the twisted-nerve chain, and :924\\n(pullback_preservesMonomorphisms for ARBITRARY O_S-modules) is WALLED AND OFF THE CRITICAL PATH --\\nsee AJC.fbc.exactness; every consumer instantiates at quasi-coherent objects where it is proved.\\n\\nTHE REMAINING OBLIGATION, in one name: BcSquareCoherence (twisted row for the full chain). Both\\nBeck-Chevalley mates in half (a) of the twisted square have been ELIMINATED -- not related across\\nsquares, which is what four rounds recorded as impossible here and in mathlib, but removed, by\\nputting each under its left adjoint and past its counit. Measured: the residual goal contains ZERO\\noccurrences of openImmersion_bareBC, bcv or mateEquiv.\\n\\nWHY THAT CHANGES THE PRICING. The old frontier needed infrastructure that does not exist (nothing\\nrelates a mate across a change of square). BcSquareCoherence needs only what mathlib and this file\\nalready have: pseudofunctor_associativity / _left_unitality / _right_unitality, pullbackCongr, and\\nnaturality of the ppTel telescope. It is a real identity and not free, but it is in-vocabulary.\\n\\nNOT DONE, and no endpoint moved: cech_flatBaseChange_oneLeaf and twisted_cech_nerve_iso still report\\nsorryAx (they are the controls in the axiom probe). Nothing previously contaminated became clean in\\nr5 or r6.\\n\\nCAVEAT: r5 and r6 have had NO independent review -- 4/4 review subagent dispatches stalled (I-0797).\\nVerification is kernel EXIT=0 (3243 jobs), axiom probes against firing controls, and probes that\\napply each new brick