ve compatibility\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Twisted Cech nerve compatibility. BOTH MATES ARE ELIMINABLE (proved, landed); the REDUCTION that\\nuses them is verified step-by-step but NOT AFFORDABLE as one declaration (run 0068 r6).\\n\\nTHE MATHEMATICAL ADVANCE, and it is real. r4/r5 recorded the frontier as \\\"nothing in the tree or in\\nmathlib relates the Beck-Chevalley mate across a change of square\\\", and priced the leaf on that.\\nCorrect diagnosis, wrong conclusion: a mate need not be RELATED across squares if it can be REMOVED.\\nr5 removed one side (mateEquiv_counit) and recorded honestly that the other was blocked by\\npushPullMap (wmap ...) sitting between mate and counit. r6's fix: THAT MAP IS ITSELF BUILT FROM A\\nUNIT, so the same move kills it.\\n\\nLANDED AND KERNEL-VERIFIED, all axiom-clean, sorry count UNCHANGED at 3 (commits 1509f3683,\\n79e2cea0b, 65036074f):\\n * counit_comp_decomp -- counit of (a >> p1) via pullbackComp-inv and the two single counits.\\n * rawPushPullMap_pullback_counit_self / _counit -- under p^* past the counit, the restriction map's\\n   UNIT dies by the left triangle. General over-triangle version is the one that reaches the\\n   consumer: wmap's triangle is a GENUINE EQUATION, not rfl (measured).\\n * bcv_hom_eq (rfl) + bcv_pullback_counit -- bcv's adjunct in CLOSED MATE-FREE form.\\n\\nTHE REDUCTION, and its honest status. bcSquareCounitSide_of_coherence reduces half (a) to\\nBcSquareCoherence, whose residue I MEASURED to contain ZERO occurrences of openImmersion_bareBC,\\nbcv or mateEquiv -- only pullbackComp/pullbackCongr/ppTel/telescope, two counits of OPEN INCLUSIONS,\\nand pushPullMap (interLegHom). Every step was machine-checked individually. BUT: as a single\\ndeclaration it burned 43 min CPU / 13 GB RSS inside CechHigherDirectImageUnconditional (a module\\nthat builds in 156-248s), and 13 min / 5.6 GB and climbing even from a separate module. So it is\\nCOMMENTED OUT in Cohomology/CechTwistedCoherenceReduction.lean, with the statements\\n(bcAdjFree, BcSquareCoherence) live and the cost note in the file. A proof nobody has seen the\\nkernel accept is not a proof, and a sorry there would have hidden that the blocker is COST, not\\nmathematics. Cause and the likely structural fix (name the intermediate composites so the erws match\\nsyntactically instead of via whnf through two asIso-wrapped IsIso instances): inbox I-0798.\\n\\nNEXT: restructure that proof, do not just raise heartbeats.\\n\\nCAVEAT: r5 and r6 have had NO independent review -- 4/4 review subagent dispatches stalled (I-0797).\\n\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.fbc.cosimplicial\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.cohomology\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 4\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.fbc.exactness\",\n      \"title\": \"Flat pullback preserves finite limits (bypassed on quasi-coherent objects; arbitrary-module case open)\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Flat pullback preserves finite limits. NOT ON THE CRITICAL PATH, and the \\\"instance leak\\\" that made\\nit the task brief's stated priority NO LONGER EXISTS (re-measured run 0068 r5).\\n\\nTHE BRIEF'S FRAMING IS STALE, and this row is where a fresh session will act on it, so it is\\ncorrected here (full measurement in I-0756):\\n * \\\"pullback_preservesFiniteLimits is one of only two sorry-bodied INSTANCES leaking through\\n   typeclass synthesis\\\" -- it is NOT an instance. This lane demoted it at r1 for exactly that leak\\n   reason; the file says so at its header. And the project now has ZERO sorry-bodied instances\\n   (grep for `instance ... := sorry` returns nothing). There is no leak to close, and no\\n   contaminated declaration for closing it to clean.\\n * r2 separately measured that discharging it would clean only the two probes that name it.\\n\\nWHY NOTHING NEEDS IT. Flat left-exactness was being demanded at the strongest generality that makes\\nthe sentence true, while every consumer instantiates it at QUASI-COHERENT objects, where it is\\nPROVED sorry-free by pullback_preservesKernel_of_isQuasicoherent (cone-cancellation off the\\ntilde-image exactness, plus fullness of tilde). And the homology comparison the Cech proof consumes\\nneeds only ONE KERNEL PER DEGREE (mapHomologicalComplexHomologyIso_of_preservesKernel), not global\\nexactness -- so pullback_mapHC_homologyIso_of_isQuasicoherent is an axiom-clean replacement.\\nMeasured: the leakProbe_qcohRoute_* lines are clean while leakControl_qcohRoute_oldRoute (same\\nconclusion, old route) still reports sorryAx.\\n\\nWHAT REMAINS OPEN, honestly: pullback_preservesMonomorphisms for ARBITRARY O_S-modules, walled --\\nmathlib gives SheafOfModules.pullback no pointwise model, and the sibling project\\nMR0555258-Compactifying-Picard independently reduced j_! to the same missing brick. It should not be\\nattempted from this row; the quasi-coherent route bypasses it entirely.\\n\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.fbc\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.cohomology\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"672a8c656\",\n        \"325b4d0e8\",\n        \"93cdfb5e5\",\n        \"c6533164c\",\n        \"8a6e5ef61\",\n        \"1573874b6\",\n        \"df899aa50\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.jacobian.assembly\",\n      \"title\": \"Package the final Jacobian witness\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Construct picardJacobianWitness from Picard representability, the Pic0 abelian-variety structure, dimension g, and the Albanese universal property; discharge the protected Jacobian interface.\\n\\nThe structure is built and wired: the witness IS Scheme.Pic0SchemeEt, the identity component of the scheme representing the etale-sheafified relative Picard functor. What remains is mathematics, not assembly, so THIS ITEM STAYS OPEN WITH ITS ONLY CHILD DONE -- that status mismatch is deliberate and must not be \\\"fixed\\\". The parent is the assembly step, not a container, and it rests on five open obligations.\\n\\nTHE FIVE OBLIGATIONS, restated after the owner decision of 2026-07-28 (protection I-0491, branch (2) ETALE-SHEAFIFY): none of them is a false statement any more, which is the substance of that change rather than the count.\\n\\n- Scheme.fgaPicardRepresentability -- representability of the etale-sheafified functor over an ARBITRARY field, with no rational-point binder. The project's central open obligation, expected to stay open.\\n- Scheme.Pic0Et.geometricallyReduced -- Cartier in characteristic zero, a genuine statement in characteristic p.\\n- Scheme.Pic0Et.universallyClosed -- Kleiman section 5.\\n- smoothOfRelativeDimension_genus_pic0Et and isAlbanese_pic0Et -- the two leaves stated at the headline.\\n\\nNote the middle two rather than Pic0Et.smooth / Pic0Et.proper: those are ASSEMBLIES over them, not obligations of their own, so citing them as the open statements is a stale reading. An earlier version of this summary did exactly that, and also listed a \\\"leaf A (rational point)\\\"; hasRationalPoint_of_curve was FALSE as stated and has been deleted, never proved (I-0491 clause 1).\\n\\nDISTANCES TO THE LANDED TREE, measured with scripts/axiom-frontier.lean rather than asserted, and unequal:\\n\\n- LEAF C (Albanese) is the closest. isAlbanese_pic0_of_isAlgClosed is a THEOREM: over an algebraically closed field, in positive genus, and given the basepoint condition, the universal property is Albanese.Pic0.albanese_universal_property applied with no transport. So leaf C adds exactly three things -- arbitrary base field (cluster G descent), genus zero (Mumford rigidity), and the basepoint condition P o iota_P = eta. The third is easily overlooked: it is a conjunct of IsAlbanese that the landed theorem never states, and it cannot be discharged before Pic0.abelJacobi is constructed, since it is a statement about that morphism.\\n- LEAF B (dimension refinement) has its landed half at the headline too, and it is NOT the dimension count. finrank_tangentSpace_pic0_eq_genus proves dim T_e Pic0 = genus C via Pic0.finrank_cotangentSpace_eq_finrank_hModuleOne with no transport, since genus C is definitionally dim_k H^1(C,O_C). So leaf B owes a TRANSLATION between two invariants of smoothness, plus the transport of that landed chain from Pic0Scheme to Pic0SchemeEt (the honest extra cost of the etale formulation). On the translation: mathlib's SmoothOfRelativeDimension mentions no tangent space, but it is not bridge-free -- Algebra.IsStandardSmoothOfRelativeDimension.iff_of_isStandardSmooth characterises relative dimension n as Module.rank S Omega[S/R] = n, an iff -- so the work is the duality over a field between rank Omega and the tangent-space dimension, plus the affine-local-to-scheme-level passage over a cover of Pic0. An earlier summary called this missing mathematics with no bridge; that was retracted (memory I-0446).\\n\\nPic0Et.geometricallyReduced and Pic0Et.universallyClosed belong to no current task and are the nearest unowned work under the headline.\\n\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.jacobian\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.jacobian.assembly\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 1,\n      \"subtree_done\": 1,\n      \"subtree_total\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.jacobian.assembly.picrep-input\",\n      \"title\": \"The representability input to the witness: fgaPicardRepresentability\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"OPEN, and it is the reason AJC.jacobian.assembly is not done. The Jacobian witness needs Scheme.fgaPicardRepresentability (Picard/FGAPicRepresentability.lean, a bare sorry) \\u2014 representability of the etale-sheafified relative Picard functor over an arbitrary field, plus the Kleiman section 2 Thm 2.5 comparison under a rational point.\\n\\nANCHOR DE-LINED 2026-07-30 (review-ajc r7). This row said \\\"\\u2026lean:347\\\". At HEAD line 347 is mid-docstring; the theorem head is 757 and the sorry 765, and both will move again \\u2014 the file is 1584 lines and several lanes edit it hourly. Cite the DECLARATION NAME, which one grep -n resolves and no docstring insertion invalidates. Do NOT \\\"refresh\\\" this back into a line number: that is the failure AJC.picrep has now filed four times, and it had reproduced itself at three fresh numbers (347, 371, 377) across four AJC rows by the time I re-read them.\\n\\nADDED 2026-07-29 by review-ajc to resolve a standing consistency warning HONESTLY. The parent had every child done while itself open; the parent's own summary said that mismatch was deliberate because 'what remains is mathematics, not assembly'. That is true but it made the board warn on every command, which trains readers to scroll past warnings. The mismatch is now representable: this row IS the remaining mathematics, so the parent is open because a child is open.\\n\\nNot claimable as a round target \\u2014 see AJC.picrep for the ten absent campaign modules between the landed tree and this sorry. Its route (Grassmannian for Div^d, finite Galois for the quotient, NOT Quot) is recorded on AJC.picrep and on hgraph node thm:fga_pic_representability. The three other headline leaves (Pic0Et.geometricallyReduced, Pic0Et.universallyClosed, and the two stated at the headline) are tracked by the parent's summary, not here.\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.jacobian.assembly\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.jacobian.assembly\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.jacobian.reachability\",\n      \"title\": \"Wire the headline to the infrastructure\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"The headline rests on the infrastructure it claims, and every number here is measured rather than asserted. picardJacobianWitness is built from Scheme.Pic0Scheme, so 98 of the project's modules are reachable from Jacobian.lean rather than the 8 of the Genus-only import; the 98th arrived when leaf C was stated against the landed Albanese universal property, which put the Albanese cone under the headline for the first time.\\n\\nEVERY MODULE ON DISK IS ROOTED at AlgebraicJacobian.lean -- 187 of 187 as of 2026-07-28, no exceptions. ONE CONVENTION FOR THE DENOMINATOR, since the two figures in this node count differently and Ground flagged it: 187 is the number of .lean files UNDER AlgebraicJacobian/, excluding the root aggregator AlgebraicJacobian.lean itself, which is the seed rather than a member. Both '187 of 187 rooted' and '98 of 187 reachable from the headline' use that same 187, so they are comparable; the tree contains 188 files if you count the root. which matters because an unrooted module compiles green and is invisible BOTH to the root build and to the axiom probe: #print axioms on its declarations cannot even be written against the root import. The standing check is in the probe header and in I-0388. A module not yet committed to the ledger must NOT be rooted (a clean checkout would fail); that grace period ends at the commit.\\n\\nTHE OBLIGATION COUNT IS FIVE, over a general base field AND over an algebraically closed one. The count does not drop when leaf A is discharged; only the KIND of the obligations changes. The five: instHasPicScheme, Pic0.smooth and Pic0.proper (sorry-bodied upstream), and leaves B and C stated at the headline -- with leaf A a sixth over a general field, where it is the FALSE one. Each leaf's distance to the landed tree is COMPILER-CHECKED rather than described, by a companion theorem stated at the headline:\\n\\n  leaf A (rational point) -- FALSE over a general k, so it must be REPLACED, not proved. Over an algebraically closed field it is a THEOREM: hasRationalPoint_of_curve_of_isAlgClosed is axiom-clean via Albanese.hasRationalPoint_of_isAlgClosed, and picardJacobianWitnessOfIsAlgClosed assembles the witness with it supplied rather than assumed. This bounds I-0372's decision without choosing a branch: what is undecided is what the project claims over an ARBITRARY base field.\\n  instHasPicScheme (representability) -- the obligation that is easy to miscount. Scheme.Pic0Scheme carries [HasPicScheme C] and this sorry-bodied instance is its sole producer. Over a general field the gate is reached THROUGH leaf A, so counting it separately looks like double-counting; discharging leaf A makes it FIRE rather than removing it, so over k-bar it stands free.\\n  leaf B -- owes Pic0.smooth plus the passage from a tangent-space dimension to Mathlib's presentation-based SmoothOfRelativeDimension; the dimension count itself is landed (finrank_tangentSpace_pic0_eq_genus proves dim T_e Pic0 = genus C with no transport).\\n  leaf C -- one basepoint condition plus two generalizations away (isAlbanese_pic0_of_isAlgClosed proves the algebraically closed positive-genus case).\\n\\nWHY THE KIND OF OBLIGATION MATTERS AND CANNOT BE READ OFF THE PROBE: over k-bar all five are unproved TRUE statements; leaf A over a general field is FALSE, so the general witness rests on an inconsistent hypothesis and its consequences are vacuously true. Both states report exactly the same sorryAx, so the distinction has to be exhibited by a discharge rather than measured. That is why the alg-closed witness is a separate definition.\\n\\nRETRACTED (2026-07-28, caught by Ground and reproduced independently): an earlier revision of this summary said the alg-closed witness rests on FOUR obligations, and a later revision retracted that in a trailing paragraph while leaving the FOUR standing in its own opening -- so the node contradicted itself for one round. Both are now corrected to five. Trap (a) landed on the very declaration whose docstring warns about trap (c). MEASURED as probe section 0b: naming Pic0Scheme with leaf A discharged and nothing else in the term still reports sorryAx, against a gate-assumed control that is clean. The claim that survives is unchanged and was always the valuable one: over k-bar all five remaining obligations are TRUE statements.\\n\\nAND NOTE WHAT THIS DOES NOT MOVE: picardJacobianWitnessOfIsAlgClosed has ZERO Lean consumers. The five protected declarations still route Jacobian -> jacobianWitness -> nonempty_jacobianWitness -> picardJacobianWitness -> hasRationalPoint_of_curve, i.e. through the false leaf. Nothing about the protected surface has changed.\\n\\nREPRODUCIBLE and independently re-measured 2026-07-28 THROUGH THE ROOT PATH with lake build AlgebraicJacobian green at 8746 jobs: scripts/axiom-frontier.lean, 126 declarations, 84 clean and 42 carrying sorryAx (125/84/41 before section 0c added the branch-(1) assembly; 113/72/41 before section 6f added ajc-rr's unconditional-chi lines, all clean; 107/70/37 before that). Note how the last two additions moved the sorryAx count in OPPOSITE directions, for the right reasons: section 6f added declarations and left it at 41, because an all-clean lane adds nothing to the frontier and a clean line is therefore not by itself headline progress; section 0c added one and moved it to 42, because the branch-(1) assembly leaks on the five obligations behind it. Neither movement changed the mathematics -- the frontier is the same five obligations throughout. 26 sorry carriers over 11 modules, matching the enumeration published in the probe's section 2 exactly -- of those 26, exactly TWO are instances (instHasPicScheme, pullback_preservesFiniteLimits) and therefore the only two reachable without being named; 98 modules reachable from the headline of 187 on disk, zero unrooted. Count by output ENTRY, not by line -- Lean wraps long axiom lists, and the naive per-line filter misclassifies exactly the declarations whose lists are longest. Two earlier revisions of this summary published 24 rather than 26; the build says 26 and the probe carries the regenerating command so the number is checkable rather than asserted.\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.jacobian.assembly\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.jacobian.assembly\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"ad09baf14\",\n        \"b65f25d6a\",\n        \"4905dc11b\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.maintenance\",\n      \"title\": \"Project quality and documentation\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n   