o 22.68s, composition builds independently in 1:37.28, and unit plus naturality consumers complete in 29.76s in parallel; all affected LSP and kernel checks pass.\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"refactor\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.maintenance.build\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.maintenance\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"dda80b2d7\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.maintenance.build.heartbeats\",\n      \"title\": \"Heartbeat and recursion-budget audit\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"The missing-rationale and recursion-depth audit is complete. Thirty-one inherited obsolete heartbeat scopes were removed, seven required sites were measured and documented, and all depth scopes were measured. The current active inventory is 140 maxHeartbeats scopes, 39 synthesis-heartbeat scopes, 15 maxSynthPendingDepth overrides, and 5 maxRecDepth overrides, partitioned under resource-budgets.\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"refactor\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.maintenance.build\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.maintenance\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"db85e701c\",\n        \"00b4c44ed\",\n        \"afbd88600\",\n        \"ce7e4a001\",\n        \"e142308c0\",\n        \"fb29d460b\",\n        \"98353cd99\",\n        \"2e6d3c83e\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.maintenance.build.imports\",\n      \"title\": \"Replace the remaining bare import Mathlib (66 of 172 modules) by precise imports\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"The dominant build cost, and the method is now settled. 86 of 164 modules opened with a bare 'import Mathlib'; measured on Cohomology/SheafCompose.lean (49 lines), 16.6 s and about 7 GB with the umbrella versus 3.5 s and 1.97 GB with four precise imports. Converted modules were observed at 2.5-3.4 GB against 6.8-7.0 GB before, which is the second lever: at 7 GB per process a 62 GB host sustains about 8 concurrent jobs instead of 16, and the from-scratch build's 33-minute serial tail ran with exactly one job.\\n\\nORDERING RULE, learned the expensive way. Bottom-up is right for probe CORRECTNESS -- a module's minimal imports cannot be computed until everything beneath it is clean -- but wrong for NET PROGRESS whenever the module has a cone of import-less dependents above it. Narrowing StructureSheafModuleK/Presheaf.lean stripped the library from nine modules in the StructureSheafModuleK -> Genus -> Jacobian chain. Over wave 2, converting 8 modules forced 25 back onto the umbrella and the count went 39 back up to 64. Give a module's import-less dependents their own precise imports FIRST, top-down within the cone, then narrow the parent.\\n\\nTHE REAL WORK ITEM is the 54 modules that declare no Mathlib import at all and inherit the library transitively. They are invisible to the minimal-import probe because nothing in their own text says what they need, and every one that gets its own imports permanently removes a class of breakage. Elaborating all 54 in parallel with 'lake env lean' (read-only against .lake/build, safe alongside a running build) resolves the whole exposure in minutes; a full build finds only one victim per round because lake stops at the first failure in a chain. Of the 54, exactly 24 needed Mathlib -- the other 30 were loading 1.79 GB of oleans for nothing and are pure wins.\\n\\nSTATE: 64 of 164 bare, down from 86. GrassmannianQuot.lean resists narrowing outright (times out at isDefEq :924 and whnf :1217 at default heartbeats WITH precise imports, builds fine with the umbrella) and stays bare deliberately. scripts/deumbrella-wave.sh now repairs its own cascade per wave and refuses to advance until green.\\n\\nDEFERRED 2026-07-27 (janitor hygiene pass, run 0053) -- status moved active -> pending, and the\\ncampaign is paused, not abandoned. Nothing here is retracted; the ordering rule and the 54-module\\nfinding stay the durable content. Re-measured today: 66 of 172 modules still open with a bare\\n'import Mathlib' (the total rose from 164 because run 0053 added Picard/RigidPushforward* modules).\\nLast wave was 3fbc2cace ('wave 2 lands green -- 8 modules narrowed, 25 restored, net 86 to 64\\nbare'), under run 0046 / task ajc-optimize, which is queued and not running.\\n\\nWHY PENDING RATHER THAN ACTIVE. It had no owner, no live run, and its parent AJC.maintenance is\\nalready active with the same milestone, so it was spending one of the workspace's active slots\\nwhile the three live runs (ajc-gate, ajc-rr, ajc-truth) all work elsewhere. Set it back to active\\nwhen a session actually picks up wave 3 -- and read the ORDERING RULE above before doing so.\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.maintenance.build\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.maintenance\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.maintenance.build.resource-budgets\",\n      \"title\": \"Structural elaboration-budget reduction\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Open. 140 maxHeartbeats, 39 synthInstance.maxHeartbeats, 15 maxSynthPendingDepth and 5 maxRecDepth scopes remain, against ZERO 'set_option maxHeartbeats' in all of Mathlib/ and exactly one synthInstance budget upstream. None of the 179 cites a measured number, and Mathlib's own '#count_heartbeats in' appears nowhere in this project. Closed cones so far: P1ChartData, QcohTildeSections localisation, the five CechTerm adjunction/presentation wrappers and the Cech contraction declarations all elaborate at Lean defaults. STRATEGY: re-measure each remaining scope only AFTER its module leaves the umbrella import -- a narrowed environment changes elaboration cost in both directions, and GrassmannianQuot has already shown it can get slower. Note that trimming a ceiling saves no compute by construction; the value here is honesty about cost, not speed.\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"refactor\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.maintenance.build\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.maintenance\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"5edda3284\",\n        \"885608a29\",\n        \"1396cfbb4\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 3,\n      \"subtree_done\": 0,\n      \"subtree_total\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.maintenance.build.resource-budgets.quot-presentation\",\n      \"title\": \"Quot presentation budgets\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Ten adjacent scopes in QuotScheme presentation descent remain candidates: five 2M command budgets paired with five 800k synthesis budgets. Equivalent pullback wrappers already shed similar scopes, but this target costs about 6:42 and has eleven direct consumers.\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"refactor\"