ectory index already distinguishes this archive from live project state.\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"workspace\",\n      \"priority\": \"low\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.maintenance\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.maintenance\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.pic0av\",\n      \"title\": \"Pic^0 is an abelian variety (A.3)\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Pic^0 is an abelian variety of dimension g (A.3). FIVE open sorries across the leg, on four\\nfronts. Front (d), AJC.rr.principal, is CLOSED -- RiemannRoch/WeilDivisor.lean is sorry-free.\\n\\n (a) TANGENT / H1 (AJC.pic0av.tangent). ONE sorry: Pic0AbelianVariety.lean:853,\\n     semilinearComparison_cotangentSpaceDual_h1Cok. The load-bearing one -- everything else\\n     in this leg that leaks sorryAx leaks it from here and nowhere else, measured. Its own\\n     residue is clause (iii) alone (clauses (i) and (ii) are theorems). Do NOT retry the\\n     AJCR two-chart CechPic port: refuted at the CARRIER, not on cost (I-0689) -- AJCR's only\\n     sheaf-side bridge cechPicEquivPic carries [IsAffine] irremovably and this clause lives on\\n     a proper curve.\\n\\n (b) SMOOTHNESS / PROPERNESS (AJC.pic0av.structure). Two sorries, both fully reduced:\\n     geometricallyReduced (:1135) and universallyClosed (:1373). Properness has exactly ONE\\n     live route, universallyClosed_of_valuativeCriterion -- the ambient route is REFUTED\\n     (universal closedness of Pic_{C/k} would force CompactSpace on an infinite disjoint union\\n     over deg in Z; Picard/AmbientPicNotProper.lean), and the quasi-projectivity route needs\\n     vocabulary mathlib v4.31 does not have (I-0074 Caveat 2).\\n\\n (c) DEGREE / DIMENSION (AJC.pic0av.identity). Two sorries. The degree map is BUILT and\\n     sorry-free. THE DIMENSION HALF'S r7 REDUCTION IS REFUTED (run 0067 r8, 27f526ea7): its\\n     \\\"orbit condition\\\" is not a gap but CONTRADICTORY for g >= 1 -- a k-rational orbit forces\\n     T1 hence topologicalKrullDim 0 (Picard/HomogeneityOrbitCollapse.lean), so both\\n     topologicalKrullDim_eq_genus_of_homogeneous theorems are VACUOUS where this leg exists.\\n     The \\\"uniform cotangent bound\\\" that r7 declared dead is REINSTATED as the owed statement,\\n     and it needs a transport reaching NON-CLOSED points. Fourth wrong framing of this leg.\\n\\nMEASURE AT A SYNTHESIS SITE, not at the declaration: smooth/proper and their reductions\\nquantify over [HasPicScheme C] and report clean axioms as stated. Every clean claim in this\\nleg has been probed against controls that DO fire sorryAx; keep that discipline.\\n\",\n      \"status\": \"active\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.jacobian\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.pic0av\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 1,\n      \"subtree_done\": 0,\n      \"subtree_total\": 6\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.pic0av.albanese-et\",\n      \"title\": \"Headline obligation 5: the Albanese universal property of Pic0SchemeEt over an arbitrary field\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Headline obligation 5: isAlbanese_pic0Et (Jacobian.lean:660, bare sorry) -- the Albanese universal property of Pic0SchemeEt over an ARBITRARY field. ADVANCED in its SUPPLY ROUTE, obligation UNTOUCHED, by ajc-p4 (run 0086 r4). Owner released.\\n\\n*** THE r2 COSTING ON THIS ROW 