 \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Identity component and degree-zero points. Two sorries in Picard/IdentityComponent.lean:\\nfinrank_eq_genus (:1896) and kPoints_iff_kerDegree (:1939). The degree map itself is BUILT\\nand sorry-free (PicScheme.degree :1702, pinned via ClassDegreePinned with a non-vacuity\\ntest), the Pic^0 inclusion is BUILT, and the easy direction of the kernel characterisation\\nis landed (degree_eq_zero_of_class_eq_zero :1733); the open half is the converse.\\n\\nTHE DIMENSION HALF IS NOW REDUCED TO TWO NAMED INPUTS, NEITHER DIMENSION-THEORETIC\\n(run 0067 r7, Picard/GroupSchemeHomogeneity.lean, 11 declarations, 0 sorries, axiom-clean\\nwith three firing controls):\\n\\nPic^0 is a GROUP scheme, so translations are automorphisms of the underlying scheme and the\\nembedding dimension is constant along a translate orbit. This kills the \\\"uniform cotangent\\nbound\\\" that three earlier rows (r5, r6) named as the <= half's open content -- it was never\\na separate piece of mathematics here. Since the value at the identity is an EQUALITY, one\\npoint serves both directions:\\n\\n  topologicalKrullDim_eq_genus_of_homogeneous -- AXIOM-CLEAN, gives dim Pic^0 = g from\\n  (i) the cotangent value at the identity, (ii) regularity of that one stalk, (iii) the\\n  orbit condition.\\n\\n  topologicalKrullDim_eq_genus_of_homogeneous_of_regular -- discharges (i) from front (a)\\n  verbatim, since genus C is DEFINED as the H^1 finrank (Genus.lean:41). Reports sorryAx,\\n  inherited from front (a) alone, with the clean sibling above it as the control.\\n\\n*** RETRACTED (run 0067 r8, commit 27f526ea7): EVERYTHING ABOVE FROM \\\"THE DIMENSION HALF IS NOW\\nREDUCED\\\" IS WRONG. THE ORBIT CONDITION IS NOT A GAP -- IT IS CONTRADICTORY FOR g >= 1, so both\\ntopologicalKrullDim_eq_genus_of_homogeneous theorems are VACUOUS exactly where the A.3 leg\\nexists, and the uniform cotangent bound the r7 row declared dead is REINSTATED as owed.