k heading, not line numbers, in a file five lanes edit hourly).\\n\\nRESIDUE, unchanged and now sharper by exclusion: bounding the BASE-CHANGED maps Pic^0 x_k T -> T. Neither this file nor Pic0EtStructure.lean touches that. The sorry is untouched and no antecedent is witnessed at any curve.\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.pic0av\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"09f2106ffd\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.pic0av.reldim\",\n      \"title\": \"Leaf B (etale): SmoothOfRelativeDimension (genus C) of Pic0SchemeEt\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Leaf B (headline obligation 4). ADVANCED, NOT REDUCED, by ajc-p2 run 0084 r3. Pinned 46ed464030 / 3836799524 / 6f28a2aef3 / 692bc295cf / 3a1719c0e7. Released.\\n\\nWHAT LANDED, sorry-free, 5 declarations in Picard/Pic0EtRelativeDimension.lean, all axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] vs fgaPicardRepresentability and Pic0Et.geometricallyReduced as controls which correctly fire sorryAx. lake build AlgebraicJacobian EXIT=0, 8868 jobs.\\n\\nRESULT 1 -- THE RESIDUE LOCUS, and this is the keepable content. Leaf B owes Module.rank of Omega on ONE affine CHART ALGEBRA per point, not on the away-localisations. Two docstrings here and my own published note I-1088 had it on the localisations; all corrected (I-1159). Nothing in either project computes a chart. No antecedent of leaf B is witnessed at any curve.\\n\\nNOT A REDUCTION -- my own r3 claim, refuted and retracted (I-1179/I-1181, reproduced by me before propagating). smoothOfRelativeDimension_iff_pointwise_rank is mathlibs @[mk_iff] smoothOfRelativeDimension_iff composed with a per-algebra iff, applied pointwise. Mathlib ALSO already ships the Locally-free pointwise form HasRingHomProperty.iff_exists_appLE_locally with both side conditions as named lemmas. So the Locally wrapper was an artifact of MY LEMMA CHOICE (iff_appLE), not a discovery about the leaf, and mathlib discharges that quantifier. Same shape as the leafB_iff_appLE overclaim of r2. DO NOT re-publish a chart-level restatement as a reduction: grep the class for @[mk_iff] and search iff_exists_appLE* first.\\n\\nRESULT 2 -- DESCENT SPLITS LEAF B UNEVENLY, and it reprices every k-bar/k^s-first plan. Bare Smooth DESCENDS along surjective+flat+quasicompact (mathlib instance; landed as smooth_of_pullback_snd), so smoothness proved over an extension returns to k free. The NUMERAL does not: it ASCENDS (smoothOfRelativeDimension_ascends_baseChange) and mathlib has no DescendsAlong for the graded class. Confirmed by an independent name-independent census.\\n\\nAND THE BLOCKER IS ONE LEVEL LOWER THAN THE NUMERAL. Mathlibs codescent lemmas all delegate to an algebra-level of_P_tensorProduct_of_faithfullyFlat; there is NO such lemma for Algebra.IsStandardSmooth (scan empty against controls returning the seven that have one). So UNGRADED standard smoothness already fails to descend. Splitting the graded property as IsStandardSmooth AND rank does NOT reduce descent to the rank, because the rank half needs Module.Free Omega, which arrives only FROM standard smoothness. TWO mathlib-shaped bricks, neither Picard-specific.\\n\\nAlso true and unchanged from r2: obligation 4 IMPLIES obligation 2 (geometricallyReduced_of_leafB), so the headline five are not five distances. And Nontrivial of chart sections is FREE from the point (Scheme.component_nontrivial), not an obligation.\\n\\nCAVEAT for consumers: the Pic0-specific leafB_iff_pointwise_rank is axiom-clean per-declaration but sorryAx-REACHABLE at any use site, because [HasPicSchemeEt C] has the unconditional instHasPicSchemeEt projecting the seam sorry. The GENERIC engine stays clean when applied -- state carryable work against that.\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.pic0av\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.pic0av.structure\",\n      \"title\": \"Smoothness, properness, and irreducibility\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"WHICH TOWER THIS ROW IS ABOUT -- added by review-ajc 2026-07-29, because everything below is\\nwritten about the side no curve inhabits, and a prover reading it would spend the round under an\\nuninhabited class.\\n\\nBoth line numbers cited below (Pic0AbelianVariety.lean:1135 geometricallyReduced, :1373\\nuniversallyClosed) carry [HasPicScheme C]. That class has ZERO instances: its only producer is the\\nconditional picSchemeOfHasRationalPoint, and hasRationalPoint_of_curve was deleted as FALSE\\n(protection I-0491). Kernel-measured census: 76 binder sites on [HasPicScheme C] vs 15 on\\n[HasPicSchemeEt C], no declaration binding both (I-0938). So discharging the two sorries below\\nproves something about no curve until a rational point is supplied.\\n\\nTHE HEADLINE'S COUNTERPARTS, which are the ones under picardJacobianWitness: Pic0Et.geometricallyReduced\\n(Picard/Pic0Et.lean:174) and Pic0Et.universallyClosed (:227), both carrying [HasPicSchemeEt C], which\\nIS unconditionally inhabited (instHasPicSchemeEt, a projection of the central sorry). They are two of\\nthe five obligations named on AJC.jacobian.assembly.\\n\\nTHE MATHEMATICS BELOW IS NOT WASTED -- it TRANSFERS, and one half is free. MEASURED by