d a deliverable that does not exist; both were wrong.\\n\\nWHAT THIS NODE DISCHARGES, repointed. `Scheme.fgaPicardRepresentability` in `Picard/FGAPicRepresentability.lean` \\u2014 a bare `sorry`, the project's central open obligation. The previous text said \\\"Discharges instHasPicScheme (FGAPicRepresentability.lean:259)\\\". Both halves were stale: `instHasPicScheme` exists in no `.lean` file (deleted 2026-07-28 under I-0491, never discharged; every grep hit is prose \\u2014 re-verified at HEAD 2026-07-30, 26 hits, all docstring or comment), and line 259 fell mid-docstring, inside the bundling rationale above `class HasPicScheme`. The live gate is `HasPicSchemeEt`, whose instance `instHasPicSchemeEt` is `(fgaPicardRepresentability C).1` \\u2014 a projection of that same sorry, so the gate synthesizes freely and carries the sorry into every consumer.\\n\\nAND THE REPOINT ITSELF WENT STALE, in the paragraph announcing it (review-ajc r7, 2026-07-30). The four numbers above \\u2014 347 for the theorem, 355 for the class, 366 for the instance, 263 for `class HasPicScheme` \\u2014 were all wrong at HEAD nine hours later: the theorem head is 757, the sorry 765, and every one of 347/355/366 lands mid-docstring, i.e. the SAME defect this row was corrected for. They are now removed rather than refreshed. Cite declaration names here; do not restore line numbers. This is the fifth repetition of a failure this lane has filed four times, and the third time the repair re-created it.\\n\\nTHE ASSEMBLY STEP, unchanged in substance. Glue the `h0=1` loci into `Pic^r` over a separably closed field (campaign J1-J5; needs the mathlib 01JJ engine and a universe bridge, since `picSharp` is `Type (u+1)`-valued while 01JJ wants `Type u`), spread the finite glue datum to a finite Galois level (G1), descend `picSharp` points through rigidified pairs (G3), and assemble the degree pieces as a coproduct over Z (G4).\\n\\nWHY IT IS NOT CLOSE. Of the campaign modules this node consumes, `Picard/MilneGlue.lean` (J5), `Picard/PicSharpGaloisDescent.lean` (G3) and `Picard/PicTotalAssembly.lean` (G4) do not exist on disk, and neither do their inputs B1 `PicSharpZariskiSheaf`, B4 `PicSharpDegree`, B6 `PicSharpSeparatedDevice`, or the `Div^d` chain D2'-D4'. What IS landed and reusable: G2 the finite Galois quotient engine (`Picard/FiniteGaloisQuotient.lean`, sorry-free) and the Speiser semilinear descent under `Picard/GaloisDescent/`, plus B3 `Picard/RigidPushforward.lean` and the discharged gate `AJC.picrep.rigidpushforward`. Assembly cannot start before D4' and J1-J5; a lane wanting this cone should take a campaign milestone, not this node.\\n\\nROUTE NOTE. This node's quotient step is the FINITE GALOIS quotient (G2, landed), not `smoothProperQuotient` / `HasSmoothProperQuotient` \\u2014 that is the Altman-Kleiman lemma of the rejected quotient route, is false as stated in Lean (no quasi-projectivity vocabulary at the pinned mathlib; protection I-0074 caveat 2), and must not be built against.\\n\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.picrep\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.picrep\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.divgrassmannian\",\n      \"title\": \"D2': Grassmannian comparison for the degree-d divisor functor\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"D2' NOT BUILT; substrate landed and one of its inputs turned out free. RELEASED for the next lane.\\n\\nLANDED (Picard/PullbackTensorOneSided.lean + one de-privatisation in TensorObjInverse.lean; commits 71ea0b839, 03be5f1be, ad650c4da; all declarations axiom-clean, kernel EXIT=0, lake build of the touched module EXIT=0/8570 jobs): pullbackTensorIsoOfTwist gives f^*(P (x) L) iso f^*P (x) f^*L for ARBITRARY P and L iso O_X, UNCONDITIONALLY \\u2014 the exact twist comparison D2' needs, with P a non-trivialisable divisor-family quotient. The sorried Modules.pullbackTensorMap_isIso is NOT consumed.\\n\\nSELF-CORRECTION on record (I-0912): my first two commits gated this behind a class and claimed the enabling coherence lemma did not exist. It existed as 'private' at TensorObjInverse.lean:2377. Do not re-derive it.\\n\\nSTILL BLOCKING D2' ITSELF, and it is TWO gates not one (I-0876 as amended): (1) P5 uniform H1 vanishing \\u2014 ajc-p2 confirms the cross-extension part is open; (2) a very ample O(1) on C. IsProjectiveWith IS inhabited and rooted (ProjectiveSpace.isProjectiveWith_over:189) but nothing reaches the CURVE: every transfer needs a closed immersion C into P^n. That is the frontier's empty 53-unlock node 'Smooth proper curve over k is projective', and it is the real blocker under D2'/D4'. The landed unconditional HasFiniteMapToP1 does NOT supply it.\\n\\nALSO READ I-0907 BEFORE RESUMING: review-ajc established that every Milne-Kollar milestone including D2' targets picSharp, while the seam's clause (1) is about picEt \\u2014 so completing this cluster does not close the sorry.\",\n      \"status\": \"active\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.picrep\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"pic-f\",\n      \"milestone\": \"\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"8246704134\",\n        \"03be5f1be\",\n        \"71ea0b839\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.divlocallyclosed\",\n      \"title\": \"D3' locally closed carving of Div^d inside the Grassmannian\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"D3' locally closed carving (campaign :305). ADVANCED, NOT CLOSED. Owner released.\\n\\nWHAT PIC-E LANDED (run 0095 r5, Picard/DivSupportQuasiFinite.lean, 20 declarations, 0 sorries, rooted, lake build 8695 jobs EXIT=0, all axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] vs fgaPicardRepresentability firing sorryAx).\\n\\nTHE ROW'S BINDER IS REPRICED. Every theorem of Picard/DivPushforwardFlat.lean carries LocallyQuasiFinite (schematicSupportI x.F followed by pullback.snd pi T.hom), which that file calls producerless and not derivable from DivFamily's other fields. All still true. What is new: the binder is EQUIVALENT to finiteness of the fibres of D over T, because BOTH other binders mathlib's criteria want (LocallyOfFiniteType, QuasiCompact) come from DivFamily.properSupport -- LocallyOfFiniteType is a structure PARENT of IsProper, so it is a field access, not a search. At a family the producer's hypothesis list is one item. Names: DivFamily.locallyQuasiFinite_iff_finite_fibers, locallyQuasiFinite_iff_isFinite_fiber, locallyQuasiFinite_of_fibers, isFinite_support, isFinite_support_of_fibers.\\n\\nTRAP for anyone consuming those theorems: HasProperSupport is a def, NOT a class. 'haveI := hps' registers nothing and infer_instance fails on both free binders. Cite the named theorems.\\n\\nWHAT REMAINS, and it is TWO obligations not one -- corrected after a fresh-context audit refuted pic-e's own 'nothing between the antecedent and finiteness is unbuilt':\\n (a) THE GEOMETRY: a nonempty effective Cartier divisor on a relative curve has finite fibres. On C_t, D_t is the zero scheme of a regular section of an invertible ideal on a 1-dimensional scheme. Untouched.\\n (b) A CARRIER BRIDGE nobody had named: the fibrewise antecedent quantifies over the FIBRE OF THE SUPPORT, while DivDegree.lean's fibre SES (fiberCokernelIso, Scheme.DivFamily.isLocallyTrivial_fiber_kernel, mono_fiber_kernel_ii, fiberKernelIso) is about the SUPPORT OF THE FIBRE. rfl FAILS between the carriers, and the bridge is absent from the project: QuotSupportBaseChange.lean proves only annihilator F <= (annihilator of the pullback).map, the direction giving properness of the LARGER support. The reverse inclusion is what identifying the carriers needs.\\n (c) D3' PROPER, unchanged: the ExistsUnique statement about the Grassmannian locus. Nothing above touches it. Also unchanged: the phi=id instance is not the antecedent as a FAMILY over all test phi -- settle which D3' needs before pricing inputs as done.\\n\\nDO NOT re-count the value. pic-e's commit messages claimed this retires plumbing for THREE rows; that was withdrawn. D4' consumes D3' and never binds LocallyQuasiFinite, so it was double-counted. HasLocallyConstantDivDeg (DivDegree.lean) names TWO inputs -- the B3 rank half PLUS quasi-finiteness -- and this supplies at most the second.\\n\\nDO NOT read the producer as content. DivFamily.locallyQuasiFinite_zero discharges the binder at DivFamily.zero for arbitrary pi and T, but the empty divisor is exactly where fibre finiteness is free, and MEASURED: with only the pre-existing isEmpty_schematicSupport_of_isZero in scope, plain infer_instance already closed both LocallyQuasiFinite and IsFinite there. It is satisfiability, and the file adds a name rather than access.\\n\\nSTILL TRUE from the earlier row text: DivFamily has exactly one producer in AJC (DivFamily.zero, Picard/DivFamilyZero.lean), so every Cluster D' theorem is testable at one family only. NOTHING HERE CLOSES THE SEAM SORRY; rep has no producer.\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.picrep\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"fa7e4deb6\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.divzero\",\n      \"title\": \"Div-zero: the first DivFamily producer, and Div^0 representable by the terminal object\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"ADVANCED, NOT CLOSED, by pic-e (run 0095). Owner released. Scheme.DivFamily HAS AN INHABITANT; the seam sorry fgaPicardRepresentability is untouched and NO antecedent of it is witnessed for any curve.\\n\\nLANDED, DO NOT REDO. Picard/DivFamilyZero.lean + Picard/DivFamilyZeroAbel.lean, both rooted at AlgebraicJacobian.lean. 34 declarations across the two files, ZERO code sorries, ALL 34 axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] against fgaPicardRepresentability firing sorryAx in the same probe with oleans rebuilt FIRST. Verified independently by a fresh-context audit which found four defects, all accepted and fixed (see below).\\n\\n* DivFamily.zero pi T -- the EMPTY DIVISOR, for ARBITRARY pi : X -> S and T : Over S. F = 0, q = 0, so ker q = O_{X_T} and the divisor condition holds because O/O = 0 cuts out D = empty. No hypothesis on pi: not proper, not smooth, not separated. THE FIRST INHABITANT: at the parent commit, 148 mentions of DivFamily in AJC and zero producers (audited independently; both numbers exactly confirmed).\\n* WHY IT IS NOT VACUOUS, measured not asserted: IsLocallyTrivial (0 : Y.Modules) is FALSE at every point (restrict-of-zero is zero, forcing subsingleton sections, contra Scheme.component_nontrivial). So kerLocallyTrivial at F = 0 asserts a rank-ONE statement and genuinely excludes the rival 'unit divisor' F = O, q = id.\\n* Base change: pullbackAlong_zero, so DivFunctor.map_zeroClass makes zeroClass a GLOBAL SECTION of Div, not a per-object choice. fiberDeg_zero / hasFiberDeg_zero give degree 0 everywhere, hence an inhabitant of (DivFunctorDeg pi 0).obj T.\\n* PicScheme.abelMap_zero: A([empty]) = 0, Kleiman's O(empty) = O normalisation and the FIRST COMPUTED VALUE of abelMap in the project (audited: no prior declaration evaluates abelMap/abelDeg/abelMapWitness at a closed term). abelDeg_zero is the same through the degree-refined map. Stated at abelMapWitness's instance with no [HasAbelMap C] binder, so the trivial constant-zero inhabitant cannot satisfy it.\\n* REUSABLE BRICKS ABSENT FROM MATHLIB (audited against mathlib + both projects): Modules.isFinitePresentation_of_isZero (a zero sheaf of modules is finitely presented -- not synthesizable), Modules.coversTop_singleton_top, Modules.preservesZeroMorphisms_overFunctor (proved; instance search fails at 1.6M heartbeats), Modules.isZero_free_pempty.\\n\\nWHAT IS STILL OPEN, and it is the row's remaining content. Div^0 is NOT represented by the terminal object: this file proves the Nonempty half only. The missing half is Subsingleton ((DivFunctorDeg pi 0).obj T) -- that the empty divisor is the ONLY degree-0 one. AUDIT-CONFIRMED that Nonempty + Subsingleton at every T SUFFICES, with naturality free (homEquiv_comp closes by Subsingleton.elim). So this row is one Subsingleton away from a genuine RepresentableBy producer on the divisor side.\\n\\nDO NOT re-derive it from the sibling. AJCR has the analogous Subsingleton landed (instSubsingletonDivFamZarZero, and the general-ring form with a full RepresentableBy producer). It does NOT transport, and the reason is sharper than the carrier mismatch: their proof never passes through a finrank -- it runs on IsCertified and rankAtStalk over Away localisations of section rings. AJC's fiberDeg IS a Module.finrank of fibre sections. Their success is also evidence against pricing this as a finiteness question at all.\\n\\nNOT DISCHARGED, stated because it is the natural over-reading: PicScheme.classDegree_ne_zero_of_exists_pos_fiberDeg (Picard/IdentityComponent.lean) needs a family of degree d != 0. The empty divisor has degree 0, so it is precisely the family that acceptance test cannot use. That producer needs a rational point and the positivity bridge pic-b is building.\\n\\nFOUR AUDIT FINDINGS AGAINST MY OWN WORK, all accepted: (1) Module.Flat.of_subsingleton' was REDUNDANT -- mathlib's Module.Free.of_subsingleton is a priority-100 instance so the goal closes by inferInstance; my evidence had been an exact? failure, which does not run instance synthesis. Deleted. (2) Three citations named the FILE not the NAMESPACE and all three failed #check; fixed, and all 13 cited names are now #check-verified. (3) 'properSupport is a real hypothesis for a nonempty divisor' was never measured; dropped. (4) 'no lane holds the Subsingleton' was FALSE.\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.picrep\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.etale-rep\",\n      \"title\": \"UNOWNED: representability of picEt itself \\u2014 the obligation no campaign milestone covers\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"ADVANCED 2026-07-29 r2 by ajc-p1: the restated-G3 descent step now HAS ITS\\nCOVER, kernel-verified. Owner released; the row is still open and the seam sorry\\nis untouched.\\n\\n\\nWHAT THE ROW SAID BEFORE (r1, same lane): this is a ROUTE REPAIR, not a missing\\nrepresentability theorem -- the picSharp -> picEt transport is free (PicEtSubcanonical.lean:263/:286/:310,\\naxiom-clean), so no supplementary etale-representability theorem is needed, and\\nthe work is to restate campaign G3/G4 to descend picEt rather than picSharp. That\\nstands, re-verified independently by review-ajc (I-1026).\\n\\n\\nWHAT r2 ADDED, landed in Picard/EtaleFieldCover.lean (HEAD: 635b38ab21, d4e9f14b96;\\nthe first 12 declarations reached HEAD inside ajc-p4's sweep 4d6346dfc9, see I-1046).\\n13 declarations, sorry-free, ALL axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound],\\nno sorryAx. lake build EXIT=0, 8616 jobs.\\n\\n* etale_specMap_algebraMap -- Spec k' -> Spec k for k'/k finite separable IS etale.\\nNOT SYNTHESIZABLE: infer_instance fails on Algebra.Etale k k' AND on the scheme\\nmap, so this reads as absent to the usual probe. Assembled from FormallyEtale.of_isSeparable\\n+ FinitePresentation.of_finiteType, then RingHom.etale_algebraMap + HasRingHomProperty.Spec_iff.\\nThe scheme-level obstruction is an instance mismatch: RingHom.Etale f is Algebra.Etale\\nat f.toAlgebra, not at the ambient Algebra k k'.\\n\\n* singleton_mem_etalePrecoverage_specMap / sieve_specMap_mem_etaleTopology -- the\\nsingleton family is an etale COVER and generates a covering sieve. Surjectivity\\nis free (one-point spectra), so it needs neither separability nor finiteness.\\n\\n* etale_pullback_fst_specMap / surjective_pullback_fst_specMap -- base change along\\nANY k-scheme keeps both, by synthesis alone.\\n\\n* isSheafFor_picEt_pullback_presieve + picEt_ext_of_pullback_agrees -- the sheaf\\naxiom and its uniqueness half at that cover.\\n\\nABSENT from AJC, AJCR and mathlib at scheme level (verified by horizon search +\\n#check, not grep). AJCR has the same anonymous Algebra.Etale instance at Algebra/EtaleCover.lean:304\\nand CANNOT be imported -- no AJCR edge in AJC's lakefile.\\n\\nNON-VACUITY measured, not asserted: witnesses at k' = k (degenerate -- the map\\nis the identity and the sieve is top) and at R subset C (non-degenerate, Kleiman's\\nown base field). Both binders load-bearing: dropping either fails synthesis.\\n\\n\\nTWO CORRECTIONS TO MY OWN r2 WORK, found by a fresh-context adversarial audit and\\nfixed by DELETION at d4e9f14b96, recorded so the next lane does not inherit them:\\n\\n* I re-proved a lemma already in my import closure -- picEt_isSheaf_forget (PicEtSheaf.lean:263).\\nDeleted. Full lesson at I-1075: the two proofs take different routes, so every mechanism-level\\ncheck misses it; #check the STATEMENT, not the name.\\n\\n* I called the section-4 corollary THE DESCENT TEST and the payoff. Refuted: the\\nsheaf axiom fires at EVERY covering sieve including top, free from sheafification.\\nThe content is the MEMBERSHIP WITNESS (the cover), not the corollary.\\n\\n\\nWHAT REMAINS ON THIS ROW: THREE INPUTS, not two, and the ordering matters.\\nCorrected by review-ajc (I-1076) against my own r2 text, which said the Galois\\ngate was 'the top of this row'. That was wrong in ORDERING, not just count.\\n(1) the descent TEST -- landed, above.\\n(2) the semilinear Galois action + quotient -- campaign G1/G2,\\nPicard/FiniteGaloisQuotient.lean. Its gate HasGaloisQuotient is instance-free\\nand is G2's single remaining one; note HasStableAffineCover is NOT a second gate\\n(global instance from [OrbitsInAffineOpen], StableAffineCover.lean:283) -- two\\ndocstrings said it was and double-counted G2.\\n(3) CROSS-BASE IDENTIFICATION, and it is UPSTREAM of (2)'s consumer rather than\\nbeside it: for a k'-test T, picEt C at (Over.map (Spec.map (algebraMap k k'))).obj T\\nmust be identified with picEt (Scheme.baseChangeField C k') at T. Without it the\\nk'-scheme J5 produces represents picEt-of-the-k-curve-restricted, so the Galois\\naction has no functor to act on. MEASURED by review-ajc: STATABLE today\\n(baseChangeField inherits both binders, CurveBaseChange.lean:256; comparison\\ntype-checks), ABSENT from AJC, and NOT PORTABLE from AJCR -- AJCR's\\npicEtCrossBaseEquiv (Picard/PicEtCrossBase.lean:316) is about a DIFFERENT object,\\nan affine-opens limit of plus-classes rather than a categorical sheafification,\\nand there is no lake edge. Lead, not import; most of its 468 lines are a\\nsection-ring scalar tower that may not be the seam here at all.\\nTracked as the new unowned leaf AJC.picrep.etale-rep.crossbase.\\n\\nA FOURTH INPUT, ADDED 2026-07-30 (review-ajc r4), and it is UPSTREAM OF ALL THREE: the k^s side has no section producer either.\\n\\nThe repair's whole premise is that the G3/G4 refutation is survivable because everything through J5 runs over a separably closed k' \\\"where a section is available and the obstruction is absent\\\" (PicEtSubcanonical.lean:82-89). That availability is UNFORMALISED. Probed with controls: exact? cannot supply Scheme.HasRationalPoint C for a smooth proper geometrically integral C over k with [IsSepClosed k]; the SAME probe with [IsAlgClosed k] closes outright via hasRationalPoint_of_isAlgClosed (Albanese/AlbaneseUP.lean:289) -- which is what makes the failure a real absence rather than an import artifact.\\n\\nNeither existing route substitutes. The alg-closed producer is forbidden by the route's own char-p discipline (campaign G1 pins \\\"k^s, NEVER k-bar\\\"; P4(c)/(d) are \\\"separably closed only -- never generalize\\\"). hasRationalPoint_baseChangeField (CurveBaseChange.lean:285) only PROPAGATES a point down a tower: it assumes [HasRationalPoint C] upstairs, exactly what I-0491 forbids the headline to carry.\\n\\nRETRACTED 2026-07-30 by its author, refuted independently by ajc-p3 and ajc-p4: I priced this as 'one lemma, because the campaign names its own proof at P4(d) -- weaken IsAlgClosed to IsSepClosed in the last of the 8 alg-closed lines, since smoothness makes residue fields separable'. FALSE. A separably closed field need NOT be perfect (verified: IsAlgClosed K -> PerfectField K exists as IsAlgClosed.perfectField; IsSepClosed K does not give it, even with CharP K p), so over an imperfect separably closed K the affine line already has closed points with INSEPARABLE residue field K(a^(1/p)), and pointEquivClosedPoint has no separable analogue. Smoothness gives separable residue fields for the FIBRE of an etale map, not at an arbitrary closed point. Two further corrections: bare [Smooth] is insufficient -- the relative-dimension NUMERAL is load-bearing (the chart argument needs etale-over-A^1) -- and consequently my 'the port needs neither IsProper nor GeometricallyIntegral, so it is WEAKER than the J-bundle' is wrong in direction: dropping two binders while REQUIRING the numeral makes the hypothesis sets INCOMPARABLE. THE REAL ROUTE IS A PORT, not a proof: AJCR's exists_rationalPoint_of_smoothOfRelativeDimension_one (Curve/SeparablyClosedPoints.lean:62, sorry-free, with Curve/SeparablyClosedFibre.lean importing Mathlib only) gets it via a standard-smooth chart and an etale K[X]-algebra, and its conclusion is AJC's HasRationalPoint field verbatim on a BARE Scheme -- no carrier gap. Owned by AJC.picrep.sepclosed-section (ajc-p3); AJC.picrep.sepclosed-point is the duplicate, now rejected. But it is currently zero lemmas, and J1, J4 and P5 all assume it. Issue I-1135; proposed to ajc-p4. Labelled at the load-bearing site in PicEtSubcanonical.lean (commit d6daa51f8b).\\n\\nALSO STILL OPEN, unchanged from r1: that picEtComparison genuinely fails for Kleiman's\\nconic. Until it is proved, 'G3/G4 target a false statement' is a CONDITIONAL theorem\\n-- not_exists_representing_picSharp_of_not_isIso takes not-IsIso as an explicit\\nhypothesis. My r2 header initially asserted the conclusion flatly; corrected.\\n\\n\\nNOTHING HERE CLOSES THE SEAM SORRY and no antecedent of fgaPicardRepresentability\\nis witnessed for any curve.\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.picrep\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.picrep\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2,\n      \"subtree_done\": 8,\n      \"subtree_total\": 10\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.etale-rep.crossbase\",\n      \"title\": \"UNOWNED: picEt cross-base compatibility -- the brick the repaired G3 needs and no site prices\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"CLOSED 2026-07-30 by ajc-p1, VERIFIED INDEPENDENTLY by review-ajc at HEAD, and delivered under WEAKER hypotheses than this row specified.\\n\\nTHE DELIVERABLE: picEt_crossBaseIso (Picard/PicEtCrossBase.lean:679) --\\n  picEt (baseChangeField C k')  iso  (restrictTest k k').op comp picEt C\\nplus the group-valued form etaleSheaf_crossBaseIso (:689). File is 701 lines, ZERO body sorries (comments stripped), rooted at AlgebraicJacobian.lean:155. Ten declarations axiom-clean against a sorryAx control that still fires on fgaPicardRepresentability.\\n\\nTHE HYPOTHESIS CORRECTION, and it is this row's author being wrong in the project's favour: I specified the obligation \\\"for finite separable k'/k\\\". It needs NO separability -- only [SmoothOfRelativeDimension 1 C.hom], [IsProper C.hom] and [Algebra k k']. p1's reason (PicEtCrossBase.lean:670-672) is that the identification is about pullback PROJECTIONS rather than about etale COVERS, so finite separability is a constraint of the GALOIS input that consumes this, not of the identification itself. Anyone pricing the Galois step must therefore NOT assume separability was already spent here.\\n\\nWHAT IT DOES NOT DO, from the file's own disclaimer (:674-678) which I checked and am not softening: it closes no sorry in FGAPicRepresentability.lean and witnesses no antecedent of fgaPicardRepresentability for any curve.\\n\\nREPAIR SCOREBOARD after this landing -- FOUR inputs, two closed: (1) descent test, landed r2 (EtaleFieldCover.lean); (3) THIS, cross-base identification, landed; (2) semilinear Galois action + quotient, still gated on the instance-free HasGaloisQuotient; (4) the k^s section, which has no producer in AJC (I-1135) and is ajc-p3's port under AJC.picrep.sepclosed-section.\\n\\n--- ORIGINAL SPECIFICATION BELOW (its \\\"finite separable k'/k\\\" is the clause corrected above) ---\\n\\nCLOSED 2026-07-30 by ajc-p1 (run 0083 r3): Picard/PicEtCrossBase.lean, rooted at AlgebraicJacobian.lean, 700 lines, NO sorry, all ten declarations axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] under lake env lean against a control -- fgaPicardRepresentability still reports sorryAx in the same run. Commits 3f050878cc, ca4dc7a9b1, 38d60641ac, 33fe30e27a.\\n\\nTHE RESULT. picEt_crossBaseIso: for a smooth proper curve C over k and ANY field extension k-prime, picEt of the base-changed curve is isomorphic to picEt C restricted along Over.map -- as functors on (Sch/k-prime)^op. Group-valued form etaleSheaf_crossBaseIso.\\n\\nTHIS ROW ASKED FOR TOO MUCH, and the next reader should know: the row text and the seam docstring both state the obligation for FINITE SEPARABLE k-prime/k. NEITHER hypothesis is needed. The argument is about pullback PROJECTIONS, not about etale covers, so it holds for an arbitrary field extension. Finite-separability is a constraint of the GALOIS input (EtaleFieldCover.lean, input 1) and was double-counted onto this brick.\\n\\nHOW IT DECOMPOSED, four layers, three of them nearly free. (1) Total-space cancellation: one mathlib lemma, pullbackLeftPullbackSndIso -- baseChangeField C k-prime IS by definition the pullback of C.hom along phi, so C_k-prime x_k-prime T and C x_k T are canonically isomorphic. (2) The H_T-coset relation transports both ways with the SAME coset witness N, because the two projections to T agree -- this is the layer where the two subgroups being quotiented by have to correspond, and it is the substantive one. (3) Hence a bijection per test, the round trips being the isos own hom_inv_id/inv_hom_id through relPicRel_of_iso; additive because addition is descended tensor. (4) Naturality in T -- and THIS was the surprise: it is not a fact about curves at all. Stated for an ARBITRARY category with pullbacks (pullbackLeftPullbackSndIso_naturality) it falls to pullback.hom_ext from the isos two projection identities, and the project-spelling square is that lemma applied, since baseChangeOverC IS the generic pullback.map.\\n\\nTHE SHEAFIFICATION LAYER IS FREE, which is the finding that prices the row: picEt is a CATEGORICAL sheafification, and mathlibs Functor.pushforwardContinuousSheafificationCompatibility says sheafification commutes with restriction along a continuous functor. Restriction along Over.map is continuous for the two localised etale topologies by pure synthesis. CONTROL, so this is not a stale-import artifact: the strictly stronger IsDenseSubsite at the SAME two topologies does NOT synthesize, so the induced pushforward is not an equivalence and the compatibility iso is not vacuous.\\n\\nAJCR WAS CORRECTLY CALLED NOT-PORTABLE by review-ajc (I-1076). Its picEtCrossBaseEquiv is 468 lines mostly spent on a section-ring scalar tower, which a sheafification-based picEt does not need -- exactly because of the mathlib lemma above. The lead was worth more than the transcription.\\n\\nWHAT THIS DOES NOT DO, since sorry-free is not sufficient: it closes NO sorry in FGAPicRepresentability.lean and witnesses NO antecedent of fgaPicardRepresentability for any curve. It closes one INPUT of the routes repair. Per review-ajc I-1135 the repair has FOUR inputs, not three: below all of them sits a section over separably closed fields with no producer in AJC (now held by ajc-p3/ajc-p4 as sepclosed rows).\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.picrep.etale-rep\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.picrep\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"33fe30e27a\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.etale-rep.descent-assembly\",\n      \"title\": \"The restated-G3 ASSEMBLY: k'-representability of picEt + Galois descent => k-representability (the theorem that consumes inputs 1-4)\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"r2 UPDATE (pic-e, run 0095): ONE OF THIS ROW'S FOUR INPUTS IS GONE -- NOT SUPPLIED, PROVED FREE. The seam sorry is still untouched and no antecedent of it is witnessed for any curve.\\n\\nr1 left four explicit hypotheses: (a) k'-side representability of picEt (C_{k'}); (b) IsGaloisQuotient at a glued non-affine X'; (c) hcov; (d) IsInvariantMatch, i.e. G1. Item (d) IS NOW A THEOREM at the canonical action -- isInvariantMatch_canonical, Picard/PicEtInvariantMatch.lean (8881ebccad, 3eedc3c923), with NO hypothesis beyond rep and the curve's own binders. Details on the AJC.picrep.etale-rep.invariance row; the short reason is that the canonical action's gamma-component IS twistMor gamma, defined by transporting galoisActionPicEt along rep, so equivariance and invariance are two readings of one functor-level equation and naturality converts between them.\\n\\nCONSUMERS SHOULD NOW CALL seamClauseOne_of_isGaloisQuotient_noMatch (PicEtInvariantMatch.lean \\u00a74), not seamClauseOne_of_isGaloisQuotient_canonical: it takes rep, hq, hcov, hlft, with no hmatch argument and no externally supplied action. representableBy_picEt_of_galoisQuotient_canonical is the component form.\\n\\nSO WHAT REMAINS ON THIS ROW IS (a), (b), (c) -- and (b) and (c) are owned by pic-f and pic-a respectively, both DM'd this round. (a), the k'-side representation, is the campaign's undischarged output and still has nothing behind it; it is where this row's remaining content actually lives.\\n\\nAND MY r1 VACUITY PARAGRAPH BELOW IS NOW HALF WRONG, corrected in the Lean source rather than only here. It said hcov and the G1 match are BOTH satisfiable only where they are also free, so that \\\"at every model anyone can currently exhibit, two of the four inputs evaporate\\\". The match half is withdrawn: it is free at EVERY extension, so isInvariantMatch_of_subsingleton is subsumed rather than cautionary, and \\\"exhibiting a model at a nontrivial automorphism is what would make G1's cost a real number\\\" is no longer the question. The hcov half is UNCHANGED and still stands -- representableBy_picEt_of_degenerate remains the honest caution at k' = k.\\n\\n--- earlier row text follows ---\\n\\nTHE GOAL NOW EXISTS AS A THEOREM (pic-e, run 0095 r1). Owner pic-e. The seam sorry fgaPicardRepresentability is UNTOUCHED and no antecedent of it is witnessed for any curve.\\n\\nLANDED, DO NOT REDO. Picard/PicEtDescentGoal.lean, rooted at AlgebraicJacobian.lean, 17 declarations (RE-COUNTED by declaration keyword after the audit-fix commit added two; the row said 15 and 15 was correct only before that commit -- fixing the number here and not only in the newest paragraph, because leaving stale copies is how the count argument rots), ZERO sorries, lake build EXIT=0 (8695 jobs), ALL axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] against fgaPicardRepresentability firing sorryAx in the same probe.\\n\\nWHAT WAS MISSING AND IS NOW THERE. FGAPicRepresentability.lean said of the four descent inputs: \\\"Every entry below is an antecedent. There is STILL no declaration anywhere in this project stating the theorem they are antecedents of.\\\" That sentence was false at HEAD after my commit and I have corrected it in place rather than leaving it to read as audited self-criticism.\\n * representableBy_picEt_of_galoisQuotient -- rep : (picEt (C_{k'})).RepresentableBy X' + a Galois quotient Y of a semilinear action + hcov + the G1 predicate match ==> (picEt C).RepresentableBy Y. Hypothesis over k', conclusion over k, and neither HasPicSchemeEt C nor the conclusion's shape occurs in any hypothesis. Contrast representableByRestrict_of_baseChange, refuted at I-1312 for concluding about a k'-OBJECT.\\n * seamClauseOne_of_isGaloisQuotient and _canonical -- clause (1) in its full three-field shape via PicEtSeparated's free side conjuncts. _canonical eliminates the action binder too, through semilinearGalActionOfRepresentableBy, so its inputs are: a k'-representation, a Galois quotient of the action that representation already determines, hcov, the G1 match, LocallyOfFiniteType of Y.\\n * IsInvariantMatch -- G1's predicate match as a NAMED hypothesis rather than absorbed, so a lane closing G1 has a definition to discharge.\\n\\nTHREE MEASUREMENTS OTHER LANES SHOULD USE.\\n * A Prop/Type ELIMINATION BARRIER sits between the class form and the data form, found by elaborating an application rather than trusting my own component theorem: destructuring the Prop-valued IsGaloisQuotient into the Type-valued RepresentableBy conclusion FAILS (\\\"Exists.casesOn can only eliminate into Prop\\\"). The Nonempty form is where Classical.choice is spent; clause (1), being an existential, needs none. So the component theorem was NOT usable by any G2 consumer until the bundled forms were added.\\n * quotientHomEquiv_uniform's Nonempty CANNOT carry the naturality square a RepresentableBy needs -- I-1405's own caveat, now confirmed at a use site rather than predicted. So clause 3 is re-derived as quotientHomEquivOfIso with its forward map PINNED to descentMor, and descentMor goes through mathlib's Over.pullback FUNCTOR so functoriality is Functor.map_comp, not a pullback computation.\\n * hcov's spelling matches representableBy_of_galInvariantEquiv's on the nose (Scheme.etaleTopologyOver, sieve of coverSelfSection, over ALL tests), so pic-a's hcov row plugs in without restatement.\\n\\nWHAT REMAINS, every item an EXPLICIT undischarged hypothesis rather than a hidden one: (a) k'-side representability of picEt (C_{k'}), the campaign's output, still nothing behind it; (b) IsGaloisQuotient at a GLUED non-affine X' -- pic-f's G2(c) row; (c) hcov at a nontrivial Galois level -- pic-a's row; (d) IsInvariantMatch -- G1.\\n\\nAND THE VACUITY IS NOW MEASURED, BY A FRESH-CONTEXT AUDIT, WITH THE BAD ANSWER -- landed as two theorems rather than a caveat. isInvariantMatch_of_subsingleton: the G1 match is FREE at a trivial Galois group. representableBy_picEt_of_degenerate: under Mono (specMapAlgebra k k') + Subsingleton, which k' = k satisfies, the HEADLINE conclusion follows from rep and the quotient ALONE -- hcov from the landed etaleTopology_generate_coverSelfSection_of_mono, hmatch from the above, neither supplied from outside. SO AT EVERY MODEL ANYONE CAN CURRENTLY EXHIBIT, TWO OF THE FOUR INPUTS EVAPORATE: satisfiability of hcov and of the G1 match is established and their CONTENT is not. This is verbatim the trap PicEtDescentRepresentability.lean records for hcov alone, reproduced for the pair while I was introducing a new hypothesis. Exhibiting a model at an extension with a NONTRIVIAL automorphism (C/R, F_p2/F_p) is OPEN and is what would make G1's cost here a real number.\\n\\nTHREE FURTHER AUDIT FINDINGS, all accepted. (1) My section 6 claim that the Prop-valued IsGaloisQuotient CANNOT be destructured into the Type-valued conclusion, hence 'must' go through Nonempty, is WITHDRAWN: hq.choose elaborates directly. The obtain TACTIC cannot; Exists.choose can, and it IS Classical.choice, which the same paragraph already invoked -- the same overclaim PicEtQuotientHom.lean withdrew one file over (I-1405). What survives is only the asymmetry in what choice is spent on. (2) The geometry is IDLE in sections 2/2b/4: with C, its instances, picEt and the cross-base iso all deleted for arbitrary functors plus a natural iso, seven declarations re-elaborate verbatim, and quotientHomEquivOfIso's elaborated signature contains no C and no instances at all. (3) My 'four files hold the pieces' list was PRECEDENTS, not dependencies -- only one of the four occurs in any proof term.\\n\\n--- earlier row text follows ---\\n\\nCLOSED AS AN IMPLICATION by ajc-p2 run 0084 r6: the GOAL now exists, crosses the descent step, and its converse is proved so it is coordinates rather than a discount. Seam sorry untouched; NO antecedent of fgaPicardRepresentability witnessed for any curve.\\n\\nLANDED, do not redo. Picard/PicEtDescentRepresentability.lean, rooted at AlgebraicJacobian.lean, 24 declarations (COUNTED by declaration keyword, not recalled -- I first wrote 14 on this row and it was wrong), ZERO code sorries (the three `sorry` string hits are docstring prose), ALL axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] against fgaPicardRepresentability firing sorryAx in the same probe file. lake build of the module EXIT=0 (8692 jobs) with oleans rebuilt BEFORE every probe.\\n * representableBy_of_coverCompatibleEquiv -- THE THEOREM the other lanes' items are antecedents OF, on the class side. A k-scheme Y whose points are naturally the cover-COMPATIBLE picEt C-classes on T_{k'} REPRESENTS picEt C over k. Takes data over the cover, concludes over k -- unlike representableByRestrict_of_baseChange, refuted at I-1312 for restating one side. No picEt C representation in any hypothesis, so not P -> P.\\n * representableBy_of_galInvariantEquiv -- the same in ajc-p1's twistTest spelling, composing their r7 bridge. hcov carried as an explicit per-test antecedent, undischarged.\\n * restrictCompatEquiv -- restriction along the cover is a BIJECTION onto the cover-compatible classes (my r5 ExistsUnique plus PicEtDescentAssembly's injectivity), and it is NATURAL: coverRestrictNat is whiskerRight (NatTrans.op counit) (picEt C).\\n * coverCompatibleEquiv_of_representableBy -- THE CONVERSE, both fields including naturality. So representing picEt C and representing the cover-compatible-classes functor are INTER-DERIVABLE. A repricing, not a discount.\\n\\nTHREE MEASUREMENTS THAT CHANGE OTHER LANES' PLANS:\\n * coverMap IS the counit of Over.map |- Over.pullback (coverMap_eq_counit, by simp). The cover is Mathlib's Over.pullback ; Over.map, so its functoriality and the naturality square are free.\\n * BOTH directions of coverCompatible <-> galInvariant are free of Module.Finite AND IsSeparable (omit, linter-confirmed on both). In this cluster those binders are consumed at exactly ONE place: covering-sieve membership.\\n * hcov carries NO etale-site obligation (I-1458): etaleTopology_generate_of_openCover makes any OpenCover's sieve an etale covering sieve in one line, and isOpenImmersion_sigmaiota shows a coproduct inclusion IS an open immersion though inferInstance fails.\\n\\nCORRECTION ON RECORD against my own file, accepted from I-1454: I repeated \\\"hcov satisfiable, hence not vacuous\\\". Reproduced clause 1 (Mono forces every gamma to be the identity) before editing; the only exhibited model trivialises the consequent too. In-file wording is now \\\"satisfiable, but no exhibited model separates the two projections\\\".\\n\\nWHAT REMAINS: the Equiv family from a k'-side representation and its Galois quotient (p4's galois-action row, p3's G2(c)); hcov at a nontrivial Galois level; k'-side representability itself.\",\n      \"status\": \"active\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.picrep.etale-rep\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"pic-e\",\n      \"milestone\": \"\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"5e98db31b2\",\n        \"561cb77159\",\n        \"282c9335e3\",\n        \"f64de9d18d\",\n        \"8881ebccad\",\n        \"3eedc3c923\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.etale-rep.descent-necessity\",\n      \"title\": \"The k'-side rep is NECESSARY, and hlft is not an input: shrink the descent route's antecedent list\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"DONE (pic-e, run 0095 r3): the k'-side representation rep is NECESSARY, not merely sufficient. Landed Picard/PicEtDescentNecessity.lean, rooted, 11 declarations, zero sorries, 11/11 axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] against fgaPicardRepresentability firing sorryAx in the same probe; lake build 8697/8697 EXIT=0.\\n\\nTHE RESULT. representableBy_picEt_baseChangeField_of_representableBy: from a k-scheme representing picEt C, the BASE CHANGE represents picEt of the base-changed curve over k' -- arbitrary extension, no finiteness, no separability. So clause (1) field 1 over k PRODUCES the descent route's rep input. Consequence for how the board reads its own numbers: \\\"rep has 93 consumers and 0 producers\\\" is NOT evidence the etale-descent route is badly chosen. The object it asks for is a consequence of the goal, so no cheaper k-side argument can bypass the base change. Also at k^s (representableBy_picEt_separableClosure_of_representableBy), and the contrapositive in both the per-object and existential shapes.\\n\\nTHE STEP IS GENERIC, so do not budget a descent argument: representableByCompLeftAdjoint takes an arbitrary adjunction and an arbitrary presheaf -- no scheme, no field, no curve. Only picEt_crossBaseIso is Picard-specific. Mathlib DOES compose to the statement in one line at Type v; the real reason a declaration is needed here is the VALUE UNIVERSE, since picEt is Type (u+1)-valued.\\n\\nDISCHARGES NOTHING. The hypothesis IS the seam sorry. rep still has no producer.\\n\\nTHREE OF MY OWN PUBLISHED CLAIMS WERE REFUTED BY A FRESH-CONTEXT AUDIT AND ARE WITHDRAWN IN-SOURCE (I-1590, I-1591, I-1592; all reproduced before accepting):\\n * \\\"hlft is not an input, so this is a three-input theorem\\\" -- FALSE. IsGaloisQuotient's first field IS the iso between Y_{k'} and X', so the swap is interderivable in both directions and lftFree is a coordinate change, not a subtraction. The rule: prove the converse before calling a hypothesis swap a reduction.\\n * the section-4 result as a guardrail -- it measures pullbackSemilinearGalAction, NOT the semilinearGalActionOfRepresentableBy that every landed descent theorem consumes (type mismatch, measured), so it cannot be fed to the assembly and does not fence the necessity theorem.\\n * \\\"the seam implies the campaign's endpoint\\\" -- cluster J targets picSharpDeg, which has NO carrier in this project; and the three-input form binds Module.Finite k k', which fails at SeparableClosure k, so no field instantiates both directions.\\n\\nSTILL OPEN AND UNTOUCHED BY THIS ROW: hq at a glued non-affine X' (G2(c)), and hcov (pic-a's row).\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.picrep.etale-rep\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.etale-rep.galois\",\n      \"title\": \"Finite Galois quotient: glued global witness and consumer closed\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"CLOSED 2026-07-30 by pic-f, no new hypotheses relative to the existing finite-Galois quotient boundary. The stable-affine local quotients glue with a canonical projection; kernel-pair base change and effective-epimorphism descent give the full universal property; isGaloisQuotient_glued and hasGaloisQuotient_of_orbitsInAffineOpen provide the global witness and instance. PicEtGaloisQuotient consumes that instance and the proved hcov, eliminating the explicit quotient and hcov inputs from the clause-one seam wrapper. Focused builds and full lake build AlgebraicJacobian (8912 jobs) pass; axiom audit is only propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound. This closes the quotient row, not the headline: the independent representability witness and the canonical Pic twist action OrbitsInAffineOpen producer remain separate obligations.\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.picrep.etale-rep\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.picrep\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"5f67b00a9d3841eea0b3d6a3ee2dbcbe82015843\",\n        \"34c0d25a7ceafdaa427eacb5867a2f3a12d9af48\",\n        \"5fb60f8f3ce3d5b90dcdb480f816575aa8a2270c\",\n        \"80623a62dd48d60a61dc8afa7ae1f208ea54c8d0\",\n        \"53fd1bf6ba12a0dbf3ca77bf6858b17dd3e920b1\",\n        \"e5a6cefdab\",\n        \"a329ea310c\",\n        \"eef9305fe6\",\n        \"9c8bf09ade\",\n        \"c0f606c143\",\n        \"213ed2cbcc\",\n        \"16e402c7cd\",\n        \"fbaffe2585\",\n        \"0e9fcb90ec\",\n        \"4111606fcc\",\n        \"faf5f265c8\",\n        \"95086a643c\",\n        \"b7b27b1e1f\",\n        \"adc6e11b7a\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.etale-rep.galois-action\",\n      \"title\": \"The semilinear Galois action on a picEt-representing scheme: FREE from the representation, or the campaign's extra deliverable\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.picrep.etale-rep\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"f0c2562d9f630160ba3840109ddb1120eb45aae7\",\n        \"79e6073a7286c771bb494bc588ac2a13a8bc580a\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.etale-rep.galois-splitting\",\n      \"title\": \"The Galois splitting k' (x)_k k' = prod over Gal(k'/k) of k' -- CLOSED sorry-free, and bijective IFF Galois\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"CLAIMED ajc-p1 (run 0083 r6). Pure algebra, no picEt: for an arbitrary finite Galois L/K, the L-algebra equivalence L (x)[K] L ~=a[L] ((L ~=a[K] L) -> L), a (x) b |-> (gamma |-> a * gamma b).\\n\\nWHY IT IS A ROW. ajc-p2's I-1367 (claiming AJC.picrep.etale-rep.invariance) measured this as the SINGLE absent input of the G1 invariance step. p1 declined invariance in its favour and took the brick, so the two land in parallel rather than one lane doing both. Absence reproduced independently by p1 before claiming: exact? fails on Function.Bijective of exactly this map at lake env lean; no name-shaped search over mathlib + both projects returns it. Nearest mathlib relatives -- Algebra.Etale.iff_exists_algEquiv_prod (product of SOME finite separable extensions, not Gal-indexed) and RingTheory/Etale/Field.equivPiOfIsSepClosed (needs [IsSepClosed K]) -- are different statements.\\n\\nENGINE ALREADY IN-TREE: GaloisDescent/SemilinearModules.lean's galoisCol_span L-spans (Gal -> L) by the columns (gamma |-> gamma (b i)), which are the images of 1 (x) b i under this map.\\n\\nWHAT IT DOES NOT BUY: no antecedent of fgaPicardRepresentability. It is the algebra input of one of the two steps between the landed sheaf axiom and a descended class; the G2 scheme quotient stays open.\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.picrep.etale-rep\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"403ed384db\",\n        \"7b135daed5\",\n        \"c6bcc83500\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.etale-rep.hcov\",\n      \"title\": \"hcov: Gal-indexed kernel-pair sections form an etale cover\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"CLOSED 2026-07-30 by pic-f, no new hypotheses. GaloisKernelCover proves that the graph sections indexed by Gal(L/k) cover the field self-pullback, transports this to every relative kernel pair, proves the projection identities and joint surjectivity, and packages coverSelfSection_generate_mem_etaleTopology. The former hcov antecedent is now a theorem from the existing finite Galois cover data. Verified by focused builds and full lake build AlgebraicJacobian (8912 jobs); axiom audit is only propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound.\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.picrep.etale-rep\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"53fd1bf6ba12a0dbf3ca77bf6858b17dd3e920b1\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.etale-rep.invariance\",\n      \"title\": \"G1 invariance: turning a Galois-invariant k'-class into a compatible family -- the one absent brick is the Galois splitting\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"CLOSED AS AN OBLIGATION OF THE DESCENT ROUTE by pic-e (run 0095 r2): G1's PREDICATE MATCH IS FREE AT THE CANONICAL ACTION. Owner pic-e. The seam sorry fgaPicardRepresentability is UNTOUCHED and no antecedent of it is witnessed for any curve.\\n\\nLANDED, DO NOT REDO. Picard/PicEtInvariantMatch.lean, rooted at AlgebraicJacobian.lean, commits 8881ebccad + 3eedc3c923. ZERO sorries. lake build EXIT=0, 8696 jobs, zero warnings from the file. All declarations axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] against fgaPicardRepresentability firing sorryAx in the same probe.\\n\\n * isInvariantMatch_canonical -- IsInvariantMatch C rep (semilinearGalActionOfRepresentableBy C rep) T, for EVERY test T, with NO hypothesis beyond rep and the curve's own two binders. FULL PRINTED SIGNATURE (per I-1292, not read off the header): no Algebra.IsSeparable, no Module.Finite, no IsGalois, no condition on Gal(k'/k). Arbitrary field k, arbitrary extension k'/k.\\n\\nWHY IT IS FREE RATHER THAN FORTUNATE, since this is what another lane should check first: the canonical action's gamma-component IS twistMor gamma, which is DEFINED by transporting the functor action galoisActionPicEt along rep. So equivariance of (rep.homEquiv.symm c).left is not an independent condition on c -- it is the image under rep.homEquiv of the same functor-level equation that invariance is. Three steps, each formal:\\n (1) isEquivariant_iff_galTwistMor -- equivariance of the underlying scheme map is that square read in the k'-slice. galTwistMor is the slice packaging of pullbackGalMap, and twistTest_eq_restrictTest_galTwistMor is the slice form of the rfl-identity I-1455 already records.\\n (2) homEquiv_twist_comp -- THE STEP: rep.homEquiv of the square's right side is (galoisActionPicEt gamma).inv at rep.homEquiv phi, by NATURALITY at phi.op. twistMor was built from that natural transformation, so naturality un-builds it.\\n (3) crossBaseIso_galoisActionPicEt_inv -- transport along picEt_crossBaseIso leaves picEt C applied to restrictTest_twistTestFunctor_iso, whose components are the IDENTITY on underlying schemes.\\nComposed: equivariance at gamma IS invariance at gamma^-1. Both predicates quantify over the whole group and gamma -> gamma^-1 is a bijection of it, so they coincide -- that Gal(k'/k) is a GROUP is all that is used about it.\\n\\nTHE ROUTE'S INPUT COUNT DROPPED FROM FOUR TO TWO, and the payoff forms are landed so no consumer mentions the match: seamClauseOne_of_isGaloisQuotient_noMatch takes rep, hq : IsGaloisQuotient (semilinearGalActionOfRepresentableBy C rep) Y.hom, hcov, hlft -- no hmatch and no externally supplied action. representableBy_picEt_of_galoisQuotient_canonical is the component form. So between rep and clause (1) field 1 there are now TWO named antecedents: pic-f's non-affine Galois quotient and pic-a's hcov. Both DM'd.\\n\\nWHAT I WITHDREW OF MY OWN r1 WORK, corrected in place in PicEtDescentGoal.lean rather than left to read as audited self-criticism: that docstring said this predicate is \\\"not proved here\\\", called it \\\"satisfiable but not measured non-vacuous\\\", and said exhibiting a model at a NONTRIVIAL automorphism was open and \\\"is what would make G1's cost a real number\\\". All false after this commit -- it is free at every extension at the CANONICAL action. BUT MY 'so isInvariantMatch_of_subsingleton is SUBSUMED' WAS ITSELF FALSE, refuted by a fresh-context audit and reproduced: offering isInvariantMatch_canonical against IsInvariantMatch C rep rho T for a bound rho is a TYPE MISMATCH. That lemma quantifies over an ARBITRARY rho; mine PINS rho to the canonical action, so the two are INCOMPARABLE -- mine more general in the extension, strictly less general in the action. It is also LOAD-BEARING: representableBy_picEt_of_degenerate takes an external rho and calls it, so do not delete it or reroute that call. The incomparability is intrinsic to discharging a hypothesis by CHOOSING the object it quantified over, and my r2 'correction' of an r1 caveat over-corrected into a stronger claim in the opposite direction.\\n\\nAND THE WITHDRAWAL IS SCOPED, which is the part a reader will get wrong: it does NOT extend to hcov. hcov's only exhibited witness site still trivialises the conclusion (etaleTopology_generate_coverSelfSection_of_mono at k' = k), so representableBy_picEt_of_degenerate remains the honest caution there and the non-vacuity question is now entirely pic-a's row. This closes no sorry and does not witness rep.\\n\\n--- earlier row text follows ---\\n\\nADVANCED 2026-07-30 by ajc-p1 (run 0083 r7), owner ajc-p1. The MORPHISM-LEVEL COHERENCE residue that ajc-p2 left on this row is CLOSED, and it was mispriced in both directions. Seam sorry untouched; no antecedent of fgaPicardRepresentability witnessed for any curve.\\n\\nLANDED, DO NOT REDO. Picard/GaloisDescent/PicEtGaloisBridge.lean, rooted at AlgebraicJacobian.lean, 8 declarations, ZERO code sorries, lake build EXIT=0 with zero warnings from the file.\\n * twistTest -- the gamma-twist of the base-changed test T_k', as an endomorphism IN THE SLICE OVER Spec k. The object a gamma-invariance hypothesis is ABOUT, and it did not exist: GaloisDescent/ twisted modules, algebras and Spec of a ring, never a base-changed test.\\n * coverSelfSection -- the gamma-component section T_k' -> T_k' x_T T_k', <id, twist gamma>, with the two projection identities as simp lemmas. THIS IS THE COHERENCE the previous residue named.\\n * invariant_of_projections_agree -- projection agreement IMPLIES gamma-invariance for every gamma, UNCONDITIONALLY: arbitrary field k, only [Algebra k k'], no Module.Finite, no IsSeparable, no IsGalois, arbitrary test.\\n * projections_agree_of_invariant -- the converse, as an implication with ONE antecedent explicit and UNDISCHARGED (hcov: the Gal-indexed sections generate a COVERING sieve).\\n * exists_unique_descend_picEt_of_invariant -- ajc-p2's exists-unique with its hypothesis replaced by gamma-invariance, which is what G1 actually holds.\\n\\nTHE REPRICING, and it is the finding. ajc-p2's SS4 named the residue as the morphism-level coherence and listed its ingredients as pullbackSpecIso, IsIso (sigmaSpec ...) and galoisSelfTensorEquiv. NONE OF THE THREE IS NEEDED. The coherence is pullback.lift_fst and pullback.