ute, whose uniform-H1 input comes from cluster P instead (AJC.rr, task ajc-rr). Serre finiteness remains of independent interest and may yet be the cheapest route to the H0-finite-generation leaf flagged in RigidPushforwardP1Engine.lean.\",\n      \"status\": \"rejected\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"low\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.picrep\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.picrep\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.picrep.tensor\",\n      \"title\": \"Pullback-tensor and fibre base change\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"AUDITED 2026-07-30 (review-ajc r4). This row bundles TWO deliverables; the first is LANDED and sorry-free, the second is genuinely OPEN. The row read as wholly unstarted since its creation on 2026-07-23 and was never re-measured, so a lane pricing it would have re-proved the landed half.\\n\\nCLAUSE 1 -- DONE, DO NOT RE-PROVE. 'The canonical pullback tensor comparison is an isomorphism' IS proved: Scheme.Modules.pullbackTensorIsoOfLocallyTrivial (Picard/TensorObjSubstrate/PullbackTensorIso.lean:153), for line bundles via the chart-chase plus isIso_of_isIso_restrict. Zero body sorries in that file (comments stripped). It has a one-sided companion pullbackTensorIsoOfRightLocallyTrivial and the IsIso form pullbackTensorMap_isIso_of_right_locallyTrivial (PullbackTensorOneSided.lean:275, :264). Already CONSUMED at 8+ sites in Picard/RelPicFunctor.lean (:366, :389, :433, :468, :609, :792, :819) and cited by QuotFunctorDef.lean:448 -- so this is settled substrate, not a frontier.\\n\\nCLAUSE 2 -- OPEN, and the file that would host it says so in the subjunctive. 'The quasi-coherent tensor-section input used by