eft pending deliberately: it is real but off the representability critical path, so it is not a round target.\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.picrep\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.picrep\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.rr\",\n      \"title\": \"Riemann--Roch, divisors, and the adelic genus\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Riemann--Roch, divisors, and the adelic genus. Cluster-P items 1 and 3 (bounded H1 vanishing, global generation) and exact Riemann--Roch are CLOSED at AJC's own curve under three curve binders (RiemannRoch/Ledger/FiberBound.lean). Item 2, extension-uniformity, is still OPEN but is now ONE input rather than two. r5 decomposed the open half into (a) base-field invariance of the genus and (b) a kappa-independent degree bound on a vanishing base divisor; r6 PROVED (a). Ledger/SectionsFieldBaseChange.lean supplies the comparison map r5 identified as the actual deliverable -- Gamma(C,V) tensor_k kappa = Gamma(C_kappa, fst^-1 V), kappa-linearly, for every qcqs open and every field extension -- and Ledger/GenusFieldInvariance.lean turns it into genus C_kappa = genus C for EVERY field extension, with no finiteness, separability, perfectness or algebraic-closedness hypothesis. Both files sorry-free, kernel-built, 20 declarations axiom-clean measured at SYNTHESIS sites with two live controls (one reaching a sorry through an import). Engine: termwise Cech base change plus right-exactness on the cokernel -- not semicontinuity, not Mumford II.5, and not Serre duality, which this workspace still does not have (r5's retraction of the 2g-1 shortcut stands). Provenance: argument adapted from AJCR's H1BaseFieldInvariance.lean, statements rederived at AJC carriers; not portable as-is because AJCR states it over AffineTwoCover (absent from AJC entirely) and because AJC lacked the right-exactness brick quotRangeBaseChangeEquiv. r5's carrier measurement is corrected: the object-level rfl between AJC and AJCR base-change carriers was true but was NOT the obstacle -- the cover-level assembly and the missing brick were. WHAT REMAINS: input (b) only, uniformVanishing_of_uniformBaseDivisor's single hypothesis, genuinely open in AJC and AJCR both (AJCR's analogue is a Nat.find per field). UniformVanishing C is NOT proved. Global generation is untouched and is still not uniform over extensions. Caveat: the Ledger vanishing chain including these two files sits outside the root import cone (262 modules reachable from the roll-up); rooting is one import line, outside this task's write scope.\\n\",\n      \"status\": \"active\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.jacobian\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.rr\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"37f95374c\",\n        \"1f2d5a1fe\",\n        \"7053bdd51\",\n        \"beb6c583a\",\n        \"e56633817\",\n        \"c5e72b89b\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 1,\n      \"subtree_done\": 6,\n      \"subtree_total\": 7\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.rr.adelic\",\n      \"title\": \"Adelic Riemann--Roch and cohomological finiteness\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Sorry-free. The adelic model of H^0 and H^1 for a smooth proper curve: a nonconstant map to P^1, its finiteness, the P^1 base case and chart data, the adelic cokernel, the Euler-characteristic ledger, and unconditional finiteness of the genus. Modules: RiemannRoch/CohomologyKit and the RiemannRoch/Adelic package (Substrate, NonconstantToP1, FiniteMapToP1, FinitenessP1, P1BaseCase, P1ChartData, Cokernel, ChiLedger, CechAcyclicInstance, CechComparisonGate, GateInstances, GenusFiniteness, GenusUnconditional).\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.rr\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.rr\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.rr.degvanish\",\n      \"title\": \"Single-field bounded vanishing on a degree half-space\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"DONE (run 0074 r3, ajc-rr). Ledger/DegreeVanishing.lean, 12 decls, 0 sorries, kernel-checked (lake build 8581 jobs exit 0), 16/16 axiom-clean including four synthesis-site probes at the challenge curve.\\n\\nThe order-cone peel of AJC.rr.sectiondrop reaches a DEGREE HALF-SPACE. subsingleton_hModule_one_of_deg_ge: from ONE base vanishing at ONE divisor D0, H1(O(D)) = 0 for every D with deg D >= deg D0 + 1 - chi(O_X). Also exact Riemann-Roch above that bound, the D0 = 0 form (unconditional given H1(O_C) = 0, hence unconditional at genus zero), and the contrapositive that non-vanishing H1 is a bounded-degree phenomenon.\\n\\nThe mathematical point, and it retracts this lane's own r2 claim: sectiondrop published exists_bound_of_cofinal_vanishing as an OPEN hypothesis, saying nothing in AJC or AJCR produces it. Both ingredients were in the same directory. H1 vanishing is a linear-equivalence invariant (Ledger/MulEquiv.mulEquivDivisorSheaf), so the whole class of D0 is available to the peel; and riemann_inequality (Ledger/ChiLedger) manufactures the translating unit once deg(D - D0) + chi >= 1. The peel never needed the GIVEN D0.\\n\\nRESIDUE: one base vanishing at a general curve, i.e. the AJCR FLVVanishing:302 port (measured: 59-module local closure; new layer FLVFiberToolkit/FLVLattice/FLVQcoh/FiberTwist/Degree plus AffineVanishingQcoh/QcohSections; Degree drags in Picard/ presentation modules the Ledger tree lacks).\\n\\nNOT this row, and still genuinely open: extension-uniformity (every statement is over the single field K; the bound depends on X, K, D0) and global generation (no evaluation map appears). Scratch-path: DegreeVanishing imports SectionDrop, which is out of the root cone (I-0600).\\n\\nRESIDUE CLOSED 2026-07-28 (run 0074 r4, same lane). The \\\"one base vanishing at a general curve\\\"\\nabove is no longer a residue. Ledger/FiberVanishing.lean ports AJCR's fibrewise large-twist\\nvanishing (bodies unchanged) and Ledger/FiberBound.lean composes it with the chi-ledger, giving\\n\\n  exists_bound_subsingleton_hModule_one_curve : three curve binders, NO vanishing hypothesis\\n  exists_bound_h0_eq_genus_curve             : h0(O(D)) = 1 - genus C + deg D above a threshold\\n\\nThe pi is CONSTRUCTED inside (MapToP1.exists_isFinite_isDominant_toP1) and both Module.Finite\\nbinders are SYNTHESISED by ChiCurve, so nothing is left for a caller to instantiate. The quantifier\\norder is what makes the bound uniform in D: the tower threshold is taken at the FIXED divisor 0,\\nfixing one D0 = n0*F before any D is seen, and the degree slack is then carried by the\\nlinear-equivalence translate this row already built.\\n\\n41/41 axiom-clean with a firing control. Eight new files, 2,556 lines, 0 sorries.\\n\\nSTILL OPEN, unchanged: extension-uniformity. Every constant here lives over the single field K.\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.rr\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.rr\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.rr.divisor\",\n      \"title\": \"Weil divisors and the degree map\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Sorry-free. The group of Weil divisors on a curve, the degree of a divisor, and the divisor functor with its base-change well-definedness. Modules: Picard/DivDegree, Picard/DivFunctorDef. The one open obligation on this substrate, deg(div f) = 0, is tracked separately under AJC.rr.principal.\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.rr\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.rr\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.rr.extuniform\",\n      \"title\": \"Extension-uniform H1 vanishing: one threshold serving every field extension\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"MAJOR PROGRESS 2026-07-31 (pic-b, run 0093 r4), with no new hypotheses.\\n\\nCLOSED: the stabilization-index obstruction. FiberLattice.fiberLattice_stable proves that one plateau propagates. Quantitative quotient stabilization therefore reaches the top by the initial quotient dimension, giving H1(O(D + h1(O(D))*F)) = 0. At D=0 this produces the explicit base divisor h1(O)*F, and on every base-changed challenge curve GenusFieldInvariance.subsingleton_genus_smul_fiber_perFieldFiniteMapToP1_curve exposes the witness exactly as genus(C)*F_pi_kappa.\\n\\nCLOSED: choosing one map before the extension. MapToP1FieldBaseChange.fixedFiniteMapToP1 chooses one finite dominant C -> P1(k), and fixedFiniteMapToP1BaseChange constructs its cartesian base change over every kappa. Finiteness and surjectivity, hence dominance, are proved after base change.\\n\\nOPEN, exact: transport the fixed map source-side two-chart coordinate datum along baseChangeFieldFst and prove invariance of the resulting fiber-divisor degree. The preferred route is local section equivalences plus two-term kernel base change; no full isomorphism between the pullback target and the separate Ledger P1(kappa) model is required. Once deg_kappa(D_kappa) = deg_k(D) for D = genus(C)*F, take d := deg_k(D) to produce UniformBaseDivisor C d and then uniform H1 vanishing.\\n\\nDO NOT CITE the previous n0(kappa) or strictness gap: both are now closed. Remaining variable: deg_kappa(F) only.\\n\\nVerification: lake builds through GenusFieldInvariance (8702 jobs); all new declarations have only propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound and no sorryAx.\",\n      \"status\": \"active\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.rr\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"pic-b\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.rr\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"534f86710bb4ba06e57dc079c7626b23aabe72a8\",\n        \"8dfdafa7c292b782195728891bd833213957c3dd\",\n        \"a4532f2ef08d8e11bc2ce123d2fb8a30bac9f77b\",\n        \"8c58b2a727b7926edb90c593a39cfe673a406241\",\n        \"e95986f87d46ea019cbed13b5df215bc71eeec23\",\n        \"8decce128\",\n        \"fd811e5fd\",\n        \"6618d6979\",\n        \"71f1cf403\",\n        \"81e3ef56f\",\n        \"f7d1ec0d0\",\n        \"57f19428d\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.rr.ledger\",\n      \"title\": \"The AJCR chi-ledger, ported into AJC and unconditional at a curve\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"RiemannRoch/Ledger/, 41 files, 9877 lines, sorry-free (re-measured at HEAD by the janitor\\npass of run 0074; the earlier \\\"38 files, ~9.4k\\\" was a mid-session count). PORT of the AJCR\\nchi-ledger cone (proof bodies byte-identical bar named adaptations) plus four AJC-native\\nrederivations.\\n\\nLANDED: chi(O(D)) = 1 - genus C + deg D on AJC's OWN frozen genus, binders\\n[IsProper][SmoothOfRelativeDimension 1][GeometricallyIrreducible] only -- both Module.Finite\\ncohomology binders are SYNTHESISED, not assumed, measured at a synthesis site rather than at\\nthe declaration. Plus riemann_inequality, h0 unbounded along n*x, deg_divOf.\\n\\nAJC-NATIVE (not ports, no producer existed in either project): ledgerGenus_eq_genus (the\\nuniverse gap is an annotation, discharged via chgUnivLinearEquiv); residueDeg = 1 over kbar,\\nwhich collapses the residue weighting to the bare coefficient sum; divOf agrees with\\nWeilDivisor.principal coefficient-wise INCLUDING SIGNS.\\n\\nNOT DONE: the port is rootable (co-importability verified after fixing three name collisions,\\nI-0576) but is imported by NOTHING -- AlgebraicJacobian.lean carries no RiemannRoch.Ledger\\nimport and nothing outside Ledger/ references it, re-confirmed at HEAD. So the root target\\nelaborates none of the cone and the standing axiom probe never sees it. The root roll-up is\\noutside this lane's write scope; tracked as issue I-0600. Extension-uniformity and global\\ngeneration remain untouched; single-field bounded vanishing is not supplied by this ledger.\\n\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.rr\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.rr\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"d7bdd5456\",\n        \"64468898f\",\n        \"3029d0dab\",\n        \"61fe05276\",\n        \"4e8665b58\",\n        \"3809f4e9a\",\n        \"fe4ab9411\",\n        \"3e4a22ed4\",\n        \"3db10ba19\",\n        \"8dc29faff\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.rr.principal\",\n      \"title\": \"Principal divisors have degree zero\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Principal divisors have degree zero. CLOSED 2026-07-28 (run 0067, ajc-pic0av, commit 8b654f78d).\\nRiemannRoch/WeilDivisor.lean has ZERO sorries. principal_degree_zero is proved at its own binders\\n(smooth proper geometrically irreducible curve over kbar, regular in codim 1), axiom-clean\\n([propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], no sorryAx), 8607 jobs, zero warnings.\\n\\nTHE IMPORT INVERSION WAS NEVER REAL, and that is the whole story of why this took four sessions.\\nThree predecessor summaries -- including two of mine -- recorded the leaf as blocked because\\nLedger/PrincipalTransport.degree_principal_eq_zero_curve, the theorem with the leaf's conclusion,\\nhas a 51-file cone containing WeilDivisor.lean. That measurement is correct and irrelevant: it is\\nthe cone of the CONSUMER, and PrincipalTransport is downstream only because it also imports the\\nindex bridge for convenience. The INPUTS were always importable:\\n  Ledger/OrdCompare             7 files, WeilDivisor-free\\n  Ledger/ResidueOneAlgClosed   37 files, WeilDivisor-free\\n  Adelic/FiniteMapToP1          4 files, WeilDivisor-free\\nUnion 42, containing neither WeilDivisor nor CurveCoheight nor CurveDivisorIndexBridge; cycle\\ndetection over all modules with the three new edges returns zero.\\n\\nAdelic.coheight_le_one_of_curve is the one nobody had checked. It was called 'strictly downstream'\\nin three roadmap summaries, in CurveCoheight.lean's own docstring and in the leaf's comment block,\\nand its cone is FOUR files -- it is downstream of Genus, which WeilDivisor.lean already imported.\\nSo the coheight bound, which CurveCoheight.lean carries as an explicit hypothesis precisely\\nbecause it was thought unavailable upstream, is simply discharged at the leaf.\\n\\nTHE PROOF, and it needs NO case split. Hartshorne II.6.10's route (finite phi : C -> P^1 from a\\nnon-constant f, then degree multiplicativity under finite pullback) is NOT taken and its two\\ngeometric sub-lemmas are no longer owed by this project. Instead the ported chi-ledger\\nchi(O(D)) = chi(O_C) + deg D gives deg(div g) = 0 by transporting chi along O(0) = O(-div g)\\n(Ledger/ChiLedger.deg_divOf, a devissage induction over closed points with skyscraper quotients).\\nThree carrier comparisons connect it to this project's degree, each DISCHARGED not assumed:\\n * ORDERS: ordZ read additively = the Ring.ordFrac-based RationalMap.order, no sign correction\\n   (Ledger/OrdCompare.ordZ_toAdd_eq_log_ordFrac);\\n * INDEX SETS: PrimeDivisor = {x != eta}, reproved inline in two lines (le_antisymm of the\\n   coheight bound against one_le_coheight_of_ne_genericPoint) since CurveCoheight imports the leaf;\\n * WEIGHTS: over kbar the residue weighting collapses to the bare coefficient sum\\n   (Ledger/ResidueOneAlgClosed). This is where [IsAlgClosed] is load-bearing and it is NOT\\n   bookkeeping -- over a general field the weighted and unweighted degrees are different numbers.\\nSince the chain is uniform in f, the former constant/non-constant split is deleted: a constant f\\nhas every coefficient zero and the same chain returns 0.\\n\\nSCOPE, stated plainly: the theorem carries [IsAlgClosed kbar], as it always did. The\\ngeneral-field statement is NOT proved and is not what this node asked for. An earlier version of\\nthis summary said the leaf had no IsAlgClosed binder; that was wrong, and ajc-rr repeated it from\\nhere -- the theorem has bound it since it was written.\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.rr\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.rr\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [\n        \"8b654f78d\",\n        \"768b6cbd4\"\n      ],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.rr.sectiondrop\",\n      \"title\": \"Section drop and the H1 peel on the ledger carrier\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Ledger/SectionDrop.lean, new, ~490 lines, 19 declarations, 0 sorries, LSP clean, KERNEL-CHECKED (olean built after last edit).\\n\\nTHE RESULT: on the ported chi-ledger carrier, H1-vanishing propagation is a theorem rather than a hypothesis. The devissage quotient 0 -> O(D-x) -> O(D) -> sky -> 0 has a SKYSCRAPER third term, so H1(sky) = 0, so ChiSlice.surjective_map_f applies at n = 1 and H1(O(D-x)) -> H1(O(D)) is onto.\\n\\nGENUINELY NEW HERE (checked against AJCR after a false first claim, see below):\\n * subsingleton_hModule_one_of_le -- the D0 <= D ORDER form of the peel;\\n * the two-sided section drop h0(O(D-x)) <= h0(O(D)) <= h0(O(D-x)) + [kappa(x):K];\\n * the drop IDENTITY: h0 gain plus h1 loss equals the residue degree exactly;\\n * exact Riemann-Roch on the order-cone above a vanishing D0, and the exact drop there;\\n * exists_bound_of_cofinal_vanishing -- degree-threshold vanishing reduced to one named COFINALITY hypothesis.\\n\\nTHE PEEL CHAIN NEEDS NO FINITENESS: 11 of 19 declarations omit both Module.Finite cohomology binders (the linter found this, not me). Hence vanishing is stated as Subsingleton (H1 ...), never h1 = 0 -- the latter is vacuously true for infinite-dimensional H1 since Module.finrank reads 0 there. Filed as memory I-0620.\\n\\nTWO RETRACTIONS OF THIS LANE'S OWN CLAIMS, found by fresh-context ground review (I-0623), verified in AJCR source and fixed at b7383a4d5:\\n\\n 1. The PEEL CHAIN IS A RE-DERIVATION, not new. AJCR RiemannRoch/FLVClass.lean already has peel_single (:260), peel_nsmul_single (:277), peel_effective (:292) -- the same three steps, the same Subsingleton spelling, the same variable block, the same surjective_map_f. Cause: this lane searched SectionBound.lean (where the finrank INEQUALITY lives), found it, and never opened FLVClass.lean (where the PROPAGATION lives). Also h0_divisorSheaf_of_subsingleton_of_le duplicates AJCR h0_eq_deg_add_chi_of_subsingleton_hModule_one at a fixed divisor.\\n\\n 2. THE BASE VANISHING IS NOT OPEN. This lane reported it open \\\"at every curve, P^1 included\\\"; that was measured inside AJC's Ledger tree only and is false about the workspace. AJCR RiemannRoch/FLVVanishing.lean:302, subsingleton_hModule_divisorSheaf_one_of_isFinite_toP1, proves it ON THIS CARRIER: for finite dominant pi : Y -> P^1 compatible with the structure maps and any D, there is n0 with H1(O(D + n*F)) = 0 for all n >= n0, F the fibre divisor.\\n\\nSO THE NEXT STEP IS A PORT, NOT A PROOF: AJC has no fibre-divisor / finite-map-to-P1 layer on the Ledger carrier. Porting it discharges the base, and exists_bound_of_cofinal_vanishing is already the right shape to consume it, since a tower D + n*F is exactly a cofinal family.\\n\\nSTILL OPEN: extension-uniformity (nothing here quantifies over a second field; AJCR lacks it too). Global generation is untouched on this carrier -- the adelic lane owns that bridge on its own degK carrier, gated on hledger.\\n\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.rr\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.rr\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.substrate\",\n      \"title\": \"Foundational substrate (rigidity, genus, and line bundles)\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Complete and sorry-free: RigidityLemma, Genus, AbelJacobi, line-bundle coherence and pullback, RelPicFunctor, and RelativeSpec. The earlier experimental cotangent modules were deliberately removed and are not part of the current AJC route.\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.jacobian\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.substrate\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"tree_depth\": 1,\n      \"subtree_done\": 7,\n      \"subtree_total\": 7\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AJC.substrate.descent\",\n      \"title\": \"Gluing and descent\",\n      \"projects\": [\n        \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Sorry-free. Gluing schemes and quasi-coherent data along an open cover, Zariski-local representability descent, and semilinear (Galois) descent for modules and algebras. Modules: Picard/GlueDescent, Picard/ZariskiDescentRepresentability, Picard/GaloisDescent/SemilinearModules, Picard/GaloisDescent/SemilinearAlgebras.\",\n      \"status\": \"done\",\n      \"kind\": \"proof\",\n      \"priority\": \"normal\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"inbox_refs\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"projects\": [\n          \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"parent\": \"AJC.substrate\",\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"owner\": \"\",\n      \"milestone\": \"AJC.substrate\",\n      \"pinned_commits\": [],\n      \"t